hadiths[900]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3548","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: I saw Ibn Masud stone the jamrah, the jamrah of al-Aqabah, from the belly of the valley, then he said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one to whom the surah of al-Baqarah was revealed."
"3549","Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Kathir ibn Mudrik al-Ashjai, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah uttered the talbiyah when he poured forth from Jam, and it was said: This is a Bedouin. Abdullah said: Have the people forgotten or strayed? I heard the one to whom the surah of al-Baqarah was revealed say in this place: Here I am, O Allah, here I am."
"3550","Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abi Hayyan al-Ashjai, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: He said to me: Recite some of the Quran to me. He said: I said to him: Did I not learn it from you, and do you teach us? He said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day and he said: Recite some of the Quran to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, was it not revealed to you, and did we not learn it from you? He said: Yes, but I love to hear it from someone else."
"3551","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Abi Razin, from Ibn Masud, he said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the surah of al-Nisa, and when I reached this verse: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you against these as a witness, he said: His eyes overflowed, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3552","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar and Mughirah informed us, from Abi Wail, he said: Ibn Masud said: Two traits, meaning one of them I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the other from myself: Whoever dies setting up a rival to Allah enters the Fire, and I say: Whoever dies setting up no rival to Allah and associating nothing with Him enters Paradise."
"3553","Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, he said: I heard Aba Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrate, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The drop remains in the womb forty days in its state without changing, and when the forty have passed it becomes a clot, then a lump likewise, then bones likewise, and when Allah wills to fashion its creation He sends an angel to it, and the angel in charge of it says: O my Lord, male or female, wretched or happy, short or tall, deficient or excess, his provision and his term, sound or sick? He said: So he writes all of that. A man among the people said: Then what is the point of deeds when all of this has already been settled? He said: Act, for each will be directed to that for which he was created."
"3554","Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, a freed slave of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abi Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty except that they will be for them a fortified fortress from the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what if they were two? He said: Even if they were two. Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sent forth only two. He said: Even if they were two. He said: Ubayy ibn Kab, Abu al-Mundhir, the chief of the reciters, said: I have sent forth only one. He said: It was said to him: Even if it were one? He said: That is only at the first shock."
"3555","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Abi Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the polytheists distracted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of al-Khandaq from four prayers until as much of the night as Allah willed had passed. He said: So he commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan, then he called the iqamah and he prayed al-Zuhr, then he called the iqamah and he prayed al-Asr, then he called the iqamah and he prayed al-Maghrib, then he called the iqamah and he prayed al-Isha."
"3556","Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Muthir ibn Afazah, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: On the night I was taken by night I met Ibrahim and Musa and Isa. He said: They discussed the matter of the Hour, and they referred their matter to Ibrahim, and he said: I have no knowledge of it. They referred the matter to Musa, and he said: I have no knowledge of it. They referred the matter to Isa, and he said: As for its appointed time, none knows it but Allah, that, and among what my Lord, mighty and majestic, entrusted to me is that the Dajjal will come forth. He said: With me will be two staffs, and when he sees me he will melt as lead melts. He said: Allah will destroy him, so that even stone and tree will say: O Muslim, beneath me is a disbeliever, come and kill him. He said: Allah will destroy them, then people will return to their lands and homes. He said: At that time Yajuj and Majuj will come forth, coming down from every mound, treading their lands, coming upon nothing but destroying it, passing no water but drinking it. Then people will return to me and complain of them to me, so I will supplicate to Allah against them, and Allah will destroy them and kill them until the earth reeks from the stench of their odor. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, will send down rain, and it will wash their bodies until it casts them into the sea. My father said: Something here escaped me which I did not understand, like a hide. Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, said: Then the mountains will be scattered and the earth stretched like the stretching of a hide. Then he returned to the hadith of Hushaym. He said: Among what my Lord, mighty and majestic, entrusted to me is that when that is so, the Hour will be like the pregnant woman at full term whose family does not know when she will surprise them with her delivery, by night or by day."
"3557","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: So-and-so slept last night past the prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is Satan urinating in his ear, or in his ears."
"3558","Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: I was with Masruq in a house in which there was an image of Maryam, and Masruq said: This is an image of Kisra. I said: No, but it is an image of Maryam. Masruq said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"3559","Ishaq, he is al-Azraq, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sees me in sleep has seen me, for Satan ought not to take my likeness."
"3560","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him."
"3561","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khusayf, Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us the fear prayer. They stood in two rows, a row stood behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a row facing the enemy. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed one rakah with the row next to him, then they stood and went and stood in the station of those facing the enemy, and those came and stood in their station, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed one rakah with them, then he gave salams. Then they stood and prayed one rakah for themselves, then they gave salams. Then they went and stood in the station of those facing the enemy, and those returned to their station, and they prayed one rakah for themselves, then they gave salams."
"3562","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Khusayf al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught him the tashahhud and commanded him to teach the people: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"3563","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in prayer and he would return it to us. When we returned from the Negus we greeted him and he did not return it to us, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you in prayer and you would return it to us. He said: Indeed in prayer there is occupation."
"3564","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The superiority of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-odd degrees."
"3565","Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Said ibn Amr, from Abi Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: When is Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Who among you remembers the night of the bright moonlit ones? Abdullah said: I, may my father and mother be ransom for you, with some dates in my hand warming myself with them, sheltering behind the rear of my saddle from the dawn, and that was when the moon rose."
"3566","Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed al-Zuhr as five, and it was said: Has the prayer been increased? It was said: You prayed five, so he prostrated two prostrations."
"3567","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The prayer of the congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five multiples, each like his prayer."
"3568","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam informed me, from Abdullah ibn Maqil ibn Muqarrin, he said: I entered with my father to Abdullah ibn Masud, and he said: Did you hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes. And he said once: I heard him say: Remorse is repentance."
"3569","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Dharr, from Wail ibn Mahanah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give charity, O company of women, even from your jewelry, for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman who was not of the high women stood and said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because you curse much and deny the husband."
"3570","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated them after the salams. And he said once: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salams."
"3571","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zir, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Hour will not rise until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name. My father said: He narrated it to us in his house, in his chamber, I think some son of Jafar ibn Yahya, or Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Yahya, asked him."
"3572","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The days will not end nor will time pass until a man from my household rules the Arabs whose name matches my name."
"3573","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Asim narrated to me, from Zir, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The world will not go, or he said: The world will not end, until a man from my household rules the Arabs and his name matches my name."
"3574","Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a cave, and By those sent forth in succession was revealed to him, so I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was moist with it, and I do not know with which of them he ended: In what narration after it will they believe, or: When it is said to them bow, they do not bow. A snake got ahead of us and entered a hole, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You were protected from its evil and it was protected from your evil."
"3575","Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when we were in Makkah before coming to the land of Abyssinia. When we arrived from the land of Abyssinia we came to him and greeted him and he did not return it, so I was seized by what was near and what was far until they finished the prayer. I asked him, and he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, brings about in His affair what He wills, and He has brought about in His affair that we not speak in prayer."
"3576","Sufyan narrated to us, from Jami, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever swears an oath by which he cuts off the property of a Muslim meets Allah while He is angry with him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited to us its confirmation from the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, those shall have no share in the Hereafter, nor will Allah speak to them."
"3577","Sufyan narrated to us, from Jami, from Abi Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: No servant withholds the zakah of his wealth but there will be made for him a bald serpent following him, fleeing from it while it follows him, saying: I am your treasure. Then Abdullah recited its confirmation in the Book of Allah: They will be collared with what they withheld on the Day of Resurrection. Sufyan said once: He collars it on his neck."
"3578","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata, from Abi Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Habib, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud attribute it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah has not sent down a disease but He has sent down for it a cure, whoever knows it knows it and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"3579","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shimr, from Mughirah ibn Sad ibn al-Akhram, from his father, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not take landed estates lest you desire the world."
"3580","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I disavow before every intimate friend his intimacy, and had I taken an intimate friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, and your companion is the intimate friend of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3581","Sufyan narrated to us, Sulayman said: I heard Shaqiq say: We were waiting for Abdullah ibn Masud in the mosque for him to come out to us, then Yazid ibn Muawiyah, meaning al-Nakhai, came to us. He said: Shall I not go and look, and if he is in the house perhaps I can bring him out to you? Then he came to us and stood over us and said: Your place is mentioned to me, but I do not come to you for fear of boring you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to time us with admonition in the days for fear of boredom for us."
"3582","Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid, from Abi al-Kanud: I found a ring one day and he mentioned it, and Ibn Masud saw it on his hand and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the gold ring."
"3583","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abi Mamar, from Ibn Masud: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, into two halves until they looked at it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bear witness."
"3584","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abi Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Masud: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered while around the Kabah were three hundred and sixty idols, so he began to stab them with a stick in his hand, saying: The truth has come and falsehood neither begins nor returns, the truth has come and falsehood has vanished, indeed falsehood is ever vanishing."
"3585","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: It is not of them that one precedes it, and it was read to Sufyan: I heard Yahya al-Jabir, from Abi Majid al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Abdullah say: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about walking with the funeral, and he said: Followed, not following."
"3586","Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina. He said: A snake came out against us, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill it. We rushed toward it but it got ahead of us."
"3587","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash report from Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah would come out to us and say: I am told of your place, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except fear of boring you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to time us with admonition in the days for fear of boredom for us."
"3588","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms upon his thighs and hunch, then he joined his palms together, as though I am looking at the interlacing of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: then he joined his palms and showed them."
"3589","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When this verse was revealed: Those who believe and do not clothe their faith with wrong, it weighed heavily upon the people, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us does not wrong himself? He said: It is not what you mean. Have you not heard what the righteous servant said: O my son, do not associate with Allah, indeed association is a great wrong. It is only association."
"3590","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: A man from the People of the Book came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Aba al-Qasim, has it reached you that Allah, mighty and majestic, carries mankind upon a finger, the heavens upon a finger, the earths upon a finger, the trees upon a finger, and the soil upon a finger? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his molars appeared, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And they have not esteemed Allah His true esteem, the verse."
"3591","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he recited the surah of Yusuf at Hims, and a man said: It was not thus revealed. Abdullah drew near him and found the smell of wine from him, and said: Do you deny the truth and drink filth? I will not leave you until I flog you the prescribed punishment. He said: So he struck him the punishment, and said: By Allah, thus did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite it to me."
"3592","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I was walking with Abdullah at Mina when Uthman met him and stood with him talking to him, and Uthman said to him: O Aba Abd al-Rahman, shall we not marry you to a young maid so that perhaps she will remind you of what has passed of your time? Abdullah said: If you say that, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: O company of young men, whoever among you can afford maintenance, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private part, and whoever cannot, fasting is for him, for it is a restraint for him."
"3593","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Uthman prayed at Mina as four, so Abdullah ibn Masud said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina as two rakahs, with Abu Bakr as two rakahs, and with Umar as two rakahs."
"3594","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then after that will come a people whose testimonies precede their oaths and whose oaths precede their testimonies."
"3595","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know the last of the people of the Fire to come out of the Fire, a man coming out of it crawling, and it will be said to him: Go and enter Paradise. He said: He will go to enter and will find the people have taken the dwellings. He said: He will return and say: O my Lord, the people have taken the dwellings. He said: It will be said to him: Do you remember the time in which you were? He said: He will say: Yes. It will be said to him: Wish. So he will wish, and it will be said: For you is what you wished and ten times the world. He said: He will say: Do You mock me while You are the King? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laugh until his molars appeared."
"3596","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I do well in Islam, will I be taken for what I did in the pre-Islamic period? He said: If you do well in Islam you will not be taken for what you did in the pre-Islamic period, and if you do badly in Islam you will be taken for the first and the last."
"3597","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath in which he is sinful in order to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man meets Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. Al-Ashath said: By Allah, that was about me. There was land between me and a Jewish man and he denied me it, so I brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do you have proof? I said: No. He said to the Jew: Swear. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear and my property will go. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"3598","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Asim narrated to me, from Zir, from Ibn Masud, he said: I was herding sheep for Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr passed by me and said: O boy, is there any milk? He said: I said: Yes, but I am entrusted. He said: Is there a sheep upon which the male has not mounted? So I brought him a sheep, and he wiped its udder and milk descended, and he milked it into a vessel and drank and gave Abu Bakr to drink, then he said to the udder: Contract, and it contracted. He said: Then I came to him after this and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from this speech. He said: He wiped my head and said: May Allah have mercy on you, for you are a taught boy."
"3599","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, with its chain, he said: Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed rock, so he milked into it and drank, and Abu Bakr drank, and I drank. He said: Then I came to him after that and said: Teach me from this Quran. He said: You are a taught boy. He said: So I took from his mouth seventy surahs."
"3600","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Allah looked into the hearts of the servants and found the heart of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the best of the hearts of the servants, so He chose him for Himself and sent him with His message. Then He looked into the hearts of the servants after the heart of Muhammad and found the hearts of his companions the best of the hearts of the servants, so He made them the ministers of His Prophet, fighting for His religion. Whatever the Muslims see as good is good with Allah, and whatever they see as bad is bad with Allah."
"3601","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perhaps you will encounter peoples who pray prayer outside its time, so when you encounter them, pray in your houses at the time you know, then pray with them and make it supererogatory."
"3602","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer, and I do not know whether he added or decreased, and when he gave salam it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in prayer? He said: No, and what is that? They said: You prayed such-and-such. He then folded his legs and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and when he gave salam he said: I am only a human, I forget as you forget, and when one of you doubts in prayer let him seek what is correct, and when he gives salam let him prostrate two prostrations."
"3603","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from a man of his people, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no evening talk after prayer, meaning the last Isha, except for one of two men: one praying or a traveler."
"3604","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: People said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for our deeds in Jahiliyyah? He said: Whoever of you does good in Islam will not be held accountable for it, and whoever does evil will be seized for his first and last deed."
"3605","Jarir narrated to us, from al-Rukayn, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to dislike ten traits: wearing a gold ring, dragging the izar, yellow dye meaning khaluq, changing white hair, Jarir said meaning only plucking it, and withdrawing water from its place, and ruqyah except with the Muawwidhat, and harming the child without making him unlawful, and tying amulets, and displaying adornment for other than its lawful place, and playing with dice."
"3606","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah who said, Sulayman said, and part of the hadith is from Amr ibn Murrah who said: My father narrated to me, from Abu al-Duha, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Recite to me. I said: Shall I recite to you when it was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from another. So I recited until when I reached: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you over these as a witness. He said: I saw his eyes shedding tears."
"3607","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah who said: A man from Banu Bajilah called Nahik ibn Sinan came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how do you read this verse, with hamzah do you find it, or alif, from water not stagnant, or not altered? Abdullah said to him: Have you enumerated all the Quran except this verse? He said: I recite the Mufassal in one rakah. Abdullah said: Hastily like the hasty recitation of poetry. Among the best of prayer is bowing and prostration, and peoples will recite the Quran not passing their collarbones, but when one recites it and it becomes firm in the heart it benefits. I know the pairs which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite, two surahs in one rakah. He said: Then he stood and entered, and Alqamah came and entered upon him. He said: So we said to him: Ask him for us about the pairs which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite, two surahs in one rakah. He said: So he entered and asked him, then he came out to us and said: Twenty surahs from the beginning of the Mufassal in the arrangement of Abdullah."
"3608","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, distributed a distribution one day. He said: A man from the Ansar said: This is a division by which the Face of Allah, Exalted and Majestic, was not intended. He said: So I said: O enemy of Allah, I shall surely inform the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of what you said. He said: So he mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his face reddened. He said: Then he said: Mercy of Allah upon Musa, he was harmed with more than this and was patient."
"3609","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman should not touch another woman so as to describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her."
"3610","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: We were walking with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he passed by Ibn Sayyad and said: I have hidden for you something hidden. Ibn Sayyad said: Dukh. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be gone, you will not exceed your stature. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike his neck. He said: No, if he is the one we fear, you will not be able to kill him."
"3611","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: As if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating a prophet struck by his people, wiping blood from his face and saying: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"3612","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which sin is greatest? He said: That you set a rival to Allah though He created you. He said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child lest he eat with you. He said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor. He said: Abdullah said: So Allah revealed confirming that: And those who do not invoke with Allah another god, nor kill the soul which Allah forbade except with truth, nor commit zina, and whoever does that meets punishment."
"3613","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: I left in the mosque a man interpreting the Quran by his opinion, saying about this verse: The day the sky brings clear smoke, to its end, a smoke will cover them on the Day of Resurrection seizing their breaths until there befalls them from it like the form of a cold. He said: Abdullah said: Whoever knows knowledge let him speak by it, and whoever does not know let him say: Allah knows best, for among the understanding of a man is to say about what he does not know: Allah knows best. This was only because when Quraysh resisted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he supplicated against them with years like the years of Yusuf, so drought and hardship struck them until they ate bones, and a man would look to the sky and see between him and the sky like the form of smoke from hardship. So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: So await the day the sky brings clear smoke covering the people, this is a painful punishment. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was approached and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for rain for Mudar, for they have perished. He said: So he supplicated for them, and Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: We shall remove the punishment. When the second time befell them they returned, so there was revealed: The day We seize with the great seizure, We shall take retribution, on the day of Badr."
"3614","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: I was screened by the curtain of the Kaaba, and three men came, a Qurashi and his two in-laws Thaqafis, or a Thaqafi and his two in-laws Qurashis, abundant in the fat of their bellies, little in the understanding of their hearts, and they spoke words I did not hear. One of them said: Do you think Allah hears this speech of ours? Another said: I think if we raise our voices He hears it, and if we do not raise them He does not hear. The other said: If He hears anything of it He hears all of it. He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: You did not hide that your hearing nor your sights nor your skins would testify against you, up to His saying: That thought of yours which you thought of your Lord ruined you, so you became among the losers."
"3615","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from the nephew of Zaynab, from Zaynab the wife of Abdullah who said: When Abdullah came from some need and reached the door he cleared his throat and spat, disliking to surprise us upon something he dislikes. She said: He came one day and cleared his throat. She said: With me was an old woman performing ruqyah for me for redness, so I put her under the bed. He entered and sat beside me and saw a thread on my neck. He said: What is this thread? She said: I said: A thread for which ruqyah was done for me. She said: So he took it and cut it, then said: The family of Abdullah are rich beyond shirk. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Ruqyah, amulets, and tiwalah are shirk. She said: So I said to him: Why do you say this, when my eye used to discharge and I used to go to so-and-so the Jew who performed ruqyah for it, and when he performed ruqyah it calmed? He said: That was only the work of Satan, he would poke it with his hand, and when you performed ruqyah he stopped from it. It would have sufficed you to say as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Remove the harm, Lord of people, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing leaving no sickness."
"3616","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one is more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Majestic, therefore He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden, and no one is dearer to him in praise than Allah, Exalted and Majestic."
"3617","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: To swear by Allah nine times that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was killed is dearer to me than to swear once, and that is because Allah, Exalted and Majestic, took him as a prophet and made him a martyr."
"3618","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah who said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was feverish, and I touched him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you suffer severe fever. He said: Yes, I suffer as two men of you suffer. I said: You have two rewards? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no Muslim on earth afflicted by harm from sickness or other than it but Allah removes his sins by it as the tree sheds its leaves."
"3619","Yala narrated it to us, al-Amash narrated like it."
"3620","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: Keep to these Mus-hafs, and perhaps he said the Quran, for it escapes from the chests of men more than camels from their hobbles. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should say: I forgot verse such-and-such, but he was made to forget."
"3621","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except by one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who leaves his religion separating from the community."
"3622","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: When we sat with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in prayer we would say: Peace upon Allah before His servants, peace upon Jibril, peace upon Mikail, peace upon so-and-so, peace upon so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard us and said: Allah is Peace, so when one of you sits in prayer let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good things. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. When he says it, it reaches every righteous servant in heaven and earth. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then afterwards let him choose of supplication what he wills."
"3623","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muslim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah, Exalted and Majestic, tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where they are called, for they are among the ways of guidance, and Allah, Exalted and Majestic, legislated for your Prophet the ways of guidance. There is none of you but has a mosque in his house, and if you prayed in your houses as this absentee prays in his house you would leave the way of your Prophet, and if you left the way of your Prophet you would go astray. I have seen myself when none absented from it except a hypocrite known for hypocrisy, and I have seen a man supported between two men until stood in the row. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no man who performs ablution well then comes to a mosque among the mosques and takes a step but a degree is raised by it, or a sin removed by it, or a good deed written for it, until we used to shorten our steps. And the excellence of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-five degrees."
"3624","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us, and he is the truthful believed one: One of you is gathered in creation in his mother's belly in forty days, then he is a clot like that, then he is a lump like that, then the angel is sent to him and breathes the spirit into him and is commanded with four words: his provision, his term, his deed, and whether wretched or happy. By the One besides Whom there is no god, one of you acts by the deeds of Paradise until there is between him and it but a cubit, then the Book overtakes him and he is sealed with the deeds of Hell and enters it. And a man acts by the deeds of Hell until there is between him and it but a cubit, then the Book overtakes him and he is sealed with the deeds of Paradise and enters it."
"3625","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one saying and I said another. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise. He said: And I said: Whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters Hell."
"3626","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Which of you is the wealth of his heir dearer to him than his wealth? He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none of us but his wealth is dearer to him than the wealth of his heir. He said: Know that there is none of you but the wealth of his heir is dearer to him than his wealth. You have of your wealth only what you sent forth, and the wealth of your heir is what you left behind. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whom do you count among you as the strong wrestler? He said: We said: The one whom men do not overthrow. He said: No, but the strong wrestler is the one who controls himself in anger. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whom do you count among you as raqub? He said: We said: The one who has no child. He said: No, but the raqub is the one who did not send forth any of his child."
"3627","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, Abdullah narrated to us two hadiths, one from himself and the other from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Abdullah said: The believer sees his sins as if at the base of a mountain fearing it will fall upon him, and the wicked sees his sins like a fly landing on his nose, so he said to it like this and it flew. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of one of you than a man who went out in a barren destructive land with his mount bearing his food, drink, provision, and what repairs him, then lost it and went seeking it until when death overtook him and he did not find it, he said: I shall return to the place where I lost it and die there. He said: So he came to his place and sleep overcame him, then awoke to find his mount at his head bearing his food, drink, provision, and what repairs him."
"3628","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, like it."
"3629","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, and al-Amash from Umarah, from al-Aswad, both said: Abdullah said: The believer sees his sins as if at the base of a mountain fearing it will fall upon him, and the wicked sees his sins like a fly landing on his nose, so he said with it like this and it flew. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of one of you than a man who went out in a barren land. Then Abu Muawiyah said: Both said: Abdullah narrated to us two hadiths, one from himself and the other from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a destructive land with his mount bearing his provision, food, drink, and what repairs him, then lost it and went seeking it until when death overtook him he said: I shall return to the place where I lost it and die there. He said: So he returned and sleep overcame him, then awoke to find his mount at his head bearing his provision, food, drink, and what repairs him."
"3630","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No soul is killed unjustly but upon the first son of Adam is a share of its blood, because he was the first to institute killing."
"3631","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, and Yahya from al-Amash, Umarah narrated to me, al-Aswad narrated to me, with the meaning, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah: None of you should give Satan a part of himself, seeing only that it is a duty upon him not to leave except from his right. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when most of his leaving was to his left."
"3632","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: When the day of Badr came he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do you say about these captives? He said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, your people and family, spare them and deal gently with them, perhaps Allah will turn to them. He said: And Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, they expelled you and denied you, bring them near and strike their necks. He said: And Abdullah ibn Rawahah said: O Messenger of Allah, look at a valley abundant in firewood, put them in it then set fire upon them. He said: Al-Abbas said: You severed your kinship. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and did not answer them anything. He said: People said: He will take the view of Abu Bakr, and people said: He will take the view of Umar, and people said: He will take the view of Abdullah ibn Rawahah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them and said: Allah softens the hearts of men in Him until they are softer than milk, and Allah hardens the hearts of men in Him until they are harder than stones. Your likeness, O Abu Bakr, is like Ibrahim, peace be upon him, who said: Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, You are Forgiving Merciful. And your likeness, O Abu Bakr, is like Isa who said: If You punish them they are Your servants, and if You forgive them You are the Mighty Wise. And your likeness, O Umar, is like Nuh who said: My Lord, leave not on earth any dweller among the disbelievers. And your likeness, O Umar, is like Musa who said: My Lord, harden their hearts so they do not believe until they see the painful punishment. You are dependents, so none of them shall escape except by ransom or striking of neck. Abdullah said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, except Suhayl ibn Bayda, for I heard him mention Islam. He said: So he was silent. He said: I never saw myself in a day more fearful that stones from heaven would fall upon me than that day, until he said: Except Suhayl ibn Bayda. He said: So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has thoroughly subdued in the land. You desire the passing goods of the world, and Allah desires the Hereafter, and Allah is Mighty Wise, up to His saying: Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took."
"3633","Abu Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, and he mentioned like it, except he said: Except Suhayl ibn Bayda. And he said in the saying of Abu Bakr: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, your kin and root and people, pardon them, Allah will save them through you from Hell. He said: And Abdullah ibn Rawahah said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley abundant in firewood, so kindle it with fire then cast them into it. Al-Abbas said: May Allah cut your kinship."
"3634","Husayn, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated it to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from al-Amash, and he mentioned like it, except he said: Abdullah ibn Jahsh stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, the enemies of Allah denied you, harmed you, expelled you, and fought you, and you are in a valley abundant in firewood, so gather much firewood for them then kindle it upon them. And he said: Sahl ibn Bayda."
"3635","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, from Ibn Masud: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set the blood money in unintentional killing in fifths."
"3636","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muslim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The poor is not the itinerant beggar, nor the one repelled by one date or two dates, nor one morsel or two morsels, but the poor is the abstinent who does not ask people anything and is not noticed so as to be given charity."
"3637","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: Abdullah said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray a prayer except at its appointed time, except two prayers: Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah, and Fajr that day before its time."
"3638","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hold to truthfulness, for truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise, and a man keeps telling truth until written with Allah, Exalted and Majestic, as a siddiq. Beware lying, for lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to Hell, and a man keeps lying and seeking lies until written with Allah, Exalted and Majestic, as a liar."
"3639","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am your forerunner at the Basin, and peoples will be contested with me, then I shall be overpowered over them, and I shall say: My Lord, my companions. He will say: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3640","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be rulers over you and you will see favoritism. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall whoever of us reaches that do? He said: Render the duty upon you, and ask Allah for what is yours."
"3641","I heard Yahya say: I heard Sulayman say: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb say: I heard Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: You will see after me favoritism and matters you deny. He said: We said: What do you command us? He said: Render to them their right, and ask Allah for your right."
"3642","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib who said: Abdullah said to Ibn al-Nawwahah: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Were it not that you are an envoy I would kill you. As for today, you are not an envoy. O Kharashah, stand and strike his neck. He said: So he stood to him and struck his neck."
"3643","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah, from Yusayr ibn Jabir who said: A red wind raged in Kufa, and a man came whose only utterance was: O Abdullah ibn Masud, the Hour has come. He said: He was reclining and sat up and said: The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and none rejoices at spoils. He said: An enemy gathering against the people of Islam, and the people of Islam gathering against them. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: The cry comes to them that the Dajjal has replaced them among their offspring, so they cast what is in their hands and advance, and send ten horsemen as scouts. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know their names, their fathers names, and the colors of their horses. They are the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day, or he said: They are among the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day."
"3644","Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Amr ibn Said, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: Ibn Masud said: I was not veiled from private counsel, nor from such nor from such. Ibn Awn said: So he forgot one and I forgot one. He said: So I came to him while Malik ibn Murarah al-Rahawi was with him, and I caught the end of his hadith while he says: O Messenger of Allah, there was apportioned to me of beauty what you see, and I do not love that anyone among people excels me by two straps or more. Is that not tyranny? He said: No, that is not tyranny, but tyranny is whoever rejects truth, or he said: deems truth foolish, and despises people."
"3645","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan who said: Awn narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: When you are told a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, think of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his most fitting, most guided, most God-fearing form."
"3646","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to me, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and he remained standing until I intended an evil matter. We said: What did you intend? He said: I intended to sit and leave him."
"3647","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Zubayd narrated to me, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. He said: I said to Abu Wail: Did you hear it from Abdullah? He said: Yes."
"3648","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Mansur narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none of you but his companion from jinn and his companion from angels was entrusted with him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And me, but Allah aided me over him, so he commands me only with truth."
"3649","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Mujahid informed him that Abu Ubaydah informed him, from his father who said: We were sitting in the mosque of Khayf on the night of Arafah before the day of Arafah, when we heard the sound of a snake. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill it. He said: So we stood. He said: It entered a crack of its hole, and a palm frond was brought and fire kindled in it, and we took a stick and removed part of the hole, but did not find it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave it, Allah protected it from your harm as He protected you from its harm."
"3650","Yahya narrated to us, Ismail, he is Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, Qays narrated to me, from Ibn Masud who said: We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, having no women, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate? He forbade us from that."
"3651","Yahya narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Qays narrated to me, from Ibn Masud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave wealth and empowered him over spending it in truth, and a man to whom Allah gave wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it to people."
"3652","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, my father narrated to me, from Abu Yala, from Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he drew a square line, and drew a line in the middle of the square line, and lines beside the line in the middle of the square line, and a line outside the square line. He said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This man is the middle line, and these lines beside him are the afflictions assailing him from every place, if this misses him that hits him, and the square line is the term encompassing him, and the outer line is hope."
"3653","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud: A man took a kiss from a woman and came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking about its expiation, so Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and approaches of the night. Good deeds remove evil deeds. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for me? He said: For whoever of my nation acted like this."
"3654","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The adhan of Bilal should not prevent one of you from his sahur, for he calls adhan, or he said: calls, that your standing one may return and your sleeping one may awake. It is not that he says like this, and he joined his hand and raised it, but until he says like this. Yahya separated between the two forefingers. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not hear this hadith from anyone."
"3655","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Atiq narrated to me, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Shall not the extremists perish? Three times. Yahya said: In a long hadith."
"3656","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah who said: Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the two rakahs as if upon hot stones. I said: Until he stands? He said: Until he stands."
"3657","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Jami ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah who said: I heard Ibn Masud say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from Hudaybiyah at night, and we alighted on uneven ground. He said: Who will guard us? Bilal said: I. He said: Then you will sleep. He said: No. Then he slept until the sun rose, and so-and-so and so-and-so awoke, among them Umar. He said: Move on. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke and said: Do as you used to do. When they did, he said: So do for whoever of you slept or forgot."
"3658","Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Zubayd narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: He is not of us who strikes cheeks, tears pockets, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."
"3659","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salamah who said: Abdullah said: Your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was given the keys of all things except five: Allah has knowledge of the Hour, sends down rain, knows what is in wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Allah is Knowing Aware."
"3660","Yahya narrated to us, from Zuhayr who said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying takbir in every lowering, rising, standing, and sitting, and giving salam to his right and left until the whiteness of his cheeks, or his cheek, was seen. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar do that."
"3661","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a dome, about forty, and he said: Are you pleased to be a quarter of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Are you pleased to be a third of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope you will be half of Paradise, and that is because none enters Paradise but a Muslim soul, and you among shirk are but like the white hair on the skin of a black bull, or the black on the skin of a red bull."
"3662","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was praying and said: Ask, you will be given, O son of Umm Abd. Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, hastened. Umar said: Abu Bakr never hastened with me to anything but Abu Bakr preceded me to it. They asked him about his saying, and he said: Among my supplication which I hardly leave: O Allah, I ask You bliss not perishing, coolness of eye not ending, and companionship of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Muhammad, in the highest Paradise, the Paradise of eternity."
"3663","I heard Yahya say: I heard Sulayman say: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb say: I heard Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: You will see after me favoritism and matters you deny. He said: We said: What do you command us? He said: Render to them their right, and ask Allah for your right."
"3664","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid who said: Prayer was established in the mosque, and we came walking with Abdullah ibn Masud. When people bowed, Abdullah bowed and we bowed with him while walking. A man passed before him and said: Peace upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. Abdullah said while bowing: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. When he finished, some people asked him: Why did you say when the man greeted you: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Among the signs of the Hour is when greeting is upon acquaintance."
"3665","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Talhah, from Murrah, from Abdullah who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taken by night, he was brought to Sidrat al-Muntaha, in the sixth heaven, to it ends what ascends from earth and is taken from it, and to it ends what descends from above it and is taken from it. He said: When there covered the Sidrah what covers, he said: Moths of gold. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was given three: the five prayers, the seals of Surah al-Baqarah, and forgiveness for whoever of his nation does not associate anything with Allah, the deadly sins."
"3666","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, from Zadham who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has angels on earth roaming conveying to me from my nation salam."
"3667","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise is nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and Hell is like that."
"3668","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman should not touch another woman to describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her."
"3669","Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Qays, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Follow between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes impurity of iron, gold, and silver. And the accepted Hajj has no reward less than Paradise."
"3670","Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. Then his face changed. Then he said: Like this or near this."
"3671","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Aban ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one day: Be shy of Allah, Exalted and Majestic, with true shyness. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we are shy, and praise be to Allah. He said: That is not it, but whoever is shy of Allah with true shyness, let him guard the head and what it contains, guard the belly and what it holds, remember death and decay, and whoever desires the Hereafter leaves the adornment of the world. Whoever does that is shy of Allah, Exalted and Majestic, with true shyness."
"3672","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Aban ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah divided among you your characters as He divided among you your provisions. Allah, Exalted and Majestic, gives the world to whom He loves and whom He does not love, and gives religion only to whom He loves. Whoever Allah gives religion has loved him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant submits until his heart and tongue are safe, and none believes until his neighbor is safe from his harms. They said: What are his harms, O Prophet of Allah? He said: His oppression and injustice. No servant earns wealth from unlawful then spends from it and it is blessed for him, nor gives charity with it and it is accepted from him, nor leaves it behind his back but it is his provision to Hell. Allah, Exalted and Majestic, does not erase evil with evil, but erases evil with good. The impure does not erase the impure."
"3673","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the remaining third of night comes, Allah, Exalted and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven, then the gates of heaven are opened, then He extends His Hand and says: Is there a asker given his request? It remains so until dawn rises."
"3674","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first judged between people on the Day of Resurrection is about blood."
"3675","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks while having what suffices him comes on the Day of Resurrection with scratches or marks on his face. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is his sufficiency? He said: Fifty dirhams, and its reckoning in gold."
"3676","Muhammad ibn al-Sammak narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not buy fish in water, for it is uncertainty."
"3677","Ammar ibn Muhammad, nephew of Sufyan al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, will send on the Day of Resurrection a caller calling: O Adam, Allah commands you to send a delegation from your offspring to Hell. Adam will say: My Lord, from how many? It will be said to him: From every hundred, ninety-nine. A man among people said: Who is this saved among us after this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Do you know what you are among people but like the mole on the chest of a camel?"
"3678","Ubaydah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muslim Abu Ishaq al-Hajari, and he mentioned its meaning, and said: Adam says: My Lord, how many shall I send?"
"3679","Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let one of you shield his face from Hell even with half a date."
"3680","Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the servant of one of you comes with his food, let him begin with him, feed him or seat him with him, for he endured its heat and smoke."
"3681","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah who said: Ibn Masud said: Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: So he prayed and raised his hands only once."
"3682","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated at al-Najm, and the Muslims prostrated except a man of Quraysh who took a handful of dust and raised it to his forehead and prostrated upon it. Abdullah said: I saw him afterwards killed as a disbeliever."
"3683","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: When there was revealed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When the help of Allah and victory comes, he would often, when reciting it and bowing, say: Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me, You are the Accepting Repentance, Merciful, three times."
"3684","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your permission with me is to lift the curtain and listen to my private counsel until I forbid you. My private counsel is my secret. He said: He permitted him to hear his secret."
"3685","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out for his need and said: Seek for me three stones. He said: So I brought him two stones and dung. He said: So he took the two stones and cast the dung and said: It is filth."
"3686","Waki narrated to us, from his father, from Ata, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to discourage for us evening talk after Isha."
"3687","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Isa ibn Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Omens are shirk, and there is none of us but, yet Allah removes it by trust."
"3688","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I was walking with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a field in Madinah while leaning on a palm stalk. He said: He passed by people of Jews, and some said to others: Ask him about the spirit. Some said: Do not ask him. Then they asked him about the spirit and said: O Muhammad, what is the spirit? He stood and leaned on the stalk. He said: So I thought revelation comes to him, and he said: They ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you were given of knowledge only little. He said: Some said: We told you not to ask him."
"3689","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed I am free from every close friend from his closeness, and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as close friend. Your companion is the close friend of Allah, Exalted and Majestic."
"3690","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to be brought captives and give a household all together, disliking to separate between them."
"3691","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil who said: A man came to Abu Musa and Sulayman ibn Rabiah and asked them about a daughter, a son daughter, and a sister by father. They said: For the daughter half, for the sister half, and come to Ibn Masud, he will follow us. He said: So he came to Ibn Masud and asked him and informed him of what they said. Ibn Masud said: I would have gone astray then and am not of the guided. I shall judge as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged: For the daughter half, for the son daughter a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains for the sister."
"3692","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I ask You guidance, piety, chastity, and sufficiency."
"3693","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ammar ibn Muawiyah al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ashjai, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ibn Sumayyah, never were two matters presented to him but he chose the more guided of them."
"3694","Waki narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gathered us while we were forty. Abdullah said: I was among the last to come to him. He said: You will be afflicted, aided, and opened for. Whoever of you reaches that, let him fear Allah, command good, and forbid evil. Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
"3695","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail who said: I was sitting with Abdullah and Abu Musa, and they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour are days in which ignorance descends, knowledge is raised, and harj increases. He said: We said: What is harj? He said: Killing."
"3696","Waki narrated to us, Bashir ibn Salman narrated to me, from Sayyar Abu Hamzah, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is afflicted by need and brings it to people is likely his need will not be eased, and whoever brings it to Allah, Allah brings him immediate provision or deferred death."
"3697","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khumayr ibn Malik who said: Abdullah said: I recited from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy surahs, while Zayd ibn Thabit had a forelock among schoolboys."
"3698","Amr ibn Muhammad Abu Said, meaning al-Anqazi, narrated to us, Israil informed us, and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: Abdullah said: I witnessed from al-Miqdad, Abu Nuaym said: Ibn al-Aswad, a scene, to be its man is dearer to me than what equals it. He came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he supplicates against the polytheists, and said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we shall not say as Banu Israil said to Musa: Go you and your Lord and fight, we sit here. But we fight to your right, left, before you, and behind you. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shining and pleased with that. Aswad said: I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shining for that and pleased with that. Abu Nuaym said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his face shone and pleased with that."
"3699","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to give salam to his right and left: Peace upon you and mercy of Allah. Peace upon you and mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen."
"3700","Waki narrated to us, from Misar, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah who said: Umm Habibah daughter of Abu Sufyan said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment by my husband the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by my father Abu Sufyan, and by my brother Muawiyah. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: You asked Allah for fixed terms, counted days, and divided provisions. Nothing is hastened before its time or delayed from its time. Had you asked Allah to shield you from punishment in Hell and punishment in the grave, it would have been better or more excellent. He said: And monkeys were mentioned with him, Misar said: I think he said: And pigs, that it is of what was transformed. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah never transformed anything leaving for it offspring or posterity. Monkeys or pigs existed before that."
"3701","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A companion of ours is complaining, shall we cauterize him? He said: Then he remained silent, then they said: Shall we cauterize him? And he remained silent, then he said: Cauterize him and press hot stones upon it."
"3702","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: I have not forgotten among what I have not forgotten that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheeks could be seen, or we could see the whiteness of his cheeks."
"3703","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"3704","Waki narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from Uthman al-Thaqafi or al-Hasan ibn Sad, al-Masudi doubted, from Abdah al-Nahdi, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not prohibited a sanctity except that He already knew that some violator among you would violate it. Beware, I am holding your waistbands lest you plunge into the Fire like the plunging of moths or flies."
"3705","Abu Qatan narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdah al-Nahdi, then he mentioned it, and thus Yazid and Abu Kamil said, from al-Hasan ibn Sad. Rawh said: Al-Masudi narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, and he said: The moths or the flies."
"3706","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Ibn Masud, he said: We used to go on expeditions with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were young men and we had no wives, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate ourselves? And he forbade us from that."
"3707","Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five or thirty-six or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the path of those who perished, and if they remain, their religion will stand for them for seventy years."
"3708","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Asim, from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah said, when Ibn al-Nawwahah was killed: This man and Ibn Uthal had come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as two envoys of Musaylimah the liar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is the messenger of Allah. Then he said: Had I been one to kill an envoy, I would have struck your necks. He said: So it became an established practice that an envoy is not to be killed. As for Ibn Uthal, Allah the Mighty and Majestic sufficed us against him, and as for this one, that kept festering in him until Allah gave power over him now."
"3709","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay down upon a mat and it left a mark on his side, so when he woke up I began wiping his side and said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not let us know so that we could spread something for you over the mat? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have I to do with this world? What am I and this world? My likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who shaded himself under a tree, then departed and left it."
"3710","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: When we returned from the expedition of al-Hudaybiyah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guard us tonight? Abdullah said: So I said: I will, until he repeated it several times, I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then you shall. He said: So I guarded them until, when it was near dawn, the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that you will sleep, overtook me, so I slept, and nothing woke us except the heat of the sun on our backs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and did as he used to do of ablution and the two rakahs of Fajr, then he led us in the morning prayer. When he finished he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic, had He willed that you not sleep, you would not have slept, but He willed that you be an example for those after you. So this is the way for whoever sleeps or forgets. He said: Then the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the camels of the people scattered, so the people went out seeking them and brought back their camels except the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Take this way. So I took the way he told me, and I found its bridle twisted around a tree; none but a hand could have untied it. He said: So I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One Who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, I found its bridle twisted around a tree; none but a hand could have untied it. He said: And there was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Surat al-Fath: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory."
"3711","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Jabir, from Abu Majid, he said: A man brought the son of his brother to Ibn Masud and said: This son of my brother has drunk. Abdullah said: I know the first prescribed punishment that occurred in Islam: A woman stole and her hand was cut, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed severely because of that, then he said: Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"3712","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, Abu Salamah al-Juhani narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is ever afflicted with worry or grief and then says: O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your decree concerning me is carried out, Your judgment concerning me is just; I ask You by every name that is Yours, by which You named Yourself, or taught to any of Your creation, or sent down in Your Book, or kept exclusive in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the dispeller of my sorrow, and the remover of my worry, except that Allah removes his worry and grief and replaces them with relief. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not learn it? He said: Yes indeed, whoever hears it should learn it."
"3713","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Ali ibn Budhaymah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Children of Israil fell into acts of disobedience, their scholars forbade them but they did not desist, so they sat with them in their gatherings, Yazid said: I think he said: And in their markets, and ate with them and drank with them, so Allah struck the hearts of some of them against others and cursed them upon the tongue of Dawud and Isa son of Maryam, because they disobeyed and used to transgress. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining, then he sat up and said: No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, until you force them back to the truth forcefully."
"3714","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The last one to enter Paradise is a man who walks upon the Sirat, stumbling once and walking once, and the Fire scorches him once. When he passes beyond the Sirat he turns toward it and says: Blessed is the One Who saved me from you. Allah has given me what He has not given anyone among the first and the last. He said: Then a tree is raised for him, and he looks at it and says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may shade myself in its shade and drink from its water. Then He says: O My servant, perhaps if I bring you near to it you will ask Me for something else. He says: No, my Lord. And he covenants with Allah that he will not ask Him for anything else, while the Lord the Mighty and Majestic knows that he will ask Him, because he sees that over which he has no patience. So He brings him near to it. Then another tree is raised for him, more beautiful than it, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may shade myself in its shade and drink from its water. He says: O My servant, did you not covenant with Me, meaning that you would not ask Me for anything else? He says: My Lord, this one, I will not ask You for anything else. And he covenants with Him, while the Lord knows that he will ask Him for something else. So He brings him near to it. Then a tree is raised for him at the gate of Paradise, more beautiful than it, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may shade myself in its shade and drink from its water. He says: O My servant, did you not covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything else? He says: My Lord, this tree, I will not ask You for anything else. And he covenants with Him, while the Lord knows that he will ask Him for something else, because he sees that over which he has no patience. So He brings him near to it, and he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and says: My Lord, Paradise, Paradise. He says: My servant, did you not covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything else? He says: My Lord, admit me into Paradise. He said: Then He the Mighty and Majestic says: What will make you stop asking Me, O My servant? Will it please you that I give you of Paradise the world and its like along with it? He says: Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might? He said: Then Abdullah laughed until his molars showed, then he said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said to him: Why did you laugh? He said: Because of the laughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because of the laughter of the Lord when he said: Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might?"
"3715","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Sad, from Abu al-Kanud, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us gold rings, or a gold ring."
"3716","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire."
"3717","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent any of you from his suhur, for he only calls, or he said: He only gives the adhan, so that your standing one may return and your sleeping one may be alerted. It is not that he says like this, but rather until he says like this. Ibn Abi Adi, Abu Amr, joined his fingers and pointed them downward and opened what was between his two forefingers, meaning the dawn."
"3718","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A person is with whom he loves."
"3719","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among what he often said: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me. He said: Then when There came the help of Allah and the victory was revealed, he said: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful."
"3720","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He taught us the sermon of need: Praise be to Allah, we seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead him, and whomever He misguides, none can guide him. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recites three verses: O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims; O people, fear your Lord Who created you from a single soul and created from it its mate and spread from them many men and women, and fear Allah by Whom you ask one another and the wombs; indeed Allah is watchful over you; O you who believe, fear Allah and speak upright words; He will amend your deeds for you and forgive your sins, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained a great triumph. Then you mention your need."
"3721","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, from Abu Ubaydah and Abu al-Ahwas, he said: And this is the hadith of Abu Ubaydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us two sermons: The sermon of need and the sermon of prayer: Praise be to Allah, or: Indeed praise be to Allah, we seek His help, then he mentioned its meaning."
"3722","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating with people of Quraysh around him, Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt came with the intestines of a slaughtered camel and threw them upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not raise his head. Then Fatimah came and took them off his back and invoked against whoever did that. He said: Then he said: O Allah, upon You are the chiefs of Quraysh: Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Utbah ibn Rabiah, Shaybah ibn Rabiah, Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, or Ubayy ibn Khalaf, Shubah, the doubter, narrated to us. He said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr and thrown into a well, except that the limbs of Umayyah or Ubayy were severed, so he was not thrown into the well."
"3723","Khalaf narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Amr ibn Hisham and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and he added: And Imarah ibn al-Walid."
"3724","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, from Abdullah, that he said: I heard a man reciting a verse, while I had heard something different from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed, or I recognized displeasure in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Both of you are doing well. Those before you differed concerning it and it destroyed them. Shubah said: And Misar narrated to me from him, and he raised it to Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So do not differ."
"3725","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrating from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: Two bargains in one bargain are not lawful, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the eater of usury, its giver, its witness, and its scribe."
"3726","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, Shubah said: And I think he raised it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The likeness of one who aids his tribe in wrongdoing is that of a camel that has fallen into a well, pulling itself out by its tail."
"3727","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A man keeps speaking the truth and seeking the truth until he is recorded as a truthful one, and he keeps lying and seeking falsehood until he is recorded as a liar."
"3728","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayrah, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"3729","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"3730","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ribi, from al-Bara ibn Najiyah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five or thirty-six or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the path of those who have perished, and if their religion stands for them, it will stand for them for seventy years. He said: I said: Of what has passed or of what remains? He said: Of what remains."
"3731","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Bara ibn Najiyah al-Kahili, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except that he said: Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, of what has passed or of what remains? He said: Of what remains."
"3732","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have permitted you to lift the curtain and hear my private words until I forbid you."
"3733","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sad ibn Iyad, from Abdullah, he said: The most beloved meaty bone to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the foreleg, the foreleg of the sheep, and he had been poisoned in the foreleg, and he thought that the Jews were the ones who poisoned him."
"3734","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya al-Jabir Abu al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to us, that Abu Majid, a man of Banu Hanifah, narrated to him, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: We asked our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral, and he said: The pace is less than trotting. If it is good, it is hastened to it, or he said: Let it be hastened to it, and if it is other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral bier is followed and does not follow. He who goes ahead of it is not from us."
"3735","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Aqmar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."
"3736","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying the takbir at every lowering and lifting, standing and sitting, and saying the salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until I could see the whiteness of his cheek. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar doing that."
"3737","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury, its giver, its two witnesses, and its scribe."
"3738","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he used to teach us a surah of the Quran."
"3739","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sharik, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"3740","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: The heart did not lie about what it saw, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibril in a garment of green brocade filling what is between the heaven and the earth."
"3741","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: Indeed I am the Provider, Possessor of power, the Strong."
"3742","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he laid his side upon his bed, said: Protect me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants."
"3743","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then command men who do not pray with us that their houses be burned over them."
"3744","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, and Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, Abu Ahmad said: From Ibn Masud, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to supplicate three times and to seek forgiveness three times."
"3745","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: Since There came the help of Allah and the victory was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he often said, when he recited it and then bowed with it, saying: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful, three times."
"3746","Abdullah ibn Yazid and Yunus said: Dawud, meaning Ibn al-Furat, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, he said: While Ibn Masud was delivering a sermon one day, there was a snake moving along the wall, so he cut short his sermon and struck it with his stick, or with a reed, Yunus said: With his stick, until he killed it, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he has killed a polytheist man whose blood has become lawful."
"3747","Abdullah ibn Yazid and Yunus said: Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from Ibn Masud, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about monkeys and pigs, whether they are from the progeny of the Jews. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah never cursed a people and transformed them and then gave them progeny so that He destroys them, but this was an existing creation. When Allah became angry with the Jews, He transformed them and made them like them."
"3748","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibril in his true form, with six hundred wings, each wing filling the horizon, falling from his wings marvels and pearls and rubies known only to Allah."
"3749","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, concerning His saying: And Allah took Ibrahim as a close friend, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed me, from Khalid ibn Ribi, from Ibn Masud, that he said: Allah took your companion as a close friend, meaning Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3750","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ribi al-Asadi, he said: I heard Ibn Masud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Your companion is the close friend of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3751","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ribi al-Asadi, that he heard Ibn Masud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Your companion is the close friend of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3752","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Khalid ibn Ribi, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion is the close friend of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3753","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik, from Khalid ibn Ribi, he said: Abdullah said: Your companion is the close friend of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"3754","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from his father, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury, however much it be, its end becomes little."
"3755","Hajjaj narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: And We have made the Quran easy for remembrance, so is there any who will remember. A man said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, muddakir or mudhdhakkir? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite muddakir."
"3756","Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses are of three kinds: A horse for al-Rahman, a horse for man, and a horse for Satan. As for the horse of al-Rahman, it is that which is tied in the path of Allah, so its fodder, dung, and urine, and he mentioned what Allah willed. As for the horse of Satan, it is that upon which bets are placed or races are wagered. As for the horse of man, it is the horse that a man keeps, seeking its offspring, and it shields him from poverty."
"3757","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, al-Rukayn narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from a man of the Ansar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses are of three kinds, then he mentioned the hadith."
"3758","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ribi, from al-Bara ibn Najiyah al-Kahili, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will pass after thirty-five or thirty-six or thirty-seven years. If it perishes, then like the path of those who were destroyed, and if their religion stands for them, it will stand for them for seventy years. He said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, of what has passed or of what remains? He said: Rather of what remains."
"3759","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Israil ibn Yunus, from al-Walid ibn Hisham, freedman of al-Hamdaniyyin, from Zayd ibn Zaidah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Let none of you convey to me anything about any of my Companions, for I love to come out to you with a sound heart. He said: Wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he divided it. He said: Then I passed by two men, one of them saying to his companion: By Allah, Muhammad did not intend by his division the face of Allah nor the Hereafter. So I waited until I heard what they said, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you said to us: Let none of you convey to me anything about any of my Companions, yet I passed by so-and-so and so-and-so while they were saying such and such. He said: Then the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reddened and it grieved him, then he said: Leave us from you. Musa was harmed with more than that, then he was patient."
"3760","Abu al-Nadr and Hasan ibn Musa said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night prayer, then he came out to the mosque and the people were waiting for the prayer. He said: Indeed, there is none among the people of these religions who remembers Allah at this hour besides you. He said: And these verses were revealed: They are not alike; among the People of the Book, until he reached: And whatever good you do, you will never be denied it, and Allah knows the pious."
"3761","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Ibn al-Nawwahah and Ibn Uthal came as two envoys of Musaylimah to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to them: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is the messenger of Allah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. Had I been one to kill an envoy, I would have killed you. Abdullah said: He said: So the practice continued that envoys are not to be killed."
"3762","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to regard the signs at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as blessings, while you regard them as frightening."
"3763","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a resting place and went off for his need. Then he came back while a man had kindled a fire over an ant colony, either in the ground or in a tree. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you did this? A man of the people said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put it out, put it out."
"3764","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Said ibn Amr ibn Jadah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about Laylat al-Qadr. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you remembers the night of the pale ones? Abdullah said: I do, by Allah I remember it, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, while there were dates in my hands with which I was taking suhur, sheltered by the back of my saddle from the dawn, and that was when the moon had risen."
"3765","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, the Ansar said: From us an amir and from you an amir. He said: Then Umar came to them and said: O company of the Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? Which of you would feel content to step ahead of Abu Bakr? They said: We seek refuge with Allah from stepping ahead of Abu Bakr."
"3766","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Sulayman, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prolonged the standing until I thought of an evil thought. He said: We said: And what was it? He said: I thought of sitting down."
"3767","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Ibn Masud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wrongdoing is greatest? He said: A span of land that one takes from the right of his brother. There is no pebble of the earth he takes except that he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection down to the depths of the earth, and none knows its depths except the One Who created it."
"3768","Abu Said narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from Ibn Masud, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about monkeys and pigs, whether they are from the progeny of the Jews. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah never cursed a people and transformed them while they had progeny so that He destroys them, but Allah the Mighty and Majestic became angry with the Jews and transformed them and made them like them."
"3769","Abu Said narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to supplicate three times and to seek forgiveness three times."
"3770","Abu Said narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: Indeed I am the Provider, Possessor of power, the Strong."
"3771","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifah, that Abu Muhammad informed him, and he was among the companions of Ibn Masud, he narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned the martyrs in his presence and said: Most of the martyrs of my ummah are companions of beds, and many a slain one between two ranks, Allah knows best his intention."
"3772","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wrongdoing is most unjust? He said: A span of land that a Muslim man takes from the right of his brother. There is no pebble of the earth that anyone takes except that he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection down to the depths of the earth, and none knows its depths except Allah the Mighty and Majestic Who created it."
"3773","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Rukayn narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked ten traits: Yellowness, changing gray hair, wearing gold rings, dragging the lower garment, displaying adornment in an unlawful setting, striking dice, withholding water from its place, corrupting the child without making him unlawful, tying amulets, and incantations except with the two protective surahs."
"3774","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the House and supplicated against a group of Quraysh, seven, among them Abu Jahl, Umayyah ibn Khalaf, Utbah ibn Rabiah, Shaybah, and Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt. I swear by Allah, I saw them fallen at Badr, discolored by the sun, and it was a hot day."
"3775","Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Isa ibn Dinar al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me that he heard Amr ibn al-Harith al-Khuzai say: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I did not fast with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine days more often than I fasted with him thirty days."
"3776","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sad or Said ibn Iyad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The most beloved meat with bone to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the foreleg of the sheep, and he thought that he was poisoned in the foreleg of the sheep, and we thought that the Jews were the ones who poisoned him."
"3777","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sad ibn Iyad, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Part of eloquence is magic. He said: And we thought that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was poisoned in the foreleg of a sheep; the Jews poisoned him."
"3778","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is none among you except that with him is his companion from the angels and from the jinn. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And me, except that Allah aided me against him so he submitted, and he commands me only with good."
"3779","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I came to Zirr ibn Hubaysh with two cloaks upon me, and affection for him was cast upon me, and there were youths with him, so they said to me: Ask him about: He was two bow-lengths or nearer. So I asked him, and he said: Abdullah ibn Masud narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibril, peace be upon him, with six hundred wings."
"3780","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: We were sitting with Abdullah ibn Masud while he was teaching us the Quran, when a man said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how many caliphs this ummah will have? Abdullah ibn Masud said: None has asked me about it since I came to Iraq before you. Then he said: Yes, we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Twelve, like the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israil."
"3781","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with them, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abdullah, do you have water with you? He said: I have nabidh in a waterskin with me. He said: Pour for me. Then he performed ablution. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah ibn Masud, a drink and a purifier."
"3782","Hasan and Abu al-Nadr and Aswad ibn Amir said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with them, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two bargains in one bargain. Aswad said: Sharik said: Simak said: A man sells a sale and says: It is on credit for such and such, and it is for cash for such and such."
"3783","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shaybah, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange and it will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: And who are the strangers? He said: Those who detach themselves from the tribes."
"3784","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man who had never done any good except tawhid, when death came to him, said to his family: When I die, take me and burn me until you leave me as charred coal, then grind me, then scatter me in the sea on a windy day. He said: So they did that to him. He said: Then he was in the grasp of Allah. He said: Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic said to him: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You. He said: So Allah forgave him."
"3785","Yahya said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3786","Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani narrated to us, from Uthman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, he said: The two sons of Mulaykah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our mother used to honor her husband and show affection to her child, he said: And he mentioned the guest, except that she had buried a daughter alive in the Jahiliyyah. He said: Your mother is in the Fire. So they turned away with evil seen in their faces, and he ordered them to be brought back, and they returned with joy seen in their faces, hoping that something had happened. Then he said: My mother is with your mother. A man of the hypocrites said: What does this avail his mother at all, while we tread upon his heels? A man of the Ansar said, and I never saw a man who asked more questions than him: O Messenger of Allah, has your Lord promised you concerning her or concerning them? He said: Then he thought it was from something he had heard, so he said: I have not asked my Lord about it, nor has He given me hope concerning it, but I shall stand the praiseworthy station on the Day of Resurrection. The Ansari said: And what is that praiseworthy station? He said: That is when you are brought naked, barefoot, uncircumcised, and the first to be clothed is Ibrahim, peace be upon him. He says: Clothe My close friend. Then two white garments are brought and he wears them, then he sits facing the Throne. Then my garment is brought and I wear it, and I stand at his right, a station where none but I shall stand, envied by the first and the last for it. He said: And a river is opened from al-Kawthar to the Hawd. The hypocrites said: Water never flows except over mud or small pebbles. He said: O Messenger of Allah, over mud or small pebbles? He said: Its mud is musk and its pebbles are aromatic rush. The hypocrite said: I have never heard like today; seldom does water flow over mud or pebbles without having vegetation. The Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have vegetation? He said: Yes, rods of gold. The hypocrite said: I have never heard like today; seldom does a rod grow without putting forth leaves or having fruit. The Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have fruit? He said: Yes, varieties of jewels, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks a draught from it will never thirst after it, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after it."
"3787","Arim and Affan said: Mutamir narrated to us, he said: My father said: Abu Tamimah narrated to me, from Amr, perhaps he said: Al-Bikali, Amr narrates to him, from Abdullah ibn Masud, Amr said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me forth. He said: So we set out until I came to such and such a place, and he drew a line for me and said to me: Stay within this line, do not leave it, for if you leave it you will perish. He said: So I stayed in it. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on a short distance, or farther, or as he said. Then he mentioned some people as if they were al-Zutt. Affan said, or as Affan said, Allah willing: They had no clothes upon them, and I could not see their private parts, tall, little flesh. He said: Then they came and began crowding upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began reciting to them. He said: And they began coming to me, appearing around me, or inclining around me, and blocking my way. Abdullah said: So I was seized with intense terror of them. He said: Then I sat, or as he said. He said: When the column of dawn broke, they began to leave, or as he said. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, heavy and in pain, or nearly in pain, from their crowding upon him. He said: I feel heavy, or as he said. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his head in my lap, or as he said. He said: Then some people came wearing long white garments, or as he said, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had dozed off. Abdullah said: So I was seized with terror of them more intense than what seized me the first time. Arim said in his hadith: He said: Then some of them said to others: This servant has been given good, or as they said. His eyes are sleeping, or he said: His eye, or as they said, while his heart is awake. Then he said: Arim and Affan said: Some of them said to others: Come, let us strike a parable for him, or as they said. Some of them said to others: Strike a parable for him, and we shall interpret, or: We shall strike and you interpret. Then some of them said to others: His likeness is that of a chief who built a fortified building, then sent to the people with food, or as he said. Whoever does not come to his food, or he said: Does not follow him, he will punish him with a severe punishment, or as they said. The others said: As for the chief, he is the Lord of the worlds, and as for the building, it is Islam, and the food is Paradise, and he is the caller. Whoever follows him will be in Paradise. Arim said in his hadith, or as they said: And whoever does not follow him will be punished, or as he said. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: What did you see, O Ibn Umm Abd? Abdullah said: I saw such and such. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of what they said was hidden from me. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are a group of angels, or he said: They are among the angels, or as Allah willed."
"3788","Arim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a grain of faith, nor shall any enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a grain of arrogance. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I like my garment to be clean, my head oiled, and the strap of my sandal new, and he mentioned things until he mentioned the thong of his whip. Is that arrogance, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, that is beauty. Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Rather arrogance is rejecting the truth and despising people."
"3789","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men will take charge of your affairs after me who extinguish the Sunnah, innovate novelties, and delay the prayer from its times. Ibn Masud said: O Messenger of Allah, how should I act when I meet them? He said: There is no obedience, O Ibn Umm Abd, to one who disobeys Allah. He said it three times."
"3790","And I myself heard the like of it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah."
"3791","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail informed us, Amr ibn Abi Amr informed me, from Ubayd Allah and Hamzah, sons of Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat meat and then stand for prayer without touching water."
"3792","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Ibn Masud, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat meat and then stand for prayer without touching a drop of water."
"3793","Abu Said narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Ibn Masud, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat meat and then stand for prayer without touching water."
"3794","Abu Said narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: Sad ibn Muadh set out for umrah and stayed with Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and Umayyah, when he set out for Sham and passed by Madinah, used to stay with Sad. Umayyah said to Sad: Wait until midday when people are heedless, then go and circumambulate. While Sad was circumambulating, Abu Jahl came to him and said: Who is this circumambulating the Kabah in security? He said: Sad said: I am Sad. Abu Jahl said: You circumambulate the Kabah in security while you have sheltered Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him. So they exchanged harsh words. Umayyah said to Sad: Do not raise your voice against Abu al-Hakam, for he is the chief of the people of the valley. Sad said to him: By Allah, if you prevent me from circumambulating the House, I shall cut off your trade route to Sham. Umayyah kept saying: Do not raise your voice against Abu al-Hakam, and kept holding him back. Sad became angry and said: Leave us from you, for I heard Muhammad claim that he will kill you. He said: Me? He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, Muhammad does not lie. When they left, he returned to his wife and said: Do you not know what the Yathribi said to me? And he told her. When the war cry came and they went out to Badr, his wife said: Do you not remember what your Yathribi brother said? He wanted not to go out, but Abu Jahl said to him: You are among the nobles of the valley, so march with us a day or two. So he marched with them, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic killed him."
"3795","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: Sad ibn Muadh set out for umrah staying with Umayyah ibn Khalaf ibn Safwan, and Umayyah, when he set out for Sham and passed by Madinah, used to stay with Sad, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Then he returned to Umm Safwan and said: Do you not know what my Yathribi brother said? She said: And what did he say? He said: He claimed that he heard Muhammad claim that he will kill me. She said: By Allah, Muhammad does not lie. When they went out to Badr, and he drove him on."
"3796","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he slept he placed his right hand under his cheek and said: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants."
"3797","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that he was in the mosque supplicating, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while he was supplicating and said: Ask, you will be given. While he was saying: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not apostatize, bliss that does not end, and companionship of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest chambers of Paradise, the Paradise of eternity."
"3798","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me in wakefulness, for Satan cannot assume my form."
"3799","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3800","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Duha, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has guardians, and my guardian among them is my father and the close friend of my Lord, Ibrahim. He said: Then he recited: Indeed the worthiest of people of Ibrahim, to the end of the verse."
"3801","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Muammal narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in a red tent - Abd al-Malik said: of leather - among about forty men, and he said: Conquests will be opened for you, and you will be aided and successful, so whoever of you lives to see that, let him fear Allah and enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and uphold his kinship. Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell. And the likeness of one who aids his people in other than truth is like a camel thrown down into a well, pulling itself out by its tail."
"3802","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none of you but that a companion from the jinn and a companion from the angels has been assigned to him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And me, but Allah has aided me against him so he has submitted, and he commands me with nothing but good."
"3803","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammam, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: I heard a man reciting Ha-Mim, the thirtieth, meaning al-Ahqaf, and he recited a letter, and another man recited a letter his companion had not recited, and I recited letters my two companions had not recited, so we went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him, and he said: Do not differ, for those before you perished only through their differing. Then he said: Look to the best reciter among you as a man, and take his recitation."
"3804","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad and from Abu Sad, from Abu al-Kanud who said: I found a gold ring in one of the expeditions and wore it, then I came to Abdullah, and he took it and placed it between his jaws and chewed it, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing a gold ring - or he said: a gold band."
"3805","Yazid narrated to us: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated in Surat al-Najm, and none of the people remained except he prostrated, except an old man who took a handful of pebbles and raised it to his forehead and said: This suffices me. Abdullah said: I saw him afterward killed as a disbeliever."
"3806","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Ibn Masud who said: We spoke at length in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, then we came to him in the morning, and he said: The prophets with their nations were shown to me tonight, and a prophet would pass with three men, and a prophet with a group, and a prophet with a few men, and a prophet with no one with him, until Musa passed by me with a great company of the Children of Israel, and they impressed me, and I said: Who are these. It was said to me: This is your brother Musa with the Children of Israel. He said: I said: Then where is my nation. It was said to me: Look to your right. I looked, and behold, the hills were covered with the faces of men. Then it was said to me: Look to your left. I looked, and behold, the horizon was covered with the faces of men. It was said to me: Are you pleased. I said: I am pleased, my Lord, I am pleased, my Lord. He said: It was said to me: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, if you can be among the seventy thousand, then do so, and if you fall short, then be among the people of the hills, and if you fall short, then be among the people of the horizon, for I saw there people crowding together. Then Ukkasha ibn Mihsan stood and said: Supplicate Allah for me, O Messenger of Allah, to make me among the seventy. So he supplicated for him. Then another man stood and said: Supplicate Allah, O Messenger of Allah, to make me among them. He said: Ukkasha has preceded you in it. He said: Then we talked and said: Who do you think these seventy thousand are - people born in Islam who never associated anything with Allah until they died. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: They are those who do not cauterize, and do not seek ruqya, and do not take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"3807","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and they found no water, so a small vessel of water was brought, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand in it and spread his fingers. He said: I saw the water gushing forth from between the fingers of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said: Come to ablution and blessing from Allah. Al-Amash said: Salim ibn Abi al-Jad informed me, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Abdullah: How many were the people that day. He said: We were one thousand five hundred."
"3808","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: A man said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: How can I know when I have done good and when I have done wrong. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you hear your neighbors saying: You have done good, then you have done good, and when you hear them saying: You have done wrong, then you have done wrong."
"3809","Hajjaj narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah has cursed the consumer of usury and its provider and its two witnesses and its scribe. He said: And he said: Usury and adultery do not appear among a people except they bring upon themselves the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3810","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Fazara, from Abu Zayd, the freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Masud who said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night he met the jinn, and he said: Do you have water with you. I said: No. He said: What is this in the waterskin. I said: Nabidh. He said: Show it to me. Dates are wholesome and water is pure. So he performed ablution from it, then led us in prayer."
"3811","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wail who said: Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever assigns a rival to Allah, Allah will place him in Hell. And he said: And another saying which I say and did not hear from him: Whoever dies without assigning a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to Paradise. And these prayers are expiations for what is between them, so long as mortal sin is avoided."
"3812","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and men will be contested with me over it and I will be overcome regarding them, and I will say: My Lord, my companions. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3813","Rawh narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast while traveling and break his fast, and he would pray two rakas and not leave them, saying: He does not add to them, meaning the obligatory prayer."
"3814","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Asim narrating, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
"3815","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"3816","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about people who stay behind from Friday prayer: I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn down the houses of men who stay behind from Friday prayer. Zuhayr said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us that he heard it from Abu al-Ahwas."
"3817","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah and Abu Musa al-Ashari, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour there will be days in which knowledge will be taken away and ignorance will descend and harj will increase. He said: And harj is killing."
"3818","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Iyad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware of belittled sins, for they gather upon a man until they destroy him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck a parable for them like a people who camped in a barren land, and the time for preparing food came, so one man went and brought a stick, and another man brought a stick, until they gathered a pile, and they kindled a fire and cooked what they threw into it."
"3819","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shown the nations at the season, and his nation was late in coming to him. He said: Then my nation was shown to me, and their multitude pleased me, filling the plain and the mountain. It was said to me: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not cauterize, and do not seek ruqya, and do not take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. Then Ukkasha said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. So he supplicated for him. Then another, meaning another man, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me with them. He said: Ukkasha has preceded you in it."
"3820","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: How will you recognize of your nation those who never saw you. He said: They will be radiant with white marks from the traces of ablution."
"3821","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the remaining third of the night comes, He descends to the lowest heaven, then He opens the doors of heaven, then He extends His hand and says: Is there any asker who will be given what he asks. And He remains so until dawn breaks."
"3822","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, from Karim ibn Abi Hazim, from his grandmother Salma bint Jabir, that her husband was martyred, so she came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: I am a woman whose husband has been martyred, and men have proposed to me, but I refused to marry until I meet him, so do you hope for me, if I am gathered with him, that I will be among his wives. He said: Yes. Then a man said to him: We never saw you transmit this since we sat with you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The quickest of my nation to join me in Paradise is a woman from Ahmas."
"3823","Muhadir Abu al-Muwarri narrated to us: Asim narrated to us, from Awsaja ibn al-Rammah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, You have made my creation good, so make my character good."
"3824","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubayda, from his father who said: I came to Abu Jahl when he had been wounded and his leg cut off. He said: I struck him with my sword but it had no effect on him. It was said to Sharik in the hadith: And he was fending with his sword. He said: Yes. He said: I kept on until I took his sword and struck him with it until I killed him. He said: Then he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Abu Jahl has been killed - and perhaps Sharik said: I have killed Abu Jahl. He said: Did you see him yourself. I said: Yes. He said: By Allah - twice. I said: Yes. He said: Then go until I look at him. So he went and came to him when the sun had changed him somewhat, and he ordered him and his companions to be dragged until they were thrown into the well. He said: And the people of the well were followed with a curse. And he said: This was the Pharaoh of this nation."
"3825","Aswad narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: This is the Pharaoh of my nation."
"3826","Talq ibn Ghannam ibn Talq narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from his father who said: A shaykh from Banu Asad narrated to me - either he said Shaqiq, or he said Zirr - from Abdullah who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicating for this tribe of al-Nakha - or he said: praising them - until I wished I were a man among them."
"3827","Abu Salama narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Masud who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating meat, then rising to prayer without touching a drop of water."
"3828","Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to seek refuge from Satan, from his hamz, his nafth, and his nafk. He said: His hamz is madness, his nafth is poetry, and his nafk is arrogance."
"3829","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murra, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The polytheists detained the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Asr prayer until the sun turned yellow - or red - so he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer. May Allah fill their bellies - or: May Allah fill their bellies and their graves - with fire."
"3830","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us - and I heard it myself from Abdullah - he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his hamz, his nafth, and his nafk. His hamz is madness, his nafth is poetry, and his nafk is pride."
"3831","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A people will emerge at the end of time, foolish in minds, young - or he said: youthful - in age, speaking with the best speech of men, reciting the Quran with their tongues, not passing their throats, passing through Islam as the arrow passes through the prey. Whoever meets them, let him kill them, for in killing them there is a great reward with Allah for whoever kills them."
"3832","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The first to proclaim their Islam were seven: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abu Bakr, Ammar and his mother Sumayya, Suhayb, Bilal, and al-Miqdad. As for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Allah protected him through his uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abu Bakr, Allah protected him through his people. As for the rest, the polytheists seized them and dressed them in coats of iron and scorched them in the sun, and there was none of them but he complied with what they wanted, except Bilal, for his soul was cheap to him for the sake of Allah and he was cheap to his people, so they gave him to the children who took him around the ravines of Makka while he said: One, One."
"3833","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah narrated to them that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your permission regarding me is that you lift the curtain and listen to my private conversation until I forbid you."
"3834","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us, he said: Sulayman said: I heard them mentioning, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your permission regarding me is that you uncover the curtain."
"3835","Abu Qatan narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at a resting place, and a man went to a thicket and took out the eggs of a humara bird, so the humara came fluttering over the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the heads of his companions. He said: Which of you has bereaved this one. A man among the people said: I took its eggs. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Return it."
"3836","Yazid narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at a resting place, and he mentioned the like of it, and he said: Return it out of mercy to her."
"3837","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us: Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Muayz al-Sadi who said: I went out in the early morning to water a horse of mine, and I passed the mosque of Banu Hanifa while they were saying: Musaylima is the messenger of Allah. So I came to Abdullah and told him, and he sent the police, and they brought them, and he asked them to repent, and they repented, so he released them, but he struck the neck of Abdullah ibn al-Nawwaha. They said: You seized people for one matter, then killed some of them and left some. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when this man and Ibn Uthal ibn Hajar came to him - say: Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah. They said: We testify that Musaylima is the messenger of Allah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. Had I been one to kill envoys, I would have killed you two. So for that reason I killed him."
"3838","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Respond to the caller, do not refuse a gift, and do not strike the Muslims."
"3839","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believer is not a stabber, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-tongued. And Ibn Sabiq once said: Not a stabber nor a curser."
"3840","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Isa ibn Dinar narrated to us: My father narrated to me that he heard Amr ibn al-Harith saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud saying: I did not fast twenty-nine days with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more often than I fasted thirty with him."
"3841","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq who said: I was sitting with Abdullah and Abu Musa while they were conversing, and they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour there will be days in which knowledge will be taken away and ignorance will descend and harj will appear. And harj is killing."
"3842","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us: Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away, the Ansar said: From us a leader and from you a leader. Then Umar came to them and said: O company of Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. They said: Yes. He said: Who among you would feel comfortable preceding Abu Bakr. The Ansar said: We seek refuge in Allah from preceding Abu Bakr."
"3843","Muawiya narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: A black slave joined the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then died, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was informed. He said: See if he left anything. They said: He left two dinars. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two brands."
"3844","Muawiya narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while they are alive, and those who take graves as mosques."
"3845","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis who said: A man from Hamdan among the companions of Abdullah narrated to us - and he did not name him to us - he said: When Abdullah wanted to come to Madina, he gathered his companions and said: By Allah, I hope that today among you are among the best found in the armies of the Muslims in religion, understanding, and knowledge of the Quran. This Quran was revealed in modes, and by Allah, two men would dispute as fiercely as men ever dispute over anything, yet when one reciter said: This is how he taught me, he would say: You have done well, and when the other said it, he would say: Both of you have done well, and he taught us. Truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise, and lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to Hell. Consider that by the saying of one of you to his companion: You lied and acted wickedly, and by his saying when he believes him: You spoke the truth and did right. This Quran does not differ, nor wear out, nor become stale from much repetition. Whoever recites it in one mode, let him not abandon it out of aversion to it, and whoever recites it in any of those modes which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught, let him not abandon it out of aversion to it, for whoever denies a verse of it denies all of it. It is like the saying of one of you to his companion: Come quickly - the like thereof. By Allah, had I known a man more knowledgeable of what Allah revealed to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than me, I would have sought him out to add his knowledge to mine. There will be people who kill prayer, so pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them voluntary. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to have the Quran reviewed with him every Ramadan, and I reviewed with him in the year he passed away twice, and he told me that I do well. And I learned from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy suras."
"3846","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Khumayr ibn Malik, from Abdullah who said: I learned from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy suras, while Zayd ibn Thabit was still a boy with a forelock among the schoolchildren."
"3847","Hashim narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim - and Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell. One of them said: In the Fire."
"3848","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Ayyash al-Amiri, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the signs of the Hour is that a man greets another man, greeting him only for acquaintance."
"3849","Hashim and Husayn, with the same meaning, said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas and al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, giving salam to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his right cheek appeared, and to his left likewise."
"3850","Hashim and Hasan ibn Musa said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and men of my companions will surely be contested with me and I will surely be overcome regarding them, then it will surely be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3851","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Abdullah, that the envoy of Musaylima came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to him: Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah. He said something to him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Were it not that I do not kill envoys - or: Had I killed any envoy - I would have killed you."
"3852","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: A man for whom cauterization had been prescribed was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Brand him - or: press him with hot stones."
"3853","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite: Is there any who will remember."
"3854","al-Hasan ibn Yahya, from the people of Marw, narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I obtained from a woman everything except that I did not have intercourse with her. He said: Then Allah revealed: Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night. Indeed good deeds remove evil deeds."
"3855","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a man: Were it not that you are an envoy, I would have killed you."
"3856","Umayya ibn Khalid narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has killed Abu Jahl. He said: Praise be to Allah who aided His servant and honored His religion. And once - meaning Umayya - he said: He made His servant truthful and honored His religion."
"3857","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abu Muawiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Abu al-Yafur, from Abu al-Salt, from Abu Aqrab who said: I went early to Ibn Masud one morning in Ramadan and found him sitting above his house, and we heard his voice saying: Allah has spoken the truth and His messenger has conveyed. We said: We heard you saying: Allah has spoken the truth and His messenger has conveyed. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Laylat al-Qadr is in the middle of the last seven of Ramadan. The sun rises that morning clear, with no rays. So I looked at it and found it as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"3858","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us: Abu Yafur narrated to us, from Abu al-Salt, from Abu Aqrab al-Asadi who said: I went early to Abdullah ibn Masud, and he mentioned its meaning."
"3859","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abu Aqil narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq who said: We were sitting with Abdullah in the mosque, teaching us, when a man came to him and said: O Ibn Masud, did your prophet tell you how many caliphs there will be after him. He said: Yes, like the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel."
"3860","Abu al-Nadr and Hasan said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast three days from the beginning of every crescent, and he would rarely not fast Friday."
"3861","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Said narrated to us: Qatada narrated to us - and Abd al-Wahhab, from Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of his journeys, we heard a caller calling: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon the fitra. Then he said: I testify that there is no god but Allah. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has escaped the Fire. He said: So we rushed to him, and behold, he was a herdsman whom prayer had overtaken, so he called it."
"3862","Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us: Husayn narrated to me: Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to me, he said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salama saying: I heard Ibn Masud saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw Jibril at Sidrat al-Muntaha, and he had six hundred wings. He said: I asked Asim about the wings, but he refused to tell me. He said: One of his companions told me that a wing spans what is between the east and the west."
"3863","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Husayn narrated to me: Husayn narrated to me: Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Masud saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril came to me in green with pearls hanging from it."
"3864","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Qays, from Ishaq ibn Abi al-Kahtala - Muhammad said: I think it is from Ibn Masud - that he said: Muhammad saw Jibril in his form only twice. As for one time, he asked him to show himself in his form, so he showed him his form and it filled the horizon. As for the other, he ascended with him when he was taken up, and His saying: While he was at the highest horizon, then he drew near and came down, and was at a distance of two bows or nearer, and He revealed to His servant what He revealed. He said: When Jibril perceived his Lord, he returned to his form and prostrated. So His saying: And he saw him at another descent, at Sidrat al-Muntaha, near it is the Garden of Refuge, when there covered the Sidra what covered, the sight did not swerve nor transgress, he saw of the great signs of his Lord - he said: The creation of Jibril, peace be upon him."
"3865","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail who said: Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever assigns a rival to Allah, Allah will place him in the Fire. He said: And another which I say and did not hear from him: Whoever dies without assigning a rival to Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will admit him to Paradise. And these prayers are expiations for what is between them, so long as mortal sin is avoided."
"3866","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and men will surely be contested with me and I will be overcome regarding them, and I will say: My Lord, my companions. Then he will say: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3867","Rawh narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast while traveling and break his fast, and he would pray the two rakas and not leave them, saying: He does not add to them, meaning the obligatory prayer."
"3868","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection will be a man killed by a prophet or who killed a prophet, a leader of misguidance, and a mutilator among the mutilators."
"3869","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us - he used to stay in the mosque of al-Matmura - from Sayyar Abu Hamza, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is afflicted with poverty and presents it to people, his poverty will not be closed, and whoever presents it to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah will soon grant him riches, either a hastened term or hastened riches."
"3870","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: We were sitting with Abdullah when a man came and said: Prayer has been established. So he stood, and we stood with him. When we entered the mosque, we saw the people bowing at the front of the mosque, so he said takbir and bowed, and we bowed, then we walked and did as he did. Then a man passed hurrying and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Allah and His messenger have spoken the truth. When we prayed and returned, he went in to his family and we sat. Some of us said to others: Did you hear his reply to the man: Allah has spoken the truth and His messengers have conveyed. Which of you will ask him. Tariq said: I will ask him. So he asked him when he came out, and he mentioned from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that before the Hour there will be greeting of acquaintance, prevalence of trade until a woman helps her husband in trade, severing of kinship, false testimony, concealment of true testimony, and prevalence of the pen."
"3871","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isa ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar al-Khuzai who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud saying: I did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more often than I fasted thirty with him."
"3872","Yunus narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad - he narrated to him - from his father, that Ibn Masud narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, generally departed from prayer to his left toward the chambers."
"3873","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: That I swear nine times that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was killed is dearer to me than that I swear once that he was not killed. That is because Allah made him a prophet and took him as a martyr. Al-Amash said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: They used to think that the Jews poisoned him and Abu Bakr."
"3874","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman who said: Abdullah used to stone the Jamra from the valley floor. I said: Do you stone it from here. He said: From here - by the One besides whom there is no god - stoned it the one to whom Surat al-Baqara was revealed."
"3875","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Umara, from Wahb ibn Rabia, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I was screened by the curtains of the Kaba when three men came, a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi brothers-in-law, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts, and they spoke among themselves. One of them said: Do you think Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hears what we say. Another said: I think He hears when we raise our voices and does not hear when we lower them. The other two said: If He hears anything of it, He hears all of it. He said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: You did not screen yourselves lest your hearing testify against you - until: the losers."
"3876","Waki narrated to us: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from al-Ayzar ibn Jarwal al-Hadrami, from a man among them called Abu Umayr, that he was a friend of Abdullah ibn Masud, and that Abdullah ibn Masud visited him among his family but did not find him. He said: He asked permission to see his family and greeted them and asked for a drink. He said: She sent the slave girl to bring him a drink from the neighbors, but she was late, so she cursed her. Then Abdullah left, and Abu Umayr came and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, one like you is not to be kept waiting. Why did you not greet the family of your brother and sit and partake of the drink. He said: I did so, but she sent the servant, who was late - either they had nothing, or they desired what they had - so the servant was late and she cursed her. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A curse goes to the one to whom it is directed, and if it finds a way against him or finds a path in him - otherwise it says: My Lord, I was directed to so-and-so but found no way against him and found no path in him. Then it is said to it: Return to where you came from. So I feared the servant might be excused, and the curse would return, and I would be its cause."
"3877","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taught the openings of good and its comprehensive forms - or: the comprehensive forms of good and its openings. And we did not know what to say in our prayer until we were taught. He said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger."
"3878","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had I taken anyone as a close friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a close friend."
"3879","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to give salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek was seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"3880","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I disavow every close friend from his closeness, and had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a close friend. And your companion is the close friend of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3881","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-Awar who said: Abdullah said: The consumer of usury and its provider and its scribe and its two witnesses, when they know of it, and the tattooer and the one tattooed for beautification, and the withholder of charity, and the apostate Bedouin after his migration, are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: Alqama narrated to me, he said: Abdullah said: The consumer of usury and its provider are alike."
"3882","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he arranged one rank behind him and a rank facing the enemy. He said: And they were all in prayer. He said: And he said takbir and they all said takbir, and he prayed with the rank next to him one raka, with a rank facing the enemy. He said: Then these went and those came, and he prayed with them one raka, then these who prayed with him the second raka stood and completed in their place, then these went to the positions of those, and those came and completed one raka."
"3883","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr - or Asr - as five, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: These two prostrations are for whoever among you thinks he added or omitted."
"3884","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim who said: Abdullah said: We used to greet the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, during prayer, until we returned from the Negus, when we greeted him and he did not return it to us, and he said: Prayer has preoccupation."
"3885","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu al-Radrad, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I used to greet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, during prayer and he would return it to me. Then one day I greeted him and he did not return it to me, and I felt distressed. When he finished, I said: O Messenger of Allah, when I used to greet you during prayer you returned it to me. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, introduces in His command what He wills."
"3886","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud who said: A man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Will any of us be taken to account for what he did in the Jahiliyya. He said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be taken to account for what he did in the Jahiliyya, and whoever does evil in Islam will be taken for the first and the last."
"3887","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: al-Thawri narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: Of what I have forgotten, I have not forgotten from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to give salam to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen, and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen as well."
"3888","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar and al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of the hadith of Abu al-Duha."
"3889","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How will you be, O Abdullah, when rulers will be over you who waste the Sunna and delay prayer past its time. He said: What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You ask me, Ibn Umm Abd, what to do. There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3890","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us: al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth informed me, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani saying: The master of this house narrated to us - pointing to the house of Abdullah - without naming him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which deed is most beloved to Allah. He said: Prayer at its time. He said: I said: Then which. He said: Then kindness to parents. He said: I said: Then which. He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah. He said: He told me these, and had I asked for more he would have given me more."
"3891","Affan narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard Abu Ubayda, from his father who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say often: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. O Allah, forgive me. Then when: When the help of Allah and the victory comes - was revealed, he said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. O Allah, forgive me. You are the Oft-Returning."
"3892","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ribi al-Asadi, that he heard Ibn Masud saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Your companion is the close friend of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"3893","Affan narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: We performed Hajj with Ibn Masud during the caliphate of Uthman. He said: When we stood at Arafa - he said: When the sun set, Ibn Masud said: Had the Commander of the Believers departed now, he would have done right. He said: I do not know whether the word of Ibn Masud was quicker or the departure of Uthman. He said: The people hastened, but Ibn Masud did not go beyond a gentle trot until we came to Jam. Then Ibn Masud led us in Maghrib prayer, then called for his supper and ate supper, then stood and prayed the last Isha, then slept until the first dawn broke, when he stood and prayed the morning prayer. He said: I said to him: You would not pray prayer at this hour - he said: And he used to pray at first light - he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on this day and in this place praying at this hour."
"3894","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuked evening conversation after Isha for us. Khalid said: The meaning of jadaba to us - he says: he faulted it, he condemned it."
"3895","Affan and Bahz said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: I heard Abu Ubayda narrating, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He would be in the first two rakas as if upon hot stones. I said: Until he stands. He said: Until he stands."
"3896","Affan narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: Abdullah used to say: Lying is not proper, neither in earnest nor in jest. And Affan once said: In earnest - nor may a man promise a child and then not fulfill it for him. He said: And Muhammad said to us: A man keeps speaking truth until he is written with Allah as a siddiq, and a man keeps lying until he is written with Allah as a liar."
"3897","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, who mentioned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service. At Your service, there is no partner for You, at Your service. Praise and blessing belong to You."
"3898","Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us - and I heard it myself from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba - Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: While the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in a field leaning on a palm stalk, a group of Jews stood before him and asked him about the spirit. He fell silent, then recited this verse to them: They ask you about the spirit. Say: The spirit is of the command of my Lord, and you have been given of knowledge only a little."
"3899","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The last to enter Paradise is a man who walks once and stumbles once and is scorched by the Fire once. When he passes it, he turns to it and says: Blessed is He who saved me from you. Allah has given me something He never gave any of the first or the last. Then a tree is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah says to him: O son of Adam, perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, my Lord. And he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it. He said: And his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, excuses him, for he sees what he cannot be patient over, so He brings him near it, and he shades in its shade and drinks of its water. Then a tree better than the first is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, this one, that I may drink of its water and shade in its shade. I will not ask You for other than it. He says: Son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for other than it. He says: Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for other than it. So he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it, and his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, excuses him, for he sees what he cannot be patient over, so He brings him near it, and he shades in its shade and drinks of its water. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two, is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade in its shade and drink of its water. I will not ask You for other than it. He says: O son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for other than it. He said: Yes, my Lord, this one - I will not ask You for other than it. He says: Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for other than it. So he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it, and his Lord excuses him, for he sees what he cannot be patient over, so He brings him near it. When He brings him near it, he hears the voices of the people of Paradise, and says: My Lord, admit me into it. He says: O son of Adam, what will make Me stop asking of you. Would it please you that I give you the world and its like with it. He says: My Lord, do You mock me while You are Lord of the worlds. Then Ibn Masud laughed and said: Will you not ask me why I laugh. They said: Why do you laugh. He said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed and said: Will you not ask me why I laugh. They said: Why do you laugh, O Messenger of Allah. He said: At the laughter of my Lord when he said: Do You mock me while You are Lord of the worlds. Then He says: I do not mock you, but I am Able over what I will."
"3900","Affan narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection."
"3901","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: On the day of Badr we were, every three on one camel. Abu Lubabah and Ali ibn Abi Talib were the two alternates of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And it was the turn of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to walk. He said: So they both said: We will walk in your place. So he said: You are not stronger than me, nor am I less in need of reward than you."
"3902","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash said, he informed me, he said: I heard Abu Wail, he said: I heard Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, distributed a distribution, so a man from the people said: This distribution is not intended thereby for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him. He said: So he became angry until I saw anger in his face, then he said: May Allah have mercy on Musa, he was harmed with more than that and he was patient."
"3903","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Zubayd and Mansur and Sulayman informed me, he said, that they heard Abu Wail narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is disbelief. Zubayd said: So I said to Abu Wail twice: Did you hear it from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes."
"3904","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: O Allah, I ask You for piety and guidance and chastity and sufficiency."
"3905","Affan narrated to us, Masud ibn Sad narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed concerning the charity on cows: When the cows reach thirty, therein is a young bull of the cows, a jadha or a jadhah, until they reach forty. Then when they reach forty, therein is an aged cow. Then when the cows become numerous, then in every forty of the cows is an aged cow."
"3906","Affan narrated to us, Abdul-Wahid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud addressed us and said: I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy-odd surahs, while Zayd ibn Thabit was a boy with two locks of hair playing with the boys."
"3907","Affan narrated to us, Shubah informed me, Abdul-Malik ibn Maysarah informed me, he said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: I heard Abdullah saying: I heard a man reciting a verse contrary to what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had taught me, so I took him by the hand until I went with him to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Both of you have done well. Do not differ. To the best of my knowledge, otherwise Misar narrated it to me thereby: For those before you differed concerning it and perished."
"3908","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdul-Malik ibn Maysarah narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah narrating from Abdullah, he said: I heard a man reciting a verse contrary to what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had taught me, so I took him by the hand and brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Both of you have done well. He said: And he became angry until anger was recognized in his face. Shubah said: The greater part of my thought is that he said: Do not differ, for those before you differed concerning it and perished."
"3909","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas saying: Abdullah used to say, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If I were to take a close friend from my nation I would take Abu Bakr."
"3910","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, that a man said to Ibn Masud: How do you know this word, water ghayr yasin or asin? So he said: Have you read all of the Quran? He said: I read all of the Mufassal in one rakah. So he said: Like the droning of poetry, may you have no father. I know the pairs of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he used to join, two pairs at a time, from the beginning of the Mufassal. And the beginning of the Mufassal of Ibn Masud was al-Rahman."
"3911","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Ibn Udnan, he said: I lent Alqamah two thousand dirhams, then when his stipend came out I said to him: Pay me. He said: Delay me till next year. So I came upon him and took it. He said: Then I came to him afterwards. He said: You have wearied me, you have withheld me. So I said: Yes, it is your deed. He said: And what is my affair? I said: You narrated to me from Ibn Masud that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The loan runs the course of half of charity. He said: Yes, so it is thus. He said: So take now."
"3912","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The two eyes commit adultery, and the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery."
"3913","Affan narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one in whose heart is the weight of a grain of arrogance will enter Paradise, and no one in whose heart is the weight of a mustard seed of faith will enter the Fire."
"3914","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that a man of the people of the Suffah died and two dinars were found in his cloak, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two brands."
"3915","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that he said concerning this verse, And he saw him at another descent: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw Jibril at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, upon him six hundred wings, scattering from his feathers gems of pearls and rubies."
"3916","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih and Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed us, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, I covenant to You in this worldly life that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger, for if You entrust me to myself You bring me near to evil and distance me from good, and I trust in nothing but Your mercy, so make for me with You a covenant which You will fulfill to me on the Day of Resurrection, indeed You do not break the promise, except that Allah will say to His angels on the Day of Resurrection: My servant has covenanted to Me a covenant, so fulfill it to him. Then Allah will admit him to Paradise. Suhayl said: So I informed al-Qasim ibn Abdur-Rahman that Awn had informed of such and such. He said: There is no slave girl among our household but she says this in her chamber."
"3917","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Mansur informed me, he said: I heard Khaythamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no staying up at night except for one of two men: one praying or one traveling."
"3918","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard al-Aswad narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite this word, Then is there any that will remember, with dal."
"3919","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a man among us would say in his prayer: Peace upon Allah, peace upon so-and-so, specifying. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us one day: Allah, mighty and majestic, is Peace. So when one of you sits in his prayer let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. Then when you say that you have greeted every servant in the heavens and the earth. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then let him choose afterwards of supplication what he wishes or what he loves."
"3920","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: When we sat in prayer we used to say: Peace upon Allah, peace upon us from our Lord, peace upon Jibril and Mikail, peace upon so-and-so, peace upon so-and-so. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Peace. So when you sit in prayer then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. For when he says that it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven and the earth. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then let him choose of speech what he wishes. Sulayman said: And Ibrahim also narrated it to me, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, with its like."
"3921","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"3922","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abdur-Rahman, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, did not send down a disease except He sent down for it a cure. Whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"3923","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise is nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is like that."
"3924","Muammal narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until I saw the mountain between the two clefts of the moon."
"3925","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my husband, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and of my father Abu Sufyan, and of my brother Muawiyah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have asked Allah for fixed terms and apportioned provisions and fulfilled traces. Nothing thereof is hastened before its time, nor is anything thereof delayed beyond its time. Had you asked Allah to grant you health from torment in the Fire and torment in the grave it would have been better for you. He said: So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are the monkeys and pigs from what was transformed? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah never transformed a people or destroyed a people and then made for them progeny or posterity. And the monkeys and pigs existed before that."
"3926","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq mentioned, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan passed by me, so I seized him and throttled him until I felt the cold of his tongue in my hands. So he said: You have hurt me, you have hurt me."
"3927","Aswad informed us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, that they were with Ibn Masud, then prayer came, so Alqamah and al-Aswad stepped back, so Ibn Masud took them by their hands and set one of them on his right and the other on his left, then they bowed and placed their hands on their knees, and he struck their hands, then he clasped between his hands and intertwined and placed them between his thighs, and said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do it."
"3928","Husayn narrated it to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid and Alqamah ibn Qays, then he mentioned it."
"3929","Aswad ibn Amir informed us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khumayr ibn Malik, he said: It was ordered that the copies of the Quran be altered. He said: Ibn Masud said: Whoever among you is able to conceal his copy, let him conceal it. For whoever conceals a thing will come with it on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then he said: I recited from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy surahs. Shall I abandon what I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him?"
"3930","Aswad said, and Khalaf ibn al-Walid informed us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, from Ibn Masud, he said: Al-Aqib and al-Sayyid, the two chiefs of Najran, came. He said: And they wanted to invoke mutual curse with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So one of them said to his companion: Do not invoke mutual curse with him. For by Allah, if he is a prophet and we curse him, Khalaf said: Then we curse him, neither we nor our posterity will ever prosper. He said: So they came to him and said: We will not invoke mutual curse with you, but we will give you what you ask. So send with us a trustworthy man. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I will send a truly trustworthy man, truly trustworthy. He said: So the companions of Muhammad looked up for it. He said: So he said: Stand, O Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. He said: Then when he turned away he said: This is the trustworthy man of this nation."
"3931","Aswad ibn Amir and Abu Ahmad said, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he slept, Abu Ahmad said: When he went to his bed, he placed his right hand under his cheek, Abu Ahmad said: The right, then he said: O Allah, protect me from Your torment on the Day You gather Your servants."
"3932","Waki narrated it to us with its meaning."
"3933","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Malik, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to give greeting in his prayer to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheeks could be seen."
"3934","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, and he is the truthful, the believed: The creation of one of you is gathered in the belly of his mother for forty nights, then he is a clot like that, then he is a lump like that, then Allah, mighty and majestic, sends to him an angel from the angels, so he says: Write his deed and his term and his provision, and write him wretched or happy. Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abdullah, a man does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is between him and Paradise but a cubit, then wretchedness overtakes him, so he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and dies and enters the Fire. Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abdullah, a man does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is between him and the Fire but a cubit, then happiness overtakes him, so he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and dies and enters Paradise."
"3935","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sayf narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid saying: Abdullah ibn Sakhbarah Abu Mamar narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Masud saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me the tashahhud, my hand between his hands, as he taught me a surah of the Quran. He said: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And he was among us. Then when he passed away we said: Peace upon the Prophet."
"3936","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abu Umays narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn al-Aqmar mentioning from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that he said: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where they are called. For Allah has legislated for your Prophet the practices of guidance, and they are of the practices of guidance. Had you prayed in your houses as this laggard prays in his house, you would have abandoned the practice of your Prophet. And had you abandoned the practice of your Prophet, you would have gone astray. And there is no man who purifies himself and perfects purification, then proceeds to a mosque among these mosques, except Allah writes for him with every step he takes a good deed, and raises him thereby a degree, and removes from him thereby a sin. You have seen us, and none stayed behind from it except a hypocrite of known hypocrisy. And a man would be brought, supported between two men, until he was stood in the row."
"3937","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed a night with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he remained standing until I thought of an evil matter. We said: And what did you think? He said: I thought to sit and leave the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Sulayman said: And Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us its like."
"3938","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abdur-Rahman al-Jumahi, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Awdi, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Forbidden to the Fire is every gentle, lenient, easy one, close to the people."
"3939","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zuhayr informed us, from Abu al-Harith Yahya al-Taymi, from Abu Majid al-Hanafi, from Abdullah, he said: We asked our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about walking with the funeral. So he said: Walking is slower than trotting. If it is good, it is hastened, or it is hastened to it. And if it is other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral is followed and does not follow. Not from us is one who goes ahead of it."
"3940","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Awn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, he said: Abdullah said: When you are told a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then think of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the manner that is most fitting of him and most guided and most pious."
"3941","Rawh and Muhammad ibn Jafar said, Shubah narrated to us, Rawh said: al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, that he performed Hajj with Abdullah, so he stoned the major jamrah with seven pebbles, and placed the House on his left and Mina on his right, and said: This is the station of the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"3942","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah ibn Masud went into the valley and faced the jamarat directly and placed the mountain behind his back, then he stoned and said: This is the station of the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"3943","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: A black slave joined the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he died, so he was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Look, did he leave anything? They said: He left two dinars. He said: Two brands."
"3944","Asbat and Ibn Fudayl, with the meaning, said, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu al-Radrad, from Ibn Masud, he said: I used to greet the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in prayer and he would return it to me. Then I greeted him one day and he did not return anything to me, so I found it in myself. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to greet you while you were in prayer and you returned it to me, and I greeted you and you did not return anything to me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah introduces into His command what He wills."
"3945","Abdul-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Masruq, that a woman came to Ibn Masud and said: I have been told that you forbid hair extensions. He said: Yes. So she said: Is it something you find in the Book of Allah or heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So he said: I find it in the Book of Allah and from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So she said: By Allah, I have perused what is between the two covers of the Mushaf and I did not find therein what you say. He said: Did you find therein, Whatever the Messenger gives you take it, and whatever he forbids you refrain from? She said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid the woman who plucks eyebrows and the woman who widens gaps between teeth and the woman who joins hair and the woman who tattoos, except due to disease. The woman said: Perhaps it is in some of your wives. He said to her: Enter. So she entered, then she came out and said: I saw no harm. He said: Then you have not memorized the advice of the righteous servant: And I do not wish to go against you to what I forbid you from."
"3946","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him."
"3947","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man in whose heart is the weight of an atom of arrogance will enter Paradise, and no man in whose heart is the weight of an atom of faith will enter the Fire."
"3948","Aswad informed us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believer is not a curser, nor a slanderer, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."
"3949","Rawh and Affan said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Affan said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Our Lord, mighty and majestic, marvels at two men: A man who jumps from his bed and blanket from among his family and tribe to his prayer, so our Lord says: O My angels, look at My servant. He has jumped from his bed and blanket and from among his tribe and family to his prayer, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me. And a man who fights in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, then they flee, so he knows what is upon him of fleeing and what is for him in returning, so he returns until his blood is shed, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me. So Allah, mighty and majestic, says to His angels: Look at My servant. He returned desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me until his blood was shed."
"3950","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I ask You for guidance and piety and chastity and sufficiency."
"3951","Rawh and Affan, with the meaning, said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, Affan said: From his father Ibn Masud, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to admit a man into Paradise. So he entered the synagogue, and there were Jews, and a Jew was reading to them the Torah. Then when they came upon the description of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they stopped. And in its corner was a sick man. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is with you that you stopped? The sick man said: They came upon the description of a prophet and stopped. Then the sick man came crawling until he took the Torah and read until he came upon the description of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his nation. So he said: This is your description and the description of your nation. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. Then he died. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Attend to your brother."
"3952","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Beware of saying: So-and-so died a martyr, or so-and-so was killed a martyr. For a man fights to gain booty, and fights to be remembered, and fights to show his place. If you are witnesses, inevitably, then bear witness for the group whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent in an expedition and they were killed. So they said: O Allah, convey to our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from us that we have met You, and we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us."
"3953","Rawh and Muhammad ibn Jafar said, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrating, Ibn Jafar said: Or Ibrahim, Shubah doubted, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, two rakahs, and with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, two rakahs. Would that my share of four rakahs were two accepted ones."
"3954","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Last night I recited to the jinn, companions, at al-Hajun."
"3955","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Hammad said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham, from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, he said: I went with an old woman of Banu Asad to Ibn Masud, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursing the women who pluck eyebrows and the women who widen gaps between teeth and the tattooing women who change the creation of Allah. Yahya said: And the women who are tattooed."
"3956","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abdul-Malik, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham, from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, he said: I went with an old woman to Ibn Masud, then he mentioned a story. So Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursing the women who pluck eyebrows and the women who widen gaps between teeth and the tattooing women who change the creation of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3957","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abdul-Malik, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fighting a Muslim brother is disbelief, and reviling him is wickedness."
"3958","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, he said: Ibrahim narrated to me, from Nuhayk ibn Sinan al-Sulami, that he came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: I read the Mufassal tonight in one rakah. So he said: Like the droning of poetry, or scattering like the scattering of cheap dates. It was only separated to be separated. I know the pairs which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to join, twenty surahs: al-Rahman and al-Najm, according to the arrangement of Ibn Masud, every two surahs in one rakah. And he mentioned al-Dukhan and Amma yatasaalun in one rakah."
"3959","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, Shubah informed us, from al-Amash, he heard Abu Wail narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: For every treacherous one is a banner, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"3960","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: How evil it is for one of you, or how evil it is for one of them, to say: I forgot verse such-and-such. Rather he was made to forget. Review the Quran. For by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it escapes more readily from the breasts of men than camels from their halters."
"3961","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abdur-Rahman informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Sakhbarah, he said: I went in the morning with Abdullah ibn Masud from Mina to Arafat, and he was reciting talbiyah. He said: And Abdullah was a dark man with two braids, upon him the appearance of the people of the desert. So a crowd of the rabble gathered against him. They said: O Bedouin, this is not a day of talbiyah, it is only a day of takbir. He said: Thereupon he turned to me and said: Are the people ignorant or did they forget? By Him Who sent Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the truth, I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not leave talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, except mixing it with takbir or tahlil."
"3962","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicate against Quraysh except one day. He was praying, and a group of Quraysh were sitting, and the afterbirth of a camel was near him. So they said: Who will take this afterbirth and throw it upon his back? He said: So Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt said: I will. So he took it and threw it upon his back. He remained prostrate until Fatimah, may the blessings of Allah be upon her, came and took it from his back. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, upon the chiefs of Quraysh. O Allah, upon Utbah ibn Rabiah. O Allah, upon Shaybah ibn Rabiah. O Allah, upon Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. O Allah, upon Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt. O Allah, upon Ubayy ibn Khalaf, or Umayyah ibn Khalaf. He said: Abdullah said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr, all of them, then dragged to the well, except Ubayy or Umayyah, for he was a bulky man and broke apart."
"3963","Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The best of people are my generation, those who follow me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. He said: And I do not know whether he said in the third or in the fourth: Then there will succeed after them successors, the testimony of one of them will precede his oath, and his oath his testimony."
"3964","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that the nations were shown to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So his nation was shown to him, and their multitude pleased him. So it was said: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning."
"3965","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, he said: On the day of Badr they were, between every three men a camel. And the two alternates of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were Ali and Abu Lubabah. He said: And when it was the turn of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they said to him: Ride until we walk in your place. So he says: You are not stronger than me, and I am not less in need of reward than you."
"3966","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: It is not Abu Ubaydah who mentioned it, but Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, that he heard Abdullah ibn Masud saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to relieve himself and ordered me to bring him three stones. So I found two stones and did not find the third, so I took a piece of dung and brought them to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he took the two stones and threw the dung and said: This is filth."
"3967","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and he mentioned the tashahhud, the tashahhud of Abdullah. He said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Mansur and al-Amash and Hammad, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, its like."
"3968","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid and Alqamah, from Abdullah, that a man came to him and said: I read the Mufassal in one rakah. So he said: Rather you droned like the droning of poetry, or like the scattering of cheap dates. But the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not do as you did. He used to recite the pairs, al-Rahman and al-Najm, in one rakah. He said: So Abu Ishaq mentioned ten rakahs with twenty surahs, according to the arrangement of Abdullah, the last of them Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat and al-Dukhan."
"3969","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I was with Abdullah ibn Masud at Jam, so he prayed the two prayers, each prayer alone with adhan and iqamah, and dinner between them. And he prayed Fajr when dawn shone, or he said: When one saying: Dawn has risen, and one saying: It has not risen. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: These two prayers are shifted from their time in this place. The people do not come to Jam until it is dark, and the Fajr prayer at this hour."
"3970","Yahya ibn Adam and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr said, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me: Indeed I am the Provider, Possessor of power, the Firm."
"3971","Yahya narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic, The heart did not lie in what it saw. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw Jibril in a robe of Rafraf that filled what is between the heaven and the earth."
"3972","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Ahmad said, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father and Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah used to say takbir in every bowing and prostration and rising and lowering, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and they gave greeting on their right and their left: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"3973","Yahya ibn Adam and Husayn ibn Muhammad said, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which deeds are best? So he said: Prayer at its time, and kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah. And had I asked for more he would have given me more. Husayn said: I asked him for more."
"3974","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he dictated to me from his book, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, Alqamah narrated to us, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught us prayer. So he said takbir and raised his hands, then he bowed and clasped between his hands and placed them between his knees. It reached Sad, so he said: My brother told the truth. We used to do that, then we were ordered with this. And he took hold of his knees. Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to me thus."
"3975","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer, I do not know whether he added or omitted, then he gave greeting and prostrated two prostrations."
"3976","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Kathir ibn Mudrik, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he recited talbiyah on the night of Jam, then he said: Here I saw the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed reciting talbiyah."
"3977","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Jabir al-Taymi, from Abu al-Majid, he said: A man came to Abdullah, then he mentioned the story, and he began narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The first man whose hand was cut in Islam, or among the Muslims, was a man brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this one stole. So it was as if the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was strewn with ashes. So some of them said: O Messenger of Allah, that is saying: What is with you? So he said: And what prevents me, while you are helpers of Satan against your companion? And Allah, mighty and majestic, is Pardoning, He loves pardon. And it is not fitting for one in charge of an affair to be brought a prescribed punishment except he carries it out. Then he recited: Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Yahya said: Sufyan dictated it to us by dictation."
"3978","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Abu al-Majid al-Hanafi, from Abdullah, he said: We asked our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about walking with the funeral. So he said: Walking is slower than trotting. If it is good, it is hastened to it. And if it is other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral is followed, and not from us is one who goes ahead of it."
"3979","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Aqmar narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: You have seen us, and prayer was not established until the rows were completed with us. So whoever is pleased to meet Allah, mighty and majestic, tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where they are called. For they are of the practices of guidance, and Allah, mighty and majestic, has legislated for your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the practices of guidance."
"3980","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Madi Karib, he said: We came to Abdullah and asked him to recite to us Ta-Sin, the two hundred. So he said: It is not with me. But upon you is one who took it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Khabbab ibn al-Aratt. He said: So we came to Khabbab ibn al-Aratt and he recited it to us."
"3981","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me a surah from the thirty of Al Hamim, meaning al-Ahqaf. He said: And the surah, when it was more than thirty verses, was called the thirty. He said: So I went to the mosque, and there was a man reciting it contrary to what he had taught me. So I said: Who taught you? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I said to another: Recite it. So he recited it contrary to my recitation and the recitation of my companion. So I went with them to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, these two contradict me in recitation. He said: So he became angry and his face changed color, and said: Those before you perished only through disagreement. He said: Zirr said: And with him was a man. He said: So the man said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, orders you that each man among you recite as he was taught, for those before you perished only through disagreement. Abdullah said: So I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told him something secretly, or he knew what was in the soul of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And the man is Ali ibn Abi Talib, may the blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3982","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Bashir Abu Ismail informed us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Tariq, from Abdullah, he said to him: O Abu Abdur-Rahman, the greeting of the man upon you, so I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. He said: So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour, greeting will be for intimates, and trade will spread until the woman helps her husband in trade, and kinship ties will be cut."
"3983","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Nahshali narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed five, Zuhr or Asr. Then when he finished it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has more been added in prayer? He said: No. They said: You prayed five. He said: So he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he said: I am only a human. I remember as you remember, and I forget as you forget."
"3984","Asbat narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever kills a snake, for him are seven good deeds. And whoever kills a gecko, for him is one good deed. And whoever leaves a snake fearing its consequence is not from us."
"3985","Asbat narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from Kurdus, from Ibn Masud, he said: The chiefs of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with him were Khabbab and Suhayb and Bilal and Ammar. So they said: O Muhammad, are you pleased with these? So there was revealed concerning them of the Quran: And warn with it those who fear they will be gathered to their Lord, up to His saying: And Allah knows best the wrongdoers."
"3986","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Abdullah, he said: We used to go out on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we had no women. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate ourselves? So he forbade us from it. Then afterwards it was permitted for us to marry the woman for a garment for a term. Then Abdullah recited: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed Allah does not love the transgressors."
"3987","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: We talked one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until we wearied of talk. Then we returned to our families. Then when morning came we went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: The prophets were shown to me with their nations and their followers from their nations. So a prophet would pass with three of his nation with him, and a prophet with a group of his nation with him, and a prophet with a company of his nation with him, and a prophet with a man of his nation with him, and a prophet with no one with him, until Musa ibn Imran, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me in a great throng of Banu Israil. Then when I saw them they pleased me. I said: O Lord, who are these? So He said: This is your brother Musa ibn Imran and those with him of Banu Israil. I said: O Lord, then where is my nation? He said: Look to your right. Then the hills, the hills of Makkah, were blocked with the faces of men. I said: Who are these, O Lord? He said: Your nation. I said: I am pleased, O Lord. He said: Are you pleased? I said: Yes. He said: Look to your left. He said: So I looked, and the horizon was blocked with the faces of men. So He said: Are you pleased? I said: I am pleased. It was said: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them. So Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, one of Banu Asad ibn Khuzaymah, arose and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. So he said: O Allah, make him among them. Then another man arose and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkashah preceded you with it."
"3988","Abdul-Wahhab informed us, Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: We talked one night, then he mentioned its meaning. And he narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that Ibn Masud said: We talked in the presence of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, then he mentioned it."
"3989","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Said informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: We talked in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night until we wearied of talk, then he mentioned it."
"3990","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the killing of a snake at Mina."
"3991","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa said, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, that he was picking a siwak from the arak tree, and he was thin in the shanks, so the wind made him topple, so the people laughed at him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do you laugh at? They said: O Prophet of Allah, at the thinness of his shanks. So he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Balance than Uhud."
"3992","Abd al-Samad and Affan, with the meaning, said, Hammad narrated to us, Affan said: Asim informed us, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me Surah al-Ahqaf, and he taught it to another man, so he differed from me in a verse. So I said to him: Who taught you it? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I came to him while he was among a group. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. He said: I said: This one claims that you taught it to him thus and thus. So the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed. So the man who was with him said: Let each man among you recite as he heard. For those before you perished only through disagreement. He said: By Allah, I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him with that, or he said it himself."
"3993","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with its meaning. And he said: So he became angry and his face changed color, and said: Those before you perished only through disagreement."
"3994","Abd al-Samad and Affan said, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that a man of the people of the Suffah died, so they found in his cloak two dinars. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two brands."
"3995","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the women. So he said to them: There is no woman among you whose three die but Allah, mighty and majestic, will admit her to Paradise. So the eldest woman among them said: O Messenger of Allah, and the one with two in Paradise? He said: And the one with two in Paradise."
"3996","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, he said: While Ibn Masud was preaching one day, a snake passed walking on the wall, so he cut his sermon, then he struck it with his staff until he killed it. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a polytheist man whose blood had become lawful."
"3997","Abd al-Samad and Rawh said, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from Ibn Masud, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the monkeys and pigs: Are they from the progeny of the Jews? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, never cursed a people at all, Rawh said: Then transformed them so they have progeny until He destroys them. But this is a creation that existed. Then when Allah, mighty and majestic, became angry at the Jews, He transformed them and made them like them."
"3998","Abd al-Samad said, Abdul-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic? He said: Pray the prayer at its times. I said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Then striving in the path of Allah. And had I asked him for more he would have given me more."
"3999","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I memorize the pairs which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to join between them: eighteen surahs of the Mufassal and two surahs of Al Hamim."
"4000","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: We talked in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night until we wearied of talk, then he mentioned it."
"4001","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, who said: We were sitting on Friday evening in the mosque. A man from the Ansar said: If one of us sees a man with his wife and kills him, you would kill him, and if he speaks you would flog him, and if he stays silent he stays silent in anger. By Allah, if I reach morning safe I shall ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of us sees a man with his wife and kills him, you would kill him, and if he speaks you would flog him, and if he stays silent he stays silent in anger. O Allah, judge. Then the verse of lian was revealed, and that man was the first to be tried with it."
"4002","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, who said: I saw Abdullah stone the jamrah from the bottom of the valley, then say: Here, by the One besides whom there is no god, stood the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"4003","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid from Ibn Masud, who said: I prayed two rakahs with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and two rakahs with Abu Bakr, and two rakahs with Umar."
"4004","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and Wal-mursalati urfa was revealed. We were receiving it from his mouth when a snake came out of its hole. We rushed toward it but it outran us and entered its hole. He said: It was protected from your harm, and you were protected from its harm."
"4005","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, the same, who said: And we were receiving it from his mouth fresh and moist."
"4006","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah narrated to me, saying: Alqamah took my hand and narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Masud took his hand, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Abdullah and taught him the tashahhud in prayer. He said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. Zuhayr said: I memorized from him, Allah willing: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: When you finish this, or he said: When you do this, your prayer is complete. If you wish to stand then stand, and if you wish to sit then sit."
"4007","Abu Dawud, meaning al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said about people who stay behind from Friday prayer: I have strongly intended to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn down the houses of men who stay behind from Friday prayer."
"4008","Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has killed Abu Jahl. He said: Praise be to Allah who aided His servant and honored His religion."
"4009","Ishaq ibn Isa and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Zir ibn Hubaysh from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: At the expedition of Badr, every three of us shared one camel. Ali and Abu Lubabah were the riding partners of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the turn of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to walk came, they said: Ride, O Messenger of Allah, while we walk for you. He said: You are no stronger in walking than I am, and I am no less in need of reward than you."
"4010","Affan narrated it to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, and he mentioned it with its meaning and its chain."
"4011","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us from al-Zubayr ibn Adi from Talhah from Murrah from Abdullah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he was brought to Sidrat al-Muntaha, which is in the sixth heaven. To it ends whatever is raised from the earth, and once he said whatever is taken up from the earth, and it is seized from there, and to it ends whatever is sent down from above it, and it is seized from there, when there covered the lote tree what covered it. He said: Moths of gold. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given three things: the five prayers, the closing verses of Surah al-Baqarah, and forgiveness for whoever of his nation does not associate anything with Allah of the grave major sins."
"4012","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us from Furat, who said: I read to Abdulkarim from Ziyad ibn al-Jarrah from Abdullah ibn Maqil, who said: My father was with Abdullah ibn Masud and heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance."
"4013","Kathir narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and were kept from the noon, afternoon, sunset, and night prayers. That weighed heavily on me, then I said: We are with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the path of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called the iqamah, and he led us in the noon prayer. Then he called the iqamah and led us in the afternoon prayer. Then he called the iqamah and led us in the sunset prayer. Then he called the iqamah and led us in the night prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around us and said: There is no group on earth remembering Allah except you."
"4014","Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us: Khusayf narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam from Abdullah ibn Maqil, who said: My father was with Ibn Masud and heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance."
"4015","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Abu Husayn from Yahya ibn Waththab from Masruq, who said: Abdullah narrated to us one day and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Then he trembled until his clothes shook, then he said: Something like this, or similar to this."
"4016","Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us: Khusayf narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam from Abdullah ibn Maqil, who said: My father was with Ibn Masud and heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance."
"4017","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-Amash and Mansur and Husayn ibn Abdirrahman, and Abu Hashim and Hammad from Abu Wail, and from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, who said: We did not know what to say in prayer. We used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mikail. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us and said: Allah is Peace. When you sit in two rakahs, say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. Abu Wail said in his hadith from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven and on earth. And Abu Ishaq said in the hadith of Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you say it, it reaches every favored angel, or sent prophet, or righteous servant. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"4018","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani from al-Hasan ibn Sad from Abdurrahman ibn Abdullah from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and passed by a village of ants that had been burned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No human being should punish with the punishment of Allah."
"4019","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Mansur and al-Amash from Dharr from Wail ibn Mahanah from Ibn Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Give charity, O assembly of women, for you are most of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. A woman who was not among the prominent women stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, why are we most of the people of Hell. He said: Because you curse much and are ungrateful to your husbands."
"4020","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Abu Wail from Ibn Masud, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Keep refreshing the Quran, for it escapes more swiftly from the chests of men than camels escape from their hobbles. Evil is it for one of them to say: I forgot verse such-and-such. Rather, he was made to forget."
"4021","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Ibn Masud, who said: A group came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a companion of ours is ill. Shall we cauterize him. He stayed silent for a while, then said: If you wish, cauterize him, and if you wish, treat him with heated stones."
"4022","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Ibn Masud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A servant keeps lying until he is recorded a liar, or he keeps telling the truth until he is recorded truthful."
"4023","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah said: We were young men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owning nothing. He said: O assembly of young men, whoever of you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity. Whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for fasting is a shield for him."
"4024","Yala and Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, who said: al-Ashath ibn Qays came to Abdullah on the day of Ashura while he was eating lunch. He said: O Abu Muhammad, come to lunch. He said: Is today not Ashura. He said: Do you know what the day of Ashura is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, it was left."
"4025","Yala narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Alqamah, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah, and Zayd ibn Hudayr was with us. Khabbab came to us and said: O Abu Abdirrahman, do all of these recite as you recite. He said: If you wish, I can order one of them to recite for you. He said: Yes. He said to me: Recite. Ibn Hudayr said: You order him to recite, yet he is not the best reciter among us. He said: By Allah, if you wish I shall tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about your people and his people. He said: So I recited fifty verses from Maryam. Khabbab said: Well done. Abdullah said: I recite nothing except what he recited. Then Abdullah said to Khabbab: Is it not time for this ring to be thrown away. He said: You will never see it on me after today. The ring was gold."
"4026","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from al-Rukayn from his father from Abdullah, raising it for us the first time, then withholding it, meaning Sharik, who said: Interest, even if abundant, its end is in paucity."
"4027","Abu Kamil and Yazid narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us from al-Hasan ibn Sad from Abdah al-Nahdi from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not prohibited a sanctity but He knew that some violator among you would violate it. I am holding your waistbands lest you plunge into the Fire like the plunging of moths and flies. Yazid said: Moths or flies."
"4028","Rawh narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Mughirah informed us from al-Hasan ibn Sad from Abdah al-Nahdi from Abdullah ibn Masud, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: Moths and flies."
"4029","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Zir ibn Hubaysh from Ibn Masud that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had as his riding partners on the day of Badr Ali and Abu Lubabah. When the turn of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, they said: Ride, O Messenger of Allah, while we walk for you. He said: You are no stronger than I am, nor am I less in need of reward than you."
"4030","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: Alqamah and al-Aswad asked permission to see Abdullah, who said: Rulers will come over you who become occupied and miss the prayer time, so pray it at its time. Then he stood and prayed between me and him, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4031","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, who said: When this verse was revealed, Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrong, they said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us does not wrong himself. He said: That is not it. It is shirk. Have you not heard what Luqman said to his son: Do not associate partners with Allah. Associating partners with Allah is a great wrong."
"4032","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and he either added or omitted. Ibrahim said: Or the forgetfulness of that came from me. We said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in prayer. He said: What is that. We said: You prayed before such-and-such. He said: I am only human. I forget as you forget. When one of you forgets, let him prostrate two prostrations. Then he turned and prostrated two prostrations."
"4033","Ibn Numayr and Yala narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Alqamah, who said: Abdullah went to Sham, and some people of Hims said to him: Recite for us. So he recited Surah Yusuf to them. A man among the people said: By Allah, it was not revealed thus. Abdullah said: Woe to you. By Allah, I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thus, and he said: Well done. While he was disputing with him, he noticed the smell of wine from him. He said: You drink filth and deny the Quran. By Allah, you shall not leave me until I flog you. So he flogged him the prescribed punishment."
"4034","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash informed us from Ibrahim from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah said when he saw Uthman pray four rakahs at Mina: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs, and behind Abu Bakr two rakahs, and Umar two rakahs. Would that my share of four were two accepted ones."
"4035","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash informed us from Umarah ibn Umayr from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, who said: He said: We came to Abdullah, and Alqamah and al-Aswad were with him. He narrated a hadith which I think he narrated only for my sake, for I was the youngest of the people. He said: We were young men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finding nothing. He said: O assembly of young men, whoever of you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity. Whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a shield for him."
"4036","Yala narrated to us: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us from al-Ayzar, from Tinah, that Ibn Masud said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a curse is directed, it goes toward the one to whom it was directed. If it finds in him a path and finds a way, it settles upon him. Otherwise it comes to its Lord and says: O Lord, so-and-so directed me to so-and-so, and I found no way against him and found no path in him. What do you command me. He says: Return whence you came."
"4037","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Dharr from Wail ibn Mahanah from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of women, give charity even from your jewelry, for you are most of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. A woman who was not among the prominent women stood and said: Why are we most of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. He said: You curse much and are ungrateful to your husbands."
"4038","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise. He said: And I said: Whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters the Fire."
"4039","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding their companion, for that grieves him."
"4040","Source text truncated to only the words Narrated to us, with no matn or chain preserved."
"4041","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq, who said: We were sitting at the door of Abdullah waiting for him to permit us. Yazid ibn Muawiyah al-Nakhai came and entered to see him. We said to him: Inform him of our presence. He entered and informed him. It was not long before he came out to us and said: I know your place, but I deliberately leave you, fearing to bore you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose times for admonition for us in the days, fearing weariness for us."
"4042","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your predecessor at the Pond. Some people will be contested with me over it, then I shall be overpowered in their regard. I shall say: O Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"4043","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one phrase, and I said another. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters the Fire. And I said: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise."
"4044","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is more jealous than Allah, and for that He prohibited indecencies. And no one loves praise more than Allah."
"4045","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad, who said: I and Alqamah came to Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms over his thighs. It is as if I am looking at the interlacing of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer."
"4046","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray any prayer except at its appointed time, except two prayers: the sunset and night prayers at Muzdalifah, and he prayed the dawn prayer that day before its appointed time. Ibn Numayr said: The two night prayers, for he prayed them together at Muzdalifah."
"4047","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah, who said: I was hidden under the curtains of the Kabah. Three men came whose bellies had much fat but whose hearts had little understanding: a Qurashi man and his two Thaqafi in-laws, or a Thaqafi man and his two Qurashi in-laws. They spoke words I did not understand. One of them said: Do you think Allah hears these words of ours. The other two said: If we raise our voices He hears it, and if we do not raise our voices He does not hear it. The other said: If He hears anything of it, He hears all of it. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah revealed: You did not hide yourselves lest your hearing and your sight testify against you, up to His saying: And that thought of yours which you thought about your Lord ruined you, and you became among the losers."
"4048","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shimr ibn Atiyyah from Mughirah ibn Sad ibn al-Akhram from his father from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take estates, lest you desire the world. He said: Then Abdullah said: And Baradhan, what is Baradhan, and Medina, what is Medina."
"4049","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man meets Allah while He is angry with him. Al-Ashath said: By Allah, that was about me. There was land between me and a Jewish man, and he denied me my right. I brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to me: Do you have proof. I said: No. He said to the Jew: Swear. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear and my property will go. So Allah revealed: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"4050","Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us from Muslim ibn Subayh from Masruq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the most severely punished people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers. Waki said: The severest of people."
"4051","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us from Hammad from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep lying on his back until he snored, then stand and pray without performing ablution."
"4052","Ismail ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us from Fudayl from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"4053","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Layth narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for his need and said: Bring me something with which to clean myself, and do not bring me a bone or dung. Then I brought him water, and he performed ablution, then stood and prayed. Then he inclined, then joined his hands when bowing and placed them between his thighs."
"4054","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man, asking his permission to cauterize him. He stayed silent. Then we asked him another time and he stayed silent. Then we asked him a third time and said: Treat him with heated stones if you wish, as if angry."
"4055","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from Alqamah and al-Aswad from Abdullah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say the takbir at every rising and lowering, standing and sitting, and greet to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the side of his cheek was visible. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar do that."
"4056","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, saying: It was not Abu Ubaydah who mentioned it, but Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the privy and said: Bring me three stones. I searched and found two stones but did not find the third. So I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, saying: It is filth."
"4057","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us from Abu Wail from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the spoils of Hunayn at Jiranah. They crowded him. He said: A servant among the servants of Allah was sent by Allah to his people, but they denied him and wounded him. He kept wiping the blood from his forehead, saying: Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know. Abdullah said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his forehead, recounting the man."
"4058","Ibn Abi Adi and Yazid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Awn informed us from Amr ibn Said from Humayd ibn Abdirrahman, who said: Ibn Masud said: I was never kept away from three things. Ibn Awn said: Amr forgot one, and I forgot another, and this one remained: about private conversation, about such-and-such and about such-and-such. He said: So I came to him, and Malik ibn Murarah ar-Rahawi was with him. I caught the end of his hadith while he was saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man to whom beauty has been allotted as you see. I dislike that anyone among people surpasses me even by two sandal straps or more. Is that not arrogance. He said: That is not arrogance. Arrogance is rejecting the truth and despising people."
"4059","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wail from Abdullah, who said: A man who slept the night until morning was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is a man in whose ear Satan urinated, or in whose two ears."
"4060","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wail, who said: Abdullah used to remind us every Thursday. It was said to him: We wish you would remind us every day. He said: I dislike boring you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose times for admonition for us, fearing weariness for us."
"4061","Jarir narrated to us from Layth from Muhammad ibn Abdirrahman ibn Yazid from his father, who said: I was with Abdullah until he reached the Jamrah of Aqabah. He said: Hand me stones. I handed him seven stones. He said to me: Hold the halter of the camel. Then he returned to it and threw it from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles while riding, saying the takbir with each pebble. He said: O Allah, make it an accepted pilgrimage and a forgiven sin. Then he said: Here stood the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"4062","Hushaym narrated to us: Sayyar informed us from Abu Wail, who said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: I recited al-Mufassal last night in one rakah. Abdullah said: Like scattering unripe dates, and racing like poetry. I know the pairs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join together, two surahs in one rakah."
"4063","Hajjaj narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Ibn Masud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and Wal-mursalati urfa was revealed to him. We began receiving it from him when a snake came out from the side of the cave. He said: Kill it. We rushed toward it but it outran us. He said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm."
"4064","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: When we sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, we used to say: Peace be upon Allah before His servants, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mikail, peace be upon so-and-so, peace be upon so-and-so. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard us and said: Allah is Peace. When one of you sits in prayer, let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. When he says it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven and on earth. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he may choose after that whatever supplication he wishes."
"4065","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Masruq from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a person who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and one who leaves his religion and separates from the community."
"4066","Muammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be trials and matters which you will disapprove. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us. He said: You fulfill the duty that is upon you, and you ask Allah for what belongs to you."
"4067","Muammal said: I found in another place: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Wail from Amr ibn Shurahbil from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"4068","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from al-Amash and Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the cave when a snake came out upon us. We rushed toward it but it outran us and entered the hole. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm. He said: And al-Amash added in the hadith: He said: We used to receive it from his mouth while it was fresh."
"4069","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and Wal-mursalati urfa had been revealed to him. He said: We were taking it from his mouth fresh when a snake came out upon us. He said: Kill it. We rushed toward it to kill it but it outran us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah protected it from your harm just as He protected you from its harm."
"4070","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Mukhariq al-Ahmasi from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I heard Ibn Masud say: I witnessed from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, others said, a scene which, if I were its owner, would be dearer to me than anything equated with it. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was supplicating against the polytheists and said: We shall not say to you as the people of Musa said: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are sitting here. Rather, we shall fight on your right and on your left, before you and behind you. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brighten, and that pleased him."
"4071","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us from as-Suddi that he heard Murrah that he heard Abdullah, Shubah said to me, raising it, but I do not raise it to you, saying about His saying: And whoever intends therein deviation with wrong: If a man merely intends deviation therein, even while in Adan Abyan, Allah will make him taste a painful punishment."
"4072","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Jabir narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from al-Aswad from Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon or afternoon prayer as five, then prostrated two prostrations and said: These two prostrations are for whoever among you thought he added or omitted."
"4073","Hushaym narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Abu Qays from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil that al-Ashari was asked about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister. He gave the daughter half and the sister what remained, giving the son's daughter nothing. They went to Ibn Masud and informed him. He said: I would be astray then and not among the guided if I took his word and left the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Ibn Masud said: The daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets a sixth, and what remains goes to the sister."
"4074","Abdulquddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us from Misar from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah, who said: The sitting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two rakahs was as if upon hot stones."
"4075","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Khusayf from Abu Ubaydah from his father Abdullah ibn Masud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you are in prayer and doubt whether it is three or four, and your stronger thought is four, then recite the tashahhud, then prostrate two prostrations while sitting before you greet, then recite the tashahhud again, then greet."
"4076","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Khusayf narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: When you doubt in your prayer while sitting, not knowing whether you prayed three or four, if your stronger thought is that you prayed three, then stand and bow one rakah, then greet, then prostrate two prostrations, then recite the tashahhud, then greet. If your stronger thought is that you prayed four, then greet, then prostrate two prostrations, then recite the tashahhud, then greet."
"4077","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam informed us: Abu Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends forth three who did not reach puberty, they will be for him a strong fortress from the Fire. Abu Darda said: I sent forth two. He said: And two. Ubayy ibn Kab, Abu al-Mundhir, master of the reciters, said: I sent forth one. He said: And one, but that is at the first shock."
"4078","Hushaym narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam informed us from Abu Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Abu Dharr said: Only two preceded me. And Yazid also narrated it to us thus, saying: Abu Dharr said: Two of mine have gone."
"4079","Muhammad and Yazid narrated to us, saying: al-Awwam narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to me from Abu Ubaydah. They differed with Hushaym, saying: Abu Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"4080","Hushaym narrated to us: Khalid informed us from Ibn Sirin that Anas ibn Malik attended the funeral of a man from the Ansar. He said: They made the seeking of forgiveness open, and Anas did not object to that. Hushaym said: Khalid said in his hadith: And they brought him in from the foot of the grave. And Hushaym said once: A man from the Ansar died in Basra, and Anas ibn Malik attended his funeral, and they made the seeking of forgiveness open for him."
"4081","Abdulala narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us from Muhammad, who said: I was with Anas at a funeral, and he ordered the deceased to be slipped in from the side of his feet."
"4082","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: Anas was the best of people in prayer while traveling and while staying."
"4083","Hushaym narrated to us: Khalid informed us from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: I saw Anas ibn Malik crane toward something while in prayer, looking at it."
"4084","Yahya narrated to us from al-Amash: Umarah narrated to me: al-Aswad ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: And Abu Muawiyah: al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah, and Ibn Jafar: Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman, who said: I heard Umarah from al-Aswad from Abdullah, with the meaning, who said: None of you should give Satan a share of himself, thinking he must leave only to his right. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and most of his departures were to his left."
"4085","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan, and Shubah from Mansur from Abu Wail from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Evil is it for one of you to say: I forgot verse such-and-such. Rather, he was made to forget."
"4086","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Mansur and Sulayman narrated to us from Abu Wail from Abdullah, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we be taken for what we did in the pre-Islamic age. He said: If you do good, you shall not be taken. If you do evil in Islam, you shall be taken for the first and the last."
"4087","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan: Mansur and Sulayman narrated to me from Ibrahim from Abidah from Abdullah that a Jewish man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Allah holds the heavens on a finger, the earths on a finger, the mountains on a finger, the creatures on a finger, and the trees on a finger, then says: I am the King. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars were visible and said: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem. Yahya said: And Fudayl, meaning Ibn Iyad, said: In wonder and affirmation of him."
"4088","Yahya and Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from his father from Abu ad-Duha from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has allies among the prophets, and my ally among them is my father and the close friend of my Lord. Then he recited: The closest of people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, and this Prophet and those who believe."
"4089","Yahya narrated to us from al-Masudi: Jami ibn Shaddad narrated to me, saying: I heard Abdurrahman ibn Yazid say: I saw Abdullah go deep into the valley, place the jamrah at his right eyebrow, and face the House. Then he threw it with seven pebbles, saying the takbir after each pebble, then said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"4090","Yahya ibn Said and Waki narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us with the meaning, from al-Amash, who said: Abdullah ibn Murrah narrated to me from al-Harith ibn Abdullah, who said: Abdullah said: The consumer of interest, its giver, its two witnesses and its writer when they know of it, the tattooer and the tattooed for beauty, the withholder of charity, and one who reverts to Bedouin life after migration are cursed on the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection."
"4091","Yahya narrated to us from al-Amash, and Waki: al-Amash narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Wahb narrated to us from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truthful and believed, narrated to us, saying: The creation of one of you is gathered in the belly of his mother in forty days, or he said forty nights. Waki said: Nights. Then he is a clot for the same, then he is a lump for the same. Then Allah sends to him the angel with four words: his deed, his term, his provision, and whether wretched or blessed. Then the spirit is breathed into him. By the One besides whom there is no god, one of you does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only an arm's length between him and it, but the book overtakes him and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire, becoming among them. And one of you does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only an arm's length between him and it, but the book overtakes him and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise, becoming among them."
"4092","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Sulayman narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Masruq from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No soul is killed unjustly but upon the first son of Adam is a share of its blood, for he was the first to institute killing."
"4093","Yahya narrated to us from al-Amash from Shaqiq from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When they are three, two should not converse privately excluding their companion, for that grieves him."
"4094","Yahya narrated to us from at-Taymi from Abu Uthman from Ibn Masud that a man took a kiss from a woman, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking about its expiation. Allah revealed: Establish prayer at the ends of the day and portions of the night. Good deeds remove evil deeds. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for me. He said: For whoever of my nation acts upon it."
"4095","Yahya narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to me from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah, who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that a man keeps lying until he is recorded with Allah a liar, and a man keeps telling the truth until he is recorded with Allah truthful."
"4096","Yahya narrated to us from at-Taymi from Abu Uthman from Ibn Masud: Whoever buys an animal with milk withheld in its udder, and perhaps he said a sheep with milk withheld, let him return it and return a sa with it. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting goods before they reach the market."
"4097","Yahya narrated to us from Mujalid: Amir narrated to us from Masruq from Abdullah, who said, once or twice, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no judge judging among people but he is detained on the Day of Resurrection, with an angel seizing his nape until he stands him over Hell. Then he raises his head to Allah. If he says what is wrong, he is thrown into Hell, falling forty autumns."
"4098","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Asim narrated to me from Zir from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The world shall not pass, or the world shall not end, until a man from my household rules the Arabs, his name matching my name."
"4099","He said: I read to Yahya ibn Said from Hisham: Qatadah narrated to us from Khilas from Abdullah ibn Utbah, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud was asked about a man who married a woman without naming a dowry for her, then died before consummating with her. He said nothing about it at first. They went back, then came to him and asked him. He said: I shall judge in it by my best opinion. If I am right, Allah will grant me success in it, and if I err, it is from me. She gets the dowry of her peers, she inherits, and she observes the waiting period. A man from Ashja stood and said: I testify about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he judged thus. He said: Bring whoever testifies with you to that. Abu al-Jarrah testified to that."
"4100","Abdulmalik ibn Amr narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us with the meaning, except that he said: About Barwa bint Washiq. He said: Bring your two witnesses to this. Abu Sinan and al-Jarrah, two men from Ashja, testified."
"4101","Yahya narrated to us from al-A'mash, Shaqiq narrated to me from Abdullah who said: When we sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer we would say: Peace be upon Allah from His servants, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say peace be upon Allah, for Allah is al-Salam, but when one of you sits let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; for if you say that it will reach every righteous servant between the heaven and the earth; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; then let one of you choose the supplication most pleasing to him and supplicate with it."
"4102","Waki' and Abu Mu'awiyah with the same meaning both said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which sin is greatest? He said: That you set up a rival to Allah though He created you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you kill your child for fear that he eat with you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor. He said: Then Allah Mighty and Majestic sent down confirmation of that in His Book: And those who do not invoke with Allah another god, up to His saying: And whoever does that will meet punishment."
"4103","Waki' and Ibn Numayr both said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, and Ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we be held to account for what we did in the Jahiliyyah? He said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be held to account for what he did in the Jahiliyyah, and whoever does evil in Islam will be taken to account for the first and the last."
"4104","Waki' and Ibn Numayr both said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu ad-Duha from Masruq who said: While a man was narrating in the great mosque he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes smoke will descend from heaven and seize the hearing and sight of the hypocrites, and the believers will get from it something like a cold. Masruq said: So I entered upon Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and he was reclining, then he sat upright and began to narrate and said: O people, whoever among you is asked about knowledge he has, let him speak of it, and if he does not have it let him say: Allah knows best, for part of knowledge is to say for what you do not know: Allah knows best. Allah Mighty and Majestic said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say: I do not ask you for it any reward, nor am I of those who affect. When Quraysh overcame the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and defied him, he said: O Allah, help me with seven like the seven of Yusuf. Then a year of famine seized them in which they ate bones and carrion from hardship, until one of them would see between him and the heaven something like smoke from hunger. So they said: Our Lord, remove from us the punishment, indeed we are believers. It was said to him: If We remove it from them they will return. So he supplicated his Lord and He removed it from them, then they returned, and Allah took vengeance on them on the day of Badr. That is His saying Exalted: So watch for the day the heaven brings clear smoke, up to His saying: The day We seize with the great seizure, indeed We will take retribution. Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: Abdullah said: Had it been the Day of Resurrection He would not have removed it from them."
"4105","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad ibn Yazid from Abdullah who said: I recited before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there any mudhdhakir, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there any muddakir."
"4106","Waki' narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of one, for that grieves him."
"4107","Waki' and Abu Mu'awiyah both said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il who said: Abdullah said: As if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he relates a prophet among the prophets whom his people struck, and he is wiping the blood, Abu Mu'awiyah said: wiping the blood from his forehead, and saying: My Lord, forgive my people for they do not know."
"4108","Waki' and Abu Mu'awiyah both said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness and wickedness leads to the Fire, and a man keeps lying until he is written with Allah as a liar. And he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness and righteousness leads to Paradise, and a man keeps telling the truth and seeking truthfulness until he is written with Allah as a truthful one. Abu Mu'awiyah said: And a man keeps telling the truth and seeking truthfulness."
"4109","Waki' and Yazid reported to us: Isma'il reported to us from Qays from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and given him power over its spending in truth, and another to whom Allah has given wisdom and he judges by it and teaches it."
"4110","Waki' narrated to us Hasan narrated to us from Yahya ibn al-Harith from Abu Majid al-Hanafi from Ibn Mas'ud who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral, and he said: Less than trotting; the funeral is followed and is not a follower."
"4111","Waki' narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Masruq from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who tears the garments and strikes the cheeks and calls with the call of the Jahiliyyah."
"4112","Waki' narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Umarah ibn Umayr from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O company of young men, whoever among you can afford marriage let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts, and whoever cannot, upon him is fasting for it is a restraint for him."
"4113","Waki' narrated to us from Ibn Abi Khalid from Qays from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were young men, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate ourselves? So he forbade us, then he permitted us to marry a woman for a garment for a fixed term. Then Abdullah recited: Do not forbid the good things Allah has made lawful to you."
"4114","Waki' narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us from Abu Musa al-Hilali from his father that a man was on a journey and his wife gave birth and her milk was withheld, so he began to suck it and spit it out, then some entered his throat. So he came to Abu Musa and he said: She has become unlawful to you. Then he came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of suckling makes unlawful except what grows flesh and strengthens bone."
"4115","Waki' narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah that he said regarding the sermon of need: Praise belongs to Allah, we seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls; whom Allah guides none can misguide, and whom He misguides none can guide; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and I bear witness Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recited three verses from the Book of Allah: Fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims; Fear Allah by whom you ask one another and the wombs, indeed Allah is over you watchful; Fear Allah and speak upright words, to the end of the verse."
"4116","Waki' narrated to us Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of need, and he mentioned a similar hadith except that he did not say inna."
"4117","Waki' narrated to us al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Jami' ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhrah from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: When Abdullah came to the Jamrah, the Jamrat al-Aqabah, he went into the interior of the valley and faced the Ka'bah and placed the Jamrah at his right eyebrow, then he threw seven pebbles saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble, then he said: From here, by the One besides whom there is no god, threw the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"4118","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite the Qur'an to me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I recite to you when it was sent down upon you? He said: I desire to hear it from other than myself. He said: So I opened Surat an-Nisa and recited to him, and when I reached: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as witness over these, An-Nisa 41, he said: I looked at him and his eyes were shedding tears."
"4119","Waki' narrated to us from Mis'ar from Alqamah ibn Marthad from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd from Abdullah who said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my husband the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and of my father Abu Sufyan and of my brother Mu'awiyah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah Mighty and Majestic for fixed terms and counted days and apportioned provisions; nothing will be hastened before its time nor delayed from its time. Had you asked Allah Mighty and Majestic to protect you from punishment in the Fire or punishment in the grave it would have been better and more excellent. He said: And monkeys were mentioned before him, Mis'ar said: I think he said: and pigs, from what was transformed. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Mighty and Majestic did not make for one transformed any offspring or progeny, and monkeys, I think he said: and pigs, existed before that."
"4120","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us ath-Thawri narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad similar with its chain, and he did not doubt about the pigs."
"4121","Waki' narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I disavow every close friendship, and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr; your companion is the close friend of Allah Mighty and Majestic."
"4122","Waki' narrated to us from al-Mas'udi from al-Hakam from Dharr from Wa'il ibn Mahanah at-Taymi from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O company of women, give charity, for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman said: Why are we most of the people of the Fire? He said: Because you curse much and deny the kindness of the husband."
"4123","Waki' narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Masruq from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul killed unjustly but upon the first son of Adam is a share of its blood, because he was the first to institute killing."
"4124","Waki' and Abdur-Rahman with the same meaning, and this is the wording of Waki', Sufyan narrated to us from Abdul-Karim al-Jazari from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil that his father Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani said to Ibn Mas'ud: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Regret is repentance? He said: Yes."
"4125","Waki' narrated to us al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Jabir from Abu ad-Duha from Masruq from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he is the truthful and believed, said: The sale of muhaffalat is deception, and deception is not lawful for a Muslim."
"4126","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Zubayd from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Abusing the Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is disbelief."
"4127","Waki' narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You will see after me favoritism and trials and matters you will deny. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command whoever among us witnesses that? He said: You render the duty upon you and ask Allah for what belongs to you."
"4128","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Shu'bah from as-Suddi from Murrah from Abdullah: And there is none of you but will come to it. He said: They will enter it or pass into it, then they will issue from it by their deeds. I said to him: Isra'il narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or words to this meaning."
"4129","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah who said: Allah has cursed the women who tattoo and those who seek tattooing and those who pluck eyebrows and those who make gaps between teeth for beauty, those who change Allah's creation. A woman in the house called Umm Ya'qub heard of it and came to him and said: I heard you said such-and-such. He said: Why should I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed in the Book of Allah Mighty and Majestic? She said: I recite what is between its two covers and I did not find it. He said: If you had recited it you would have found it; did you not recite: Whatever the Messenger gives you take it, and whatever he forbids you abstain from it? She said: Yes. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. She said: I think your household do it. He said: Go and look. So she looked and saw nothing of what she sought. Then she came and said: I saw nothing. He said: Had it been so she would not have lived with us. He said: And I heard it from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abis narrating it from Umm Ya'qub, he heard it from her, but I preferred the hadith of Mansur."
"4130","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Abidah from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, three or four times, then there will come a people whose testimony precedes their oath and their oath their testimony. He said: Our companions used to beat us when we were children over testimony and pledges."
"4131","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Umarah from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest with Allah Mighty and Majestic? He said: That you set up a rival to Allah Mighty and Majestic though He created you. I said: Then what? He said: Then that you kill your child fearing he will eat of your food, and Abdur-Rahman once said: that he eat with you. Then I said: Then what? He said: That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor."
"4132","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us who said: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: Abdullah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which sin is greatest, and he mentioned it."
"4133","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"4134","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us Warqa narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Amr ibn Shurahbil from Abdullah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest? And he mentioned it. Then he recited: And those who do not invoke with Allah another god, up to humiliated."
"4135","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: O Allah, I ask You guidance and piety and chastity and richness."
"4136","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend I would have taken the son of Abu Quhafah as a close friend."
"4137","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Umarah from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer except at its appointed time, except that he combined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah and prayed Fajr that day out of its appointed time."
"4138","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Umarah with the same meaning."
"4139","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah who said: To swear nine times that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was killed murder is dearer to me than to swear once that he was not killed, and that is because Allah Mighty and Majestic made him a prophet and took him as a martyr. He said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim and he said: They used to hold and say that the Jews poisoned him and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4140","Abdul-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us, and Abdur-Razzaq informed us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah who said: When Glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness, indeed He is Accepting of repentance was revealed, Abdur-Razzaq said: When When the help of Allah and the victory came was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, O Allah forgive me, indeed You are the Accepting of repentance."
"4141","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Isra'il from as-Suddi from Murrah from Abdullah: And there is none of you but will come to it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All people will come to the Fire, then they will issue from it by their deeds."
"4142","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, and Yazid narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd reported to us from Asim ibn Abi an-Najud from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us then said: This is the path of Allah. Then he drew lines to its right and its left, then said: These are paths, Yazid said: diverging, upon each path among them is a devil calling to it. Then he recited: This is My straight path so follow it, and do not follow the paths lest they scatter you from His path."
"4143","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Za'idah narrated to us from Asim from Shaqiq from Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while alive, and those who take graves as mosques."
"4144","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Ali ibn al-Aqmar from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will stand only upon the worst of people."
"4145","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Za'idah narrated to us from Asim from Shaqiq from Abdullah who said: We used to speak in prayer, and some of us would greet others and one of us would instruct about a need. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him while he was praying, and he did not return it to me. So I was seized by what was past and what was new. When he prayed he said: Allah Mighty and Majestic introduces of His command what He wills, and He has introduced that you not speak in prayer."
"4146","Isma'il narrated to us Ayyub narrated to us from Humayd ibn Hilal from Abu Qatadah from Usayr ibn Jabir who said: A red wind raged at Kufah, then a man came whose only cry was: O Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, the Hour has come. He was reclining then sat and said: The Hour will not stand until no inheritance is divided nor joy taken in spoils. An enemy will gather against the people of Islam and the people of Islam will gather against them, and he gestured with his hand toward Sham. I said: You mean the Romans? He said: Yes. And at that fighting there will be severe apostasy. The Muslims will stipulate a vanguard for death that will not return except victorious, and they will fight until night separates them, then these and these will return, each not victorious, and the vanguard will perish. Then the Muslims will stipulate a vanguard for death that will not return except victorious, and they will fight until night separates them, then these and these will return, each not victorious, and the vanguard will perish. Then the Muslims will stipulate a vanguard for death that will not return except victorious, and they will fight until evening, then these and these will return, each not victorious, and the vanguard will perish. When the fourth day comes the remainder of the people of Islam will rise against them, and Allah Mighty and Majestic will grant them the victory, and they will kill a slaughter the like of which, he either said: is not seen, or said: we have not seen, until a bird passing their flanks would not leave them till it falls dead. Then the sons of one father who were a hundred will count and find only one man remaining of them, so in what spoils to rejoice or what inheritance to divide? While they are thus they will hear of people greater than that: The herald will come to them that the Dajjal has taken their place among their offspring. So they will discard what is in their hands and turn, and they will send ten horsemen as scouts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know their names and the names of their fathers and the colors of their horses; they are the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day."
"4147","Isma'il narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Uthman from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal, or he said: the call of Bilal, prevent one of you from his sahur, for he calls, or he said: he announces, so that your standing one may return and your sleeping one may be alerted. Then it is not that he says thus or thus, until he says thus."
"4148","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, then a man of the Ansar said: This distribution was not intended for the Face of Allah Mighty and Majestic. Abdullah said: O enemy of Allah, I shall surely inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what you said. So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his face reddened, and he said: May Allah have mercy upon Musa, he was harmed with more than this and was patient."
"4149","Isma'il reported to us Dawud and Ibn Abi Za'idah with the meaning both said: Dawud narrated to us from ash-Sha'bi from Alqamah who said: I said to Ibn Mas'ud: Did any of you accompany the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn? He said: None of us accompanied him, but we missed him one night and said: He has been assassinated, taken away by force, what happened to him? So we spent the worst night a people ever spent. When morning came, or he said: at dawn, there he was coming from the direction of Hira. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, and they mentioned the state they were in. He said: The caller of the jinn came to me, so I went to them and recited to them. Then he went with us and showed us their traces and traces of their fires. Ash-Sha'bi said: They asked him for provision. Ibn Abi Za'idah said: Amir said: So they asked him that night for provision, and they were of the jinn of the Peninsula. He said: Every bone over which the name of Allah is mentioned falling into your hands will have more meat on it than it ever had, and every dung is fodder for your animals. So do not clean yourselves with them, for they are provision of your brothers among the jinn."
"4150","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Ibrahim from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid that he performed Hajj with Abdullah and that he threw the Jamrah with seven pebbles. He said: He placed the House to his left and Mina to his right and said: This is the station of the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"4151","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam who said: I heard Dharr narrating from Wa'il ibn Mahanah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said to women: Give charity, for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman not among the elite of women, or among the most intelligent of them, said: O Messenger of Allah, in what or why or for what? He said: You curse much and deny the kindness of the husband."
"4152","Bahz narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us al-Hakam narrated to me from Dharr from Wa'il ibn Mahanah of Taym ar-Ribab among the companions of Abdullah from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to women: Give charity, for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman not among the elite of women said: In what and for what and why? And he mentioned the hadith."
"4153","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: I heard Abdullah saying: I said: Did you hear it from Abdullah? He said: Yes, and he raised it: There is none more jealous than Allah Mighty and Majestic, and therefore He forbade immoralities what is open of them and what is hidden, and there is none to whom praise is dearer than Allah Mighty and Majestic, and therefore He praised Himself."
"4154","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah that he heard Abu Wa'il narrating that a man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I recited all the Mufassal in one rak'ah. Abdullah said: Like the chopping of poetry; I know the pairs the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between. He said: He mentioned twenty surahs of the Mufassal, two surahs in each rak'ah."
"4155","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Abu Ubaydah, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Abu Ubaydah from his father Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sat in the first two rak'ahs was as if upon hot stones. I said to Sa'd: Until he stands? He said: Until he stands. Hajjaj said: Shu'bah said: Sa'd would move his lips with something, so I said: Until he stands? He said: Until he stands."
"4156","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Yazid reported to us al-Mas'udi from Simak ibn Harb from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, Hajjaj said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, Yazid said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered us and we were forty, and I was among the last to come to him. He said: You are aided and granted and opened to, so whoever witnesses that let him fear Allah and enjoin good and forbid evil, and whoever lies upon me deliberately let him take his seat in the Fire. Yazid said: And let him join his kin."
"4157","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us, and Abdur-Razzaq reported to us Isra'il from Simak ibn Harb from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, Abdur-Razzaq said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: May Allah brighten one who hears a hadith from us and preserves it till he conveys it, for many a conveyed one retains better than the hearer."
"4158","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: I heard Uqbah ibn Wassaj from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The excellence of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-five degrees. Hajjaj said: Shu'bah did not raise it for me, though he raised it for others. He said: I hesitate to raise it because Abdullah rarely raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4159","Bahz narrated it to me Hammam narrated to us Qatadah reported to us from Muwarriq from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami from Ibn Mas'ud that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prefer the congregational prayer over a man's prayer alone by twenty-five prayers, each like his prayer."
"4160","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us who said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud that he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taught the openings of good and its comprehensive forms and its seals. He said: When you sit in every two rak'ahs say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and I bear witness Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; then let one of you choose the supplication most pleasing to him and supplicate his Lord Mighty and Majestic with it. And Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you what al-adhu is? It is tale-carrying, spreading word among people. And Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man tells the truth until he is written truthful, and lies until he is written a liar."
"4161","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Had I taken anyone of my nation as a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4162","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: O Allah, I ask You guidance and piety and chastity and richness."
"4163","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to recite this letter: Is there any muddakir."
"4164","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Affan both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, Affan said: Abu Ishaq reported to us from al-Aswad, and Muhammad said: from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard al-Aswad narrating from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he recited an-Najm and prostrated in it, and those with him prostrated, except that an old man took a handful of pebbles or dust and raised it to his forehead and said: This suffices me. Abdullah said: I saw him afterwards killed as a disbeliever."
"4165","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ubaydah from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah passed by me while I was praying and said: Ask, you will be given, O son of Umm Abd. Umar said: So I hastened, I and Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr beat me to him, and we never raced to good but Abu Bakr beat me to it. He said: Part of my supplication I almost never leave: O Allah, I ask You bliss that does not perish, and coolness of eye that does not end, and companionship of the Prophet Muhammad in the highest Paradise, the Paradise of eternity."
"4166","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us, and Yahya from Shu'bah from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Maymun from Abdullah that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a tent, about forty. He said: Are you pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Are you pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, I hope you will be half of the people of Paradise, and that is because Paradise will be entered only by a Muslim soul, and you among the people of polytheism are but like the white hair on the skin of the black ox, or the black hair on the skin of the red ox."
"4167","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the keys of all things except the five: Allah has with Him knowledge of the Hour, and sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die; indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware. I said to him: Did you hear it from Abdullah? He said: Yes, more than fifty times."
"4168","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us who said: I heard Yahya ibn al-Mujabbir who said: I heard Abu Majid, meaning al-Hanafi, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah who said: I remember the first man whose hand he cut: A thief was brought and he ordered his cutting, and it was as if the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ashes strewn upon it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, as if you disliked his cutting? He said: What prevents me? Do not be an aid to Satan against your brother. The Imam when a prescribed punishment reaches him must establish it. Allah Mighty and Majestic is Pardoning and loves pardon; let them pardon and overlook; do you not love that Allah forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"4169","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us Sufyan reported to us from Yahya ibn Abdullah at-Taymi from Abu Majid al-Hanafi and he mentioned its meaning, and said: As if the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ashes strewn upon it, meaning dust scattered upon it."
"4170","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, and he was the imam of Alqamah's mosque after Alqamah, who said: Alqamah led us in Dhuhr, and I do not know whether he prayed three or five. It was said to him, and he said: And you O one-eyed? I said: Yes. Then he prostrated two prostrations, then Alqamah narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"4171","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj from Shu'bah from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Isa al-Asadi from Zirr from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Omens are part of shirk, and there is none of us but Allah removes it by trust."
"4172","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Jabir from Abu ad-Duha from Masruq from Abdullah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to salute to his right and to his left until I would see the whiteness of his face, and what I have not forgotten after what I forgot: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"4173","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur and Sulayman from Ibrahim from Abidah as-Salmani from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will remain a people whose testimonies precede their oaths and their oaths their testimonies."
"4174","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us Mansur wrote to me and I read it to him who said: Ibrahim narrated to me from Alqamah from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, I do not know whether he added or decreased, Ibrahim is the one saying Alqamah does not know whether he said: added or decreased, or Abdullah. Then he turned to us and we told him of his deed, then he folded his leg and faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations, then turned to us with his face and said: Had something new happened in prayer I would have informed you of it, but I am only human, I forget as you forget, so if I forget remind me, and whichever of you doubts in his prayer let him seek the closest to what is correct and complete upon it and salute, then prostrate two prostrations."
"4175","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, lest it grieve him, and a woman should not touch another woman so as to describe her to her husband."
"4176","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet that he said: How bad for one of you, or how bad for one of them, to say: I forgot verse such-and-such, rather he was made to forget; remember the Qur'an, for it escapes the chests of men faster than camels from their hobbles, or from its hobble."
"4177","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah who said: We used to say: Peace upon so-and-so and so-and-so. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and I bear witness Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. For if you say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, you will have greeted every righteous servant in the earth and in the heaven."
"4178","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur, and Zubayd from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Abusing the believer is wickedness and fighting him is disbelief. In the hadith of Zubayd he said: I heard Abu Wa'il."
"4179","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to me Rukayn who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Hassan narrating from Abdur-Rahman ibn Harmalah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike ten: saffron dye, changing gray hair, dragging the izar, a gold ring, or he said: a gold circle, playing with dice, display of adornment out of its place, incantations except with the Mu'awwidhat, amulets, withdrawing water, and spoiling the child without forbidding it."
"4180","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mughirah who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd, and men of you will be raised to me, then they will be snatched away from me, so I will say: O Lord, my companions. Then it will be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"4181","Hajjaj narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu at-Tayyah from a man of Tayy from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us tabuqur in family and wealth. Abu Hamzah, and he was sitting with him, said: Yes, Akhram at-Ta'i narrated to me from his father from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said it. Abdullah said: Then how about a family in Radhan and a family in Madinah and such family? Shu'bah said: I said to Abu at-Tayyah: What is tabuqur? He said: Abundance."
"4182","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Raja who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrating from Abu al-Ahwas who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother and my companion, and Allah Mighty and Majestic has taken your companion as a close friend."
"4183","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah, and I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Before the Hour are days of harj, days in which knowledge departs and ignorance appears. Abu Musa said: Harj in the tongue of Abyssinia is killing."
"4184","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu at-Tayyah from Ibn al-Akhram, a man of Tayy, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade tabuqur in family and wealth."
"4185","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us who said: I heard Abu Jamrah narrating from his father from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said it, and Abdullah said: How one who has three families: a family in Madinah and a family in such-and-such and a family in such-and-such."
"4186","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, Hajjaj said: I heard Abu Amr ash-Shaybani, and Muhammad said: from Abu Amr ash-Shaybani who said: The owner of this house narrated to us, and he gestured with his hand to the house of Abdullah, and he did not name him to us. He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deed is most beloved to Allah Mighty and Majestic? He said: Prayer at its time, Hajjaj said: at its time. He said: Then which? He said: Then kindness to parents. He said: Then which? He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah. Had I asked more he would have added to me."
"4187","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: A man keeps telling the truth and seeking truthfulness until he is written truthful, and a man keeps lying and seeking lying until he is written with Allah as a liar."
"4188","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah that he said: I am told of your gathering but I am prevented from coming out to you fearing I will bore you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose times for us with admonition fearing weariness upon us."
"4189","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman and Mansur and Hammad and al-Mughirah and Abu Hashim from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said in the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"4190","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur and al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of one, and a woman should not touch another woman and describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her. I think Mansur said: Unless there is a garment between them."
"4191","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you are three, and he mentioned its meaning."
"4192","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Abdul-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid from Ibn Mas'ud who said: When evening came the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: We have entered evening and dominion belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah; there is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He."
"4193","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan cannot assume my likeness."
"4194","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Salamah from Isa ibn Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Omens are shirk, omens are shirk, but Allah Mighty and Majestic removes it by trust."
"4195","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu Qays from Huzayl who said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi'ah and asked them about a daughter and a son's daughter and a sister. They said: To the daughter half and to the sister half, and go to Abdullah for he will follow us. So he came to Abdullah and told him, and he said: I would be astray then and not of the guided; I shall surely judge in it by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sufyan said thus: To the daughter half and to the son's daughter a sixth, and what remains to the sister."
"4196","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not fitting for anyone to be better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"4197","And Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated it to us with its chain who said: None of you should say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"4198","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' who said: Abu Zur'ah narrated to us a companion of ours narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: Nothing transmits disease to anything. A Bedouin stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, a mangy spot from scabies on a camel's lip or tail among great camels makes them all mangy. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then who made the first mangy? There is no contagion and no hamah and no Safar; Allah created every soul and wrote its life and its calamities and its provision."
"4199","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah who said: I prayed and stood with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he remained standing until I intended an evil matter. He said: We said: What did you intend? He said: I intended to sit and leave him."
"4200","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The first judged among the servants is blood."
"4201","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Affan narrated to us, they both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman — Affan said: Sulayman narrated to us — from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For every treacherous person there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Ja'far said: It will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"4202","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was describing a prophet: his people beat him until he fell unconscious; he would wipe his forehead and say: O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"4203","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, and a man said: This is a distribution by which the Face of Allah was not intended. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and his face turned red. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: And he became angry, until I wished I had not informed him. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: May Allah have mercy on us and on Musa — Shu'bah doubted about May Allah have mercy on us and on Musa — He was harmed with more than this and he was patient; this part has no doubt: He was harmed with more than that and he was patient."
"4204","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was suffering from fever, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering a severe fever. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I suffer the fever of two men among you. I said: Is it because you have two rewards? He said: Yes — or: Indeed. Then he said: There is no Muslim who is afflicted by harm, a thorn or anything greater, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, removes his sins from him just as the tree sheds its leaves."
"4205","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman and Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that Quraysh had become defiant toward him, he said: O Allah, help me against them with seven like the seven of Yusuf. So famine seized them until it consumed everything, until they ate skins and bones — and one of them said: until they ate skins and carrion — and there would come out of a man something like the appearance of smoke. Then Abu Sufyan came to him and said: O Muhammad, your people have perished, so supplicate Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to remove it from them. So he supplicated. Then he said: O Allah, if they return, then return — this is in the hadith of Mansur. Then he recited this verse: So watch for the day when the sky brings a clear smoke."
"4206","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while he has what suffices him, his begging will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches or lacerations on his face. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is his sufficiency? He said: Fifty dirhams, or its equivalent in gold."
"4207","Waki' narrated to us: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What have I to do with this world? My example and the example of this world is only like that of a rider who took shade under a tree on a summer day, then departed and left it."
"4208","Waki' narrated to us: Isa ibn Dinar, freedman of Khuza'ah, narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: We did not fast Ramadan in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as twenty-nine days more often than we fasted it as thirty days."
"4209","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadham, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — Waki' said: Allah has on earth traveling angels who convey to me the greetings of peace from my ummah."
"4210","Waki' narrated to us: from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: I shall pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he raised his hands at the beginning."
"4211","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath by which he seizes the property of a Muslim man, while he is wicked therein, will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him. He said: And this verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to the end of the verse."
"4212","Waki' and Humayd al-Ru'asi both said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il — Humayd said: Shaqiq ibn Salamah — from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first matter to be judged among people on the Day of Resurrection will be concerning blood."
"4213","Ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il, and he mentioned it."
"4214","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us — and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."
"4215","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah — and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said — Paradise — and Waki' said: from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is indeed nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise."
"4216","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony precedes their oaths and whose oaths precede their testimony."
"4217","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khumayr ibn Malik, he said: Abdullah said: I learned seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Zayd ibn Thabit was still a young boy with a forelock among the scribes."
"4218","Waki' narrated to us: Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Tariq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted by poverty and brings it to people, he is likely not to have his need fulfilled; and whoever brings it to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah will bring him immediate provision or a delayed death."
"4219","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Bashir Abu Isma'il, from Sayyar Abu Hamzah, and he mentioned it. My father said: And the correct one is Sayyar Abu Hamzah. He said: And Sayyar Abu al-Hakam did not narrate anything from Tariq ibn Shihab."
"4220","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Wahb ibn Rabi'ah, from Abdullah, he said: I was sheltering under the curtains of the Ka'bah when two Thaqafi men and their Qurashi brother-in-law entered — or two Qurashi men and their Thaqafi brother-in-law — abundant in the fat of their bellies, scant in the understanding of their hearts. They spoke among themselves, and one of them said to his companion: Do you think Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hears what we say? Another said: I think He hears when we raise our voices and does not hear when we whisper. The other said: If He hears anything of it, He hears all of it. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And you were not covering yourselves lest your hearing and your sight testify against you, the verse."
"4221","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, and he mentioned its meaning. Then was revealed: And you were not covering yourselves lest your hearing and your sight testify against you, up to His saying: and you became among the losers."
"4222","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan: Amr ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrated to me, he said: The owner of this house — meaning Ibn Mas'ud — narrated to me, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its proper time."
"4223","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad: al-Aswad and Alqamah — or one of them — informed us, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir in every rising and lowering. He said: And Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, did so."
"4224","Waki' narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad and Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say takbir in every lowering and rising."
"4225","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would place his hand under his cheek and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants."
"4226","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan said: al-A'mash said, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"4227","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us with admonition on different days, out of fear of boredom for us."
"4228","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not come into direct contact with another woman and then describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her."
"4229","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: May Allah curse the tattooing women and the women who seek tattooing, and the women who pluck eyebrows, and the women who file teeth for beauty. That reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub. She came to him and said: I have read what is between the two covers and I did not find what you said. He said: Did you not find: Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it? She said: I see it on some of your family. He said: Go and look. So she went and looked, then she came and said: I did not see anything. Abdullah said: Had she done so, we would not have kept her company."
"4230","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one statement, and I said another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire. And I said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise."
"4231","Ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: setting up a rival to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"4232","Waki' narrated to us, from his father and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and richness."
"4233","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shimir ibn Atiyyah al-Kahili, from Mughirah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Akhram al-Ta'i, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take estates, lest you become desirous of this world."
"4234","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm and prostrated in it, along with those with him, except for a large old man who took a handful of pebbles or dust and said with it like this, placing it on his forehead. He said: I later saw him killed as a disbeliever."
"4235","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"4236","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah — and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr as five rak'ahs. It was said to him: Has the prayer been increased? He said: What is that? They said: You prayed five. So he folded his leg, then prostrated two prostrations after he had given salam."
"4237","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Umarah, from Wahb ibn Rabi'ah, from Abdullah, he said: I was sheltering under the curtains of the Ka'bah when three men came — a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi brothers-in-law — abundant in the fat of their bellies, scant in the understanding of their hearts. They spoke among themselves, and one of them said: Do you think Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hears what we say? Another said: He hears what we raise and what we lower, He does not hear. The other said: If He hears anything, He hears all of it. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then was revealed: And you were not covering yourselves lest testimony be borne against you, up to His saying: then they will not be of those to be excused."
"4238","He said: And Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah, the like of that."
"4239","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah, he said: I heard him once raise it [to the Prophet] then he left it. He saw a commander — or a man — give two salams, and he said: How did he pick that up?"
"4240","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When this verse was revealed: Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrongdoing — it was hard upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: Which of us has not wronged himself? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not as you think; it is only as Luqman said to his son: O my son, do not associate partners with Allah; indeed association is a great wrongdoing."
"4241","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to give salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah — until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen. And Abd al-Rahman said: Until we could see the whiteness of his cheek from here, and we could see the whiteness of his cheek from here."
"4242","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from a man, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Walk to the mosque, for it is among the guidance and the sunnah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4243","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Prayer at its proper time. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Jihad in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Had I asked him for more, he would have given me more."
"4244","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan: Mansur narrated to me, from Khaythamah, from one who heard Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no evening conversation except for one who prays or a traveler."
"4245","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three persons: a life for a life, a married adulterer, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"4246","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah said: I came upon Abu Jahl on the day of Badr while his leg had been struck and he was fallen, fending people off from himself with a sword of his. I said: Praise be to Allah who has disgraced you, O enemy of Allah. He said: Is he anything but a man killed by his own people? So I began reaching at him with a sword of mine that was of little worth, and I struck his hand so his sword fell, and I took it and struck him with it until I killed him. He said: Then I went out until I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if I were lifted from the ground, and I informed him. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god? He repeated it three times. He said: I said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god. He said: Then he went out walking with me until he stood over him, and he said: Praise be to Allah who has disgraced you, O enemy of Allah; this was the Pharaoh of this ummah. He said: And my father added in it, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah said: Then he gave me his sword as spoils."
"4247","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr and said: I killed Abu Jahl. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god? He said: I said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god. He repeated it three times. He said: Allah is Most Great; praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Go and show him to me. So we went, and there he was, and he said: This is the Pharaoh of this ummah."
"4248","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a field in Madinah when he passed by some Jews. Some of them said to others: Ask him about the soul. Others said: Do not ask him. They said: O Muhammad, what is the soul? So he stood, leaning on a palm stalk, while I was behind him, and I thought revelation was being sent to him. Then he said: They ask you about the soul; say: The soul is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little. Some of them said: We told you, do not ask him."
"4249","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Mu'awiyah al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd al-Ashja'i, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Sumayyah was never offered two matters except that he chose the most guided of them."
"4250","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I met a woman in the garden and I embraced her, touched her, kissed her, and did everything with her except that I did not have intercourse with her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent toward him. Then this verse was revealed: Indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and recited it to him. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for people in general? He said: Rather, for people in general."
"4251","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Mina while he was leaning his back against a red tent. He said: Are you not pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Are you not pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: By Allah, I indeed hope you will be half of the people of Paradise. And I shall tell you about that: about the small number of Muslims among people on that day — they on that day among people are only like a white hair on a black bull, or like a black hair on a white bull; and none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul."
"4252","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Hammam narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hassan, from Fulfulah al-Ju'fi, he said: I hastened among those who hastened to Abdullah concerning the codices. We entered upon him, and a man among the people said: We did not come to you as visitors, but we came to you when this news alarmed us. He said: The Qur'an was revealed to your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from seven gates upon seven modes — or he said: letters — while the Book before it used to come down from one gate upon one mode."
"4253","Waki' narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given everything except the five keys of the unseen: Indeed Allah, with Him is the knowledge of the Hour."
"4254","Sufyan — meaning Ibn Uyaynah — narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Mughirah al-Yashkuri, from al-Ma'rur, from Abdullah, he said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my husband, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and of my brother Mu'awiyah, and of my father Abu Sufyan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: You have asked Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for fixed terms, trodden traces, and apportioned provisions; nothing of them will come before its time nor be delayed. Had you asked Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to rescue you from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. And he was asked about monkeys and pigs: Are they from what was transformed, or something that existed before that? He said: No, rather they existed before that. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not destroy a people and then give them progeny or descendants."
"4255","Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: I read to my father from here to al-Balagh, and he acknowledged it: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us: Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was between Abu Bakr and Umar, with Abdullah praying. He began al-Nisa and recited it fluently. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. Then he proceeded to ask, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given. Among what he asked, he said: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not apostatize, bliss that does not end, and companionship of Your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity. Then Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, came to Abdullah to give him glad tidings, but found Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, had preceded him. He said: If you did so, you were indeed foremost in good."
"4256","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Amr ibn Mujammi' Abu al-Mundhir al-Kindi narrated to you, he said: Ibrahim al-Hajari informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made the good deed of the son of Adam ten times its like up to seven hundredfold, except fasting; fasting is for Me and I shall reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: joy at his breaking fast, and joy on the Day of Resurrection. The breath of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"4257","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Amr ibn Mujammi' narrated to you: Ibrahim al-Hajari informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the servant of one of you brings his food, let him bring him near and seat him with him over it, or let him feed him a morsel, for he endured its heat and smoke."
"4258","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Amr ibn Mujammi' narrated to us: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first one to institute free-roaming cattle and worship idols was Abu Khuza'ah Amr ibn Amir; and I saw him dragging his intestines in the Fire."
"4259","I read to my father: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to you: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, but he did not mention: and worship idols."
"4260","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Amr ibn Mujammi' narrated to you: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor person is not the wandering beggar whom a morsel or two morsels, or a date or two dates, turn away. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then who is the poor? He said: One who does not ask people, nor finds what suffices him, nor is noticed so that charity is given to him."
"4261","Abdullah said: I read to my father: al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated to you, he said: al-Hajari informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hands are three: the Hand of Allah is the Highest, the giving hand that follows it, and the begging hand is the lowest."
"4262","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to you, he said: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling a Muslim, his brother, is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."
"4263","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of these two marked dice that are thrown vehemently, for they are the gambling of the non-Arabs."
"4264","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Hajari informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Repentance from sin is to repent from it and then not return to it."
"4265","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muslim al-Hajari informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you shield his face from the Fire, even with half a date."
"4266","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you comes to him with his food, let him seat him with him or let him hand him some of it, for he endured its heat and smoke."
"4267","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed me, he said: I came to Abu Abd al-Rahman and there he was cauterizing a boy. I said: Are you cauterizing him? He said: Yes, it is the medicine of the Arabs. Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down with it a medicine; whoever among you is ignorant of it is ignorant of it, and whoever among you knows it knows it."
"4268","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, opens the gates of heaven in the remaining third of the night, then descends to the lowest heaven, then extends His hand, then says: Is there no servant asking Me so I may give him, until dawn breaks."
"4269","Abdullah said: I read to my father: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Abdi narrated to us: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who is thrifty will never become poor. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: Up to here I read to my father, and from here my father narrated to me."
"4270","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah, that he said concerning this verse: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split: It had split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into two parts — or two halves; Shu'bah is the one who doubts — one part was behind the mountain and one part over the mountain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bear witness."
"4271","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that Ibn Mas'ud was met by Uthman at Arafat, and he withdrew with him and spoke to him. Then Uthman said to Ibn Mas'ud: Shall I marry you to a young maiden? Abdullah ibn Mas'ud called Alqamah and related that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you is able to marry, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts; and whoever is unable, let him fast, for fasting is a shield for him — or a restraint for him."
"4272","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, that al-Aswad and Alqamah were with Abdullah in the house. Abdullah said: Have these prayed? They said: Yes. So he prayed with them without adhan or iqamah, and stood in their midst, and said: When you are three, do like this; and when you are more, let one of you lead you, and let one of you place his hands between his thighs when he bows, bending down. It is as if I am looking at the interlacing of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4273","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, and from Abu Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that Subay'ah bint al-Harith gave birth fifteen nights after the death of her husband. Abu al-Sanabil entered upon her and said: It is as if you are considering marriage for yourself; that is not for you until the farther of the two terms passes. So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what Abu al-Sanabil had said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu al-Sanabil has lied. When someone you approve comes to you, bring him to me — or he said: inform me. And he informed her that her waiting period had ended."
"4274","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Subay'ah bint al-Harith — and he mentioned the hadith, or the like of it. And in it he said: And when a suitable match comes to you, bring him to me — or: inform me. And in it there is no mention of Ibn Mas'ud."
"4275","And Abd al-Wahhab said: from Khilas, from Ibn Utbah, mursal."
"4276","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said — about a man who marries and does not stipulate for her — meaning: then he dies: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas and Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, that he said: They repeatedly came to Ibn Mas'ud about that for a month, or close to that, and they said: You must give a verdict in it. He said: I judge for her the like of the dowry of a woman among her womenfolk, with neither reduction nor excess; she has the inheritance and upon her is the waiting period. If it is correct, it is from Allah, Mighty and Majestic; and if it is a mistake, it is from me and from Satan, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger are free of it. Then a group from Ashja', among them al-Jarrah and Abu Sinan, stood and said: We testify that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a woman among us called Barwa' bint Washiq with the like of what you judged. Ibn Mas'ud rejoiced at that with great joy when his statement coincided with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4277","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: My father — and I read to Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Khilas, and from Abu Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, that Ibn Mas'ud was approached concerning a woman whom a man married without naming a dowry for her, then died before consummating with her. He said: They repeatedly came to Ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Her husband was Hilal — I think he said: Ibn Murrah. Abd al-Wahhab said: And her husband was Hilal ibn Murrah al-Ashja'i."
"4278","Bahz and Affan both said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Khilas and Abu Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, that dispute was brought to Ibn Mas'ud concerning a woman whom a man married then died, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Al-Jarrah and Abu Sinan stood and testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with it among them, among al-Ashja' ibn Rayth, concerning Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'iyyah, and her husband's name was Hilal ibn Marwan. Affan said: He judged with it among them, among al-Ashja' ibn Rayth, concerning Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'iyyah, and her husband was Hilal ibn Marwan."
"4279","Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Days will not end nor time pass until a man from my household rules the Arabs, whose name corresponds to my name."
"4280","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right until the whiteness of his cheek appeared, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek appeared, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"4281","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim — and another than him said: from Alqamah — he said: Abdullah said: While we were in the mosque on Friday night, an Ansari man said: By Allah, if a man finds a man with his wife and speaks, he will surely be lashed; and if he kills him, he will surely be killed; and if he remains silent, he will surely remain silent in anger. By Allah, in the morning I shall surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In the morning he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if a man finds a man with his wife and speaks, he will surely be lashed; and if he kills him, he will surely be killed; and if he remains silent, he will surely remain silent in anger. And he kept saying: O Allah, open; O Allah, open. He said: Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed: And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves, the verse."
"4282","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah mentioning, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that he informed them, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five rak'ahs with them then turned away. Some people began whispering to others, and they said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five. So he turned away, prostrated two prostrations with them, gave salam, and said: I am only a human; I forget as you forget."
"4283","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the tattooing woman and the woman who seeks tattooing, the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom hair is joined, the muhill and the one for whom tahleel is done, and the eater of riba and its payer."
"4284","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the tattooing woman and the woman who seeks tattooing, the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom hair is joined, the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done, and the eater of riba and its feeder."
"4285","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Which deeds are best? He said: Prayers at their proper times, kindness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"4286","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from a man, from Amr ibn Wabisah al-Asadi, from his father, he said: I was in Kufah in my house when I heard at the door of the house: Peace be upon you, may I enter? I said: Upon you be peace, then enter. When he entered, there was Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what time of visit is this? That was at midday. He said: The day grew long for me, so I remembered someone to talk to. He began narrating to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I narrated to him. He said: Then he began narrating to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a tribulation; the sleeper in it is better than the one lying down, the one lying down in it is better than the one sitting, the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, the one standing in it is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the rider, and the rider is better than the one galloping. All its slain are in the Fire. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when is that? He said: That is during the days of Harj. I said: When are the days of Harj? He said: When a man does not feel safe with his companion. I said: What do you command me if I reach that? He said: Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a man enters upon me in my house? He said: Then enter your inner room. He said: I said: What if he enters upon me in my inner room? He said: Then enter your mosque and do like this — and he clasped his right hand upon the wrist — and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that."
"4287","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah — meaning Ibn al-Mubarak — informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Amr ibn Wabisah al-Asadi."
"4288","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrated to me that Shaqiq ibn Salamah said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: How bad it is for a man — or: for a person — to say: I forgot surah such-and-such and such-and-such, or verse such-and-such and such-and-such; rather, he was made to forget."
"4289","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-A'mash, concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord: Ibn Mas'ud said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a green canopy from Paradise that had covered the horizon. He mentioned it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"4290","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, that he heard Ibrahim narrating, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I took a woman in the garden and did everything with her except that I did not have intercourse with her; I kissed her and clung to her and did nothing other than that, so do with me whatever you wish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said nothing to him. The man left, and Umar said: Allah had covered him; had he covered himself. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed him with his gaze and said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back to him, and he recited to him: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds, up to: for those who remember. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: Is it for him alone or for people in general, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Rather, for people in general."
"4291","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, and he mentioned the hadith."
"4292","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Isra'il informed us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his people in wrongdoing is like a camel fallen into a well, pulling at its tail."
"4293","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I departed with Ibn Mas'ud from Arafah. When he came to Muzdalifah, he prayed Maghrib and Isha, each of them with an adhan and iqamah, and he placed dinner between them. Then he slept. When someone said: Dawn has risen, he prayed Fajr. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two prayers have been delayed from their times in this place: as for Maghrib, people do not come here until it is dark; and as for Fajr, this is its time. Then he stood, and when dawn brightened he said: If the Commander of the Believers is correct, he will depart now. He said: Abdullah had not finished his speech before Uthman departed."
"4294","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: My father informed me, from Mina, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the delegation of the jinn. When he turned away, he breathed deeply, and I said: What is the matter with you? He said: My death has been announced to me, O Ibn Mas'ud."
"4295","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command a man to lead people in prayer, then look and burn down the houses of a people who do not attend Friday prayer."
"4296","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Fazarah al-Absi, he said: Abu Zayd, freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, narrated to us, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: On the night of the jinn, two men among them stayed behind and said: We shall witness Fajr with you, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do you have water with you? I said: I do not have water with me, but I have a waterskin containing nabidh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good date and pure water. So he performed ablution."
"4297","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They stay behind from Friday prayer; I intended to command my youths to bundle firewood, then command a man to lead people, and burn down the houses of a people who do not attend Friday prayer."
"4298","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from al-Qasim, from his father, that al-Walid ibn Uqbah once delayed the prayer. Abdullah ibn Mas'ud stood and called for prayer and prayed with people. Al-Walid sent to him: What carried you to do what you did? Has an order come to you from the Commander of the Believers concerning what you did, or did you innovate? He said: No order came to me from the Commander of the Believers, nor did I innovate; but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger refused for us to wait for you with our prayer while you attend to your need."
"4299","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself and ordered Ibn Mas'ud to bring him three stones. He brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He threw away the dung and said: It is filth; bring me a stone."
"4300","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Dinar narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I did not fast with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine days more often than I fasted with him thirty days."
"4301","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to me, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd the freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me, ""Do you have any water for purification with you?"" I said, ""No."" He said, ""Then what is this in the waterskin?"" I said, ""Nabidh."" He said, ""Show it to me. A wholesome date and pure water."" Then he performed ablution from it and prayed."
"4302","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed me, from Qays, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we had no wives. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate ourselves?"" So he forbade us from that, and he said, ""O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you"" the verse."
"4303","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning the blood money for accidental killing: twenty bint makhad, twenty ibn makhad, twenty bint labun, twenty hiqqah, and twenty jadha'ah."
"4304","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, ""Whoever sees me in a dream, it is indeed me whom he has seen, for Satan cannot take my likeness."""
"4305","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, who said: Alqamah took my hand; he said: Abdullah took my hand; he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my hand and taught me the tashahhud in prayer: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"4306","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Sulayman, from Shaqiq, who said: I was with Abdullah and Abu Musa while they were conversing, and they mentioned from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, ""Before the Hour there will be days in which knowledge is taken away, ignorance descends, and harj becomes abundant."" He said: They said, Harj is killing."
"4307","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: We journeyed by night with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, if only we touched the ground and slept while our mounts grazed."" He said: So he did so. He said: Then he said, ""Let some of you guard us."" Abdullah said: So I said, ""I will guard you."" He said: Then sleep overcame me and I slept; I did not wake until the sun had risen, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not wake except at our talking. Then he ordered Bilal, who called the adhan, then called the iqamah for prayer, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer."
"4308","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu al-Wasil, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, ""Cursed is the muhallil and the one for whom tahlil is done."""
"4309","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: They used to recite behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said, ""You have confused the Qur'an for me."""
"4310","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""None shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride."""
"4311","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, who said: I visited Ibn Mas'ud, I and my uncle, at midday. He said: Then he called for prayer, and we stood behind him. He said: Then he took me by one hand and my uncle by the other hand. He said: Then he brought us forward until he placed each man of us on one side. Then he said, ""This is what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do when they were three."""
"4312","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father Ibn Mas'ud, who said: While a man among those before you was in his kingdom, he reflected and realized that it would be cut off from him, and that what he was in had distracted him from worshipping his Lord. So he slipped away and stole out one night from his palace, and by morning he was in another kingdom. He came to the seashore, where he used to mold bricks for hire, eating from it and giving the surplus in charity. He remained so until his affair, his worship, and his merit rose to their king. Their king sent to him to come to him, but he refused to come to him. He repeated, then repeated to him, but he refused to come to him, saying, ""What has he to do with me, and what have I to do with him?"" He said: So the king rode out. When the man saw him he turned and fled. When the king saw that, he galloped after him but did not catch him. He said: Then he called to him, ""O servant of Allah, you have nothing to fear from me."" So he stopped until he caught up with him. He said to him, ""Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?"" He said, ""I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, owner of such-and-such a kingdom. I reflected on my affair and realized that what I was in would be cut off, for it had distracted me from worshipping my Lord, so I left it and came here to worship my Lord, mighty and majestic."" He said, ""You are no more in need of what you have done than I am."" He said: Then he dismounted from his beast and let it loose, then followed him. They both worshipped Allah, mighty and majestic, together. They supplicated Allah to cause them both to die together. He said: So they both died. He said: Had I been at Rumaylat Misr I would have shown you their graves by the description the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, described to us."
"4313","Yazid and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best?"" He said, ""Prayer at its appointed time."" He said: I said, ""Then what, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""Kindness to parents."" He said: I said, ""Then what, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""Jihad in the path of Allah."" He said: Then I fell silent, and had I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for more, he would have given me more."
"4314","Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Abu Muhammad the freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""No two Muslims lose three of their children before they reach the age of accountability but that they will be for them a strong fortress against the Fire."" He said: Then Abu Dharr said, ""Two of mine have died, O Messenger of Allah."" He said, ""And two."" He said: Then Ubayy Abu al-Mundhir, the chief of the reciters, said, ""One of mine has died, O Messenger of Allah."" Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""And one, and that is at the first shock."""
"4315","Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then by the way of those who perished, and if they remain, their religion will remain for them seventy years."""
"4316","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, from Abdullah, who said: My father - Shu'bah raised it to the Prophet and I do not raise it for you - concerning the word of Allah, mighty and majestic, ""and whoever intends therein deviation through wrongdoing, We shall make him taste a painful punishment"": Had a man intended deviation therein while in Adan Abyan, Allah would make him taste a painful punishment."
"4317","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how will you know those of your ummah whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection?"" He said, ""They will be radiant, white-marked, piebald from the traces of ablution."""
"4318","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, Abu Salamah al-Juhani narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""No servant ever says, when anxiety and grief befall him: O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant; my forelock is in Your hand; Your decree concerning me is carried out; Your judgment concerning me is just; I ask You by every name of Yours by which You have named Yourself, or sent down in Your Book, or taught to any of Your creation, or kept to Yourself in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Qur'an the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the dispeller of my sorrow, and the remover of my anxiety, but that Allah, mighty and majestic, removes his anxiety and replaces his grief with joy."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we ought to learn these words."" He said, ""Yes, whoever hears them ought to learn them."""
"4319","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yazid informed us, Farqad al-Sabakhi narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Yazid narrated to us that he heard Masruq narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, ""I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them; and I forbade you to keep sacrificial meat beyond three days, so keep it; and I forbade you vessels for nabidh, so make nabidh in them, but avoid every intoxicant."""
"4320","Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadham, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, ""Allah, mighty and majestic, has angels roaming the earth who convey to me the greetings of my ummah."""
"4321","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn and Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, Muslim al-Batin narrated to me, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Ibn Mas'ud hardly ever missed a Thursday - Ibn Abi Adi said: a Thursday evening - but that I came to him. He said: I never heard him say of anything at all, ""The Messenger of Allah said,"" until one evening he said, ""The Messenger of Allah said"" - Ibn Abi Adi said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say - then he lowered his head. He said: So I looked at him as he stood with the buttons of his shirt undone, his eyes filled with tears and his jugular veins swollen, and he said, ""Or less than that, or more than that, or close to that, or like that."""
"4322","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me Surat al-Ahqaf, and he taught another man, who differed with me in a verse of it. So I said, ""Who taught you?"" He said, ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me."" So I said to him, ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me such-and-such."" Then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with him was a man. So I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, did you not teach me such-and-such?"" He said, ""Yes."" The other said, ""Did you not teach me such-and-such?"" He said, ""Yes."" Then the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed color. Then the man who was with him said, ""Let each of you recite as he heard, for those before you perished only through disagreement."" I do not know whether he ordered him with that or said something of his own."
"4323","Abu Dawud and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mawriq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, ""Congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five prayers, each like his prayer."" Affan said: It reached me that Abu al-Awwam agreed with him."
"4324","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the like of it."
"4325","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from his maternal uncle, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that a man said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ""I met a woman in a garden in Madinah and I took from her what is short of intercourse."" Then was revealed, ""And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night."""
"4326","Abu Qatan narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, When is Laylat al-Qadr? He said, Who among you remembers the night of al-Sahbawat? Abdullah said, I, may my father and mother be ransom for you, and in my hand were dates with which I was warming myself, sheltering from the dawn behind my saddle, and that was when the little moon had risen."
"4327","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah and Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of riba and its giver and its two witnesses and its writer."
"4328","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us, How will you be when a quarter of the people of Paradise is yours, a fourth of it, and three fourths for the rest of mankind? They said, Allah and His Messenger know best. He said, Then how will you be when a third of it is yours? They said, Then that is more. He said, Then how will you be when half is yours? They said, Then that is more. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, The people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will be one hundred and twenty rows, you among them eighty rows."
"4329","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, that they said, O Messenger of Allah, how will you know those of your ummah whom you have not seen? He said, Radiant, white-marked, piebald from the trace of purification."
"4330","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy surahs, and none disputes me in them."
"4331","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: A man of the Ansar spoke a word showing resentment toward the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and my soul would not let me rest until I told it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I wished I had ransomed myself from it with all family and wealth. Then he said, Musa was harmed with more than that and was patient. Then he told that a prophet was belied by his people and wounded when he came to them with the command of Allah, and he said while wiping blood from his face, O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"4332","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I am your forerunner at the Hawd, and men will be contested with me and I will be overcome over them, and I will surely say, Lord, my companions, my companions, and it will surely be said to me, You do not know what they innovated after you."
"4333","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Firas, from Amir, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: Perhaps he narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would stumble and his color would change while he said, Like this, or close to this."
"4334","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Allah, mighty and majestic, has not sent down a disease but He has sent down with it a cure. And Affan once said, but He has sent down for it a cure. Whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"4335","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the foot of a mountain while he stood praying and they were asleep. He said: When a snake passed by him we woke while he said, What protected her from you is what protected you from her. And there was sent down upon him, By those sent forth in succession, by the violent winds. So I took it while it was moist from his mouth, or his mouth moist with it."
"4336","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Hunayn. He said: The people turned away from him, and eighty men of the Muhajirun and Ansar stood firm with him. Then we stepped back on our feet about eighty paces, and we did not turn our backs to them, and they are those upon whom Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down tranquility. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on his mule going forward, then his mule swerved with him and he leaned from the saddle. So I said to him, Rise up, may Allah raise you. He said, Hand me a handful of dust. Then he struck their faces with it, and their eyes filled with dust. Then he said, Where are the Muhajirun and Ansar? I said, Here they are. He said, Call out to them. So I called out to them, and they came with their swords in their right hands as if they were shooting stars, and the polytheists turned their backs."
"4337","Affan and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hasan said: from Ata, and Affan said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Mas'ud, Hasan said: Ibn Mas'ud narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, There will be a people in the Fire as long as Allah wills them to be, then Allah will have mercy on them and bring them out of it, and they will be in the lowest Paradise. Then they will bathe in a river called al-Hayawan. The people of Paradise will call them al-Jahannamiyyun. If one of them hosted the people of the world he would spread carpets for them and feed them and give them drink and cover them, and I think he said, and marry them off. Hasan said: That does not diminish him anything."
"4338","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, raising the hadith to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
"4339","Affan and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, The nations were shown to me at the season, and my ummah came slowly upon me. He said: Then I saw them, and their multitude and appearance pleased me; they had filled the plain and the mountain. Hasan said: Then he said, Are you pleased, O Muhammad? So I said, Yes. He said: Then for you with these. Affan and Hasan said: Then he said, O Muhammad, with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning, and they are those who do not seek ruqyah nor take omens nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they rely. Then Ukkashah stood and said, O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them, so he supplicated for him. Then another stood and said, O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them, and he said, Ukkashah has preceded you with it."
"4340","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the mosque while he was between Abu Bakr and Umar, and Ibn Mas'ud was praying, reciting al-Nisa, and he had reached the head of a hundred. Then Ibn Mas'ud began to supplicate while standing in prayer. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Ask, you will be given, ask, you will be given. Then he said, Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was sent down, let him recite it by the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. In the morning Abu Bakr went to him to give him glad tidings, and said to him, What did you ask Allah last night? He said, I said, O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not apostatize, and bliss that does not end, and companionship of Muhammad in the highest eternal Paradise. Then Umar came, and it was said to him, Abu Bakr has preceded you. He said, May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr, I never raced him to any good but he preceded me to it."
"4341","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him between Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, then he mentioned like it."
"4342","Affan narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, Some eloquence is magic, and the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes alive, and those who take their graves as mosques."
"4343","Affan narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah, who said: May Allah curse tattooing women and plucking women and gapping women and women changing the creation of Allah. Then he said, Shall I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed? Then a woman of Banu Asad said, I think it is in your family. So he said to her, Go and look. So she went and looked, then said, I saw nothing in them. And I did not see it in the mushaf. He said, Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it."
"4344","Abu Abd al-Rahman said, Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, like it."
"4345","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zubayd and Mansur and Sulayman, they informed me that they heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, Insulting a Muslim is fisq, and fighting him is kufr. Zubayd said: I said to Abu Wa'il twice, Did you hear it from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said, Yes."
"4346","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, who said: Abdullah said, I visited the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he had a fever, so I placed my hand on him and said, You have a severe fever. He said, I am afflicted as two men of you are afflicted. He said: I said, That is because for you are two rewards. He said, Yes, no believer is afflicted by illness or anything else but Allah drops his sins thereby as a tree drops its leaves."
"4347","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, who said: I and Alqamah visited Abdullah ibn Mas'ud at midday. When the sun declined he called for prayer, and we stood behind him. Then he took my hand and my companion's hand and made us at his two sides, and stood between us. Then he said, This is what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do when they were three. Then he prayed with us, and when he finished he said, There will be imams who delay prayer from its times, so do not wait for them with it, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"4348","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I am only a human, I forget as you forget, so whichever of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the most likely correct, complete upon it, and prostrate two prostrations."
"4349","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: al-Ash'ath ibn Qays visited Abdullah while he was eating lunch, and said, O Abu Muhammad, come to lunch. He said, Is today not the day of Ashura? He said, What is it? He said, It is only a day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast before Ramadan, then when the month of Ramadan was revealed it was left."
"4350","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah, who said: I know the paired surahs the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite, two in a rak'ah."
"4351","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I am your forerunner at the Hawd, and men will surely be snatched away from me, so I shall say, O Lord, my companions, and it will be said, You do not know what they innovated after you."
"4352","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: When When the help of Allah and the victory comes was revealed, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would often say, Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me, You are indeed the Oft-Returning."
"4353","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Rafi', from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of the jinn drew a line around him, and one of them would come like the darkness of palm trees, and said to me, Do not leave your place. Then he recited to them the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, and when he saw al-Zutt he said, As if they are these. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Do you have water with you? I said, No. He said, Do you have nabidh with you? I said, Yes. So he performed ablution with it."
"4354","Abu Sa'id and Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ja'far, said: from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Had I taken a close friend from my ummah, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."
"4355","Abu Qatan narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers where they are called, for Allah, mighty and majestic, has legislated the ways of guidance for His Prophet, and they are among the ways of guidance, and I think none of you but has a mosque in which he prays in his house. Had you prayed in your houses and left your mosques, you would have left the sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and had you left the sunnah of your Prophet, you would have gone astray."
"4356","Abu Qatan narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: When When the help of Allah and the victory comes was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would often say, Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me, You are indeed the Oft-Returning. O Allah, forgive me, glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me, glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise."
"4357","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a cave, and By those sent forth in succession had been sent down upon him. He said: We were taking it moist from his mouth when a snake came out upon us, so he said, Kill it. He said: So we rushed to kill it, but it outran us. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Allah protected it from your evil as He protected you from its evil."
"4358","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forgot in prayer and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speaking."
"4359","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah from the belly of the valley with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble. It was said to him, Some people stone it from above it. Then he said, This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the One upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."
"4360","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah, who said: The moon split while we were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina, until a part of it went behind the mountain. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Bear witness."
"4361","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, He is not of us who strikes cheeks, or tears garments, or calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."
"4362","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Nahshal, from Abu Wa'il, who said: Abdullah said, Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, surpassed people in four: by his mention of the captives on the day of Badr, he ordered their killing, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down, Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took; and by his mention of the hijab, he ordered the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to veil, so Zaynab said to him, And you watch us, O son of al-Khattab, while revelation descends in our houses, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down, And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil; and by the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him, O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar; and by his opinion concerning Abu Bakr, he was the first of the people to pledge him."
"4363","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Asim, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Amir ibn al-Simt, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, There will be rulers after me who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded."
"4364","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, who said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah al-Hilali narrating from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard a man recite a verse of which I had heard the opposite from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I took him and brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then I recognized dislike in the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said, Both of you are good, do not differ. The greatest of my knowledge, Mis'ar said: He mentioned therein, Do not differ, for those before you differed and perished."
"4365","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Talhah, narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, who said: The polytheists detained the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Asr prayer until the sun turned yellow or red, so he said, They distracted us from the middle prayer, may Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire, or may Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire."
"4366","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided the spoils of Hunayn at al-Ji'irranah, they crowded him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, A servant among the servants of Allah whom Allah sent to his people, and they struck him and wounded him. He said: So he began wiping blood from his forehead and saying, Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know. Abdullah said: As if I look at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping blood from his forehead, recounting the man and saying, Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"4367","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: A man of Ahl al-Suffah died, and they found two dinars in his wrap, and they mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said, Two brands."
"4368","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: A rabbi came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, O Muhammad, or O Messenger of Allah, Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection will carry the heavens on a finger, the earths on a finger, the mountains on a finger, the trees on a finger, the water and soil on a finger, and the rest of creation on a finger, shaking them and saying, I am the King. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his molars appeared, confirming the rabbi's word, then recited, And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves, and the earth entirely will be His grasp on the Day of Resurrection, to the end of the verse."
"4369","Aswad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, and he mentioned it with its chain and meaning, and said, Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed until his molar appeared, confirming his word."
"4370","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah stoned the Jamrah in the belly of the valley. I said, People do not stone from here. He said, This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the One upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."
"4371","Yunus narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walking, he passed boys playing, among them Ibn Sayyad, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, May your hands be dusted, do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? So he said, Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said, Let me strike his neck. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, If he is the one you fear, you will not be able to."
"4372","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventy surahs, none disputes me in them."
"4373","Yunus narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said, Let those of understanding and intellect stand nearest me, then those next to them, then those next to them, and do not differ lest your hearts differ, and beware the tumults of the markets."
"4374","Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Khalid who was among Banu Dalan, Yazid al-Wasiti, narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Abu Aqrab al-Asadi, who said: I came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and found him on his rooftop, meaning a surface, and I heard him say, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. So I climbed to him and said, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why did you say, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth? He said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told us that Laylat al-Qadr is in the middle of the last seven, and the sun rises on its morning without rays. He said: So I climbed and looked at it, then said, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth."
"4375","Attab narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah informed us, Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah informed us, he said: I heard my father say, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him on the night of the jinn with a stale bone and dung and charcoal, and said, Do not clean yourself with anything of this when you go out to the privy."
"4376","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Mukhariq ibn Abdullah al-Ahmasi, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, I witnessed of al-Miqdad a scene that, were I its owner, would be dearer to me than anything on earth. He said: He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a horseman, and said, Rejoice, O Prophet of Allah, by Allah we shall not say to you as Banu Isra'il said to Musa, Go you and your Lord and fight, we sit here, but by the One who sent you with the truth, we shall surely be before you and on your right and on your left and behind you until Allah grants you victory."
"4377","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: By those sent forth in succession was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of the snake. He said: So we said to him, What is the night of the snake, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hira by night, a snake came out upon us from the mountain, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to kill it. We sought it but it eluded us. Then he said, Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your evil as He protected you from its evil."
"4378","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: I stood with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud before the Jamrah, and when he stood before it he said, This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the One upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down, the day he stoned it. He said: Then Abdullah ibn Mas'ud stoned it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble he threw, then left."
"4379","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Harith, I think meaning Ibn Fudayl, from Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar, from Abu Rafi', from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, No prophet Allah, mighty and majestic, sent before me to an ummah but had among his ummah disciples and companions who took his sunnah and followed his command, then after them come successors who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded."
"4380","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among nearly eighty men of Quraysh, none but a Qurashi, by Allah I never saw the surface of men's faces more handsome than their faces that day, they mentioned women and talked about them, and he talked with them until I wished he would fall silent. He said: Then I came to him, and he gave the testimony then said, To proceed, O company of Quraysh, you are the people of this affair so long as you do not disobey Allah, but when you disobey Him He will send to you one who will peel you as this stick is peeled, for a stick in his hand. Then he peeled his stick, and it was white, gleaming."
"4381","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Umays Utbah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd the freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth al-Makhzumi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Makkah, he among a group of his companions, he said, Let a man of you stand with me, and no man in whose heart is a speck of treachery shall stand with me. He said: So I stood with him, and I took a waterskin, thinking it only water. I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until when we were at the heights of Makkah I saw black shapes gathered. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drew a line for me, then said, Stand here until I come to you. He said: So I stood, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to them, and I saw them crowding toward him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conversed with them long into the night until he came to me at dawn, and said to me, Have you remained standing, O Ibn Mas'ud? He said: So I said, O Messenger of Allah, did you not say to me, Stand until I come to you? He said: Then he said to me, Do you have any water for ablution? He said: So I said, Yes. Then I opened the waterskin, and it was nabidh. He said: So I said to him, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I took the waterskin thinking it only water, and it is nabidh. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, A wholesome date and pure water. He said: Then he performed ablution from it. When he stood to pray, two persons of them caught up with him and said to him, O Messenger of Allah, we love that you lead us in our prayer. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arranged them behind him, then prayed with us. When he finished I said to him, Who are these, O Messenger of Allah? He said, These are the jinn of Nasibin, they came disputing to me over matters between them, and they asked me for provision, so I provided them. He said: So I said to him, Do you have with you, O Messenger of Allah, anything to provide them? He said: Then he said, I have provided them with droppings and bones: whatever dung they find they find as barley, and whatever bone they find they find clothed with meat. He said: And thereupon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade cleaning with dung and bone."
"4382","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me concerning the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the middle of prayer and at its end, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me the tashahhud in the middle of prayer and at its end, and we would memorize from Abdullah when he told us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught it to him. He said: He would say when he sat in the middle of prayer and at its end, on his left haunch: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: Then if he was in the middle of prayer he rose when he finished his tashahhud, and if he was at its end he supplicated after his tashahhud whatever Allah willed him to supplicate, then gave salutation."
"4383","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me concerning the departure of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, from his father, I heard a man asking Abdullah ibn Mas'ud about the departure of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from his prayer, whether he departed to his right or to his left. He said: Then Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, departed where he wished; the most frequent departure of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from his prayer was on his left side to his chamber."
"4384","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to him that al-Aswad narrated to him that Ibn Mas'ud narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, most often departed from prayer on his left to the chambers."
"4385","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrated to us, from one who narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with him on Friday in the mosque of Kufah, with Ammar ibn Yasir governor over Kufah for Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud over the treasury, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud looked at the shadow and saw it the measure of a sandal strap, and said, If your companion hits the sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he will come out now. He said: By Allah, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud had not finished his speech until Ammar ibn Yasir came out saying, Prayer."
"4386","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from his father, who said: My uncle Alqamah and I visited Abdullah ibn Mas'ud at midday. He said: Then he called the Zuhr to pray, and we stood behind him. Then he took my hand and my uncle's hand, then made one of us on his right and the other on his left, then stood between us, and we lined behind him in one row. He said: Then he said, This is what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do when they were three. He said: Then he prayed with us, and when he bowed he joined his fingers and stuck his forearms to his thighs and inserted his palms between his knees. He said: When he gave salutation he turned to us and said, There will be imams who delay prayer from its times, so when they do that do not wait for them with it, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"4387","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Ansari then al-Khatmi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja al-Sulami, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of Uthman ibn Affan, with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud in Madinah. He said: Then Uthman went out and prayed with the people that prayer, two rak'ahs with two prostrations in each rak'ah. He said: Then Uthman left and entered his house, and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud sat by the chamber of A'ishah, and we sat with him. Then he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to pray at the eclipse of the sun and the moon, so when you see it afflict them, hasten to prayer, for if it is what you fear, you will be not heedless, and if it is not, you will have attained good and earned it."
"4388","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father informed us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the two rak'ahs as if on hot stones. Sa'd said: I said to my father, Until he stands? He said, Until he stands."
"4389","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the two rak'ahs as if on hot stones, and perhaps he said the first two. He said: I said to my father, Until he stands? He said, Until he stands. My father said."
"4390","And Nuh ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the two rak'ahs as if on hot stones. He said: I said to my father, Until he stands? He said, Until he stands."
"4391","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, The last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise and the last of the people of the Fire to exit the Fire is a man who exits the Fire crawling, and Allah, mighty and majestic, says to him, Go and enter Paradise. Then he comes to it and it appears to him as if it is full, so he returns and says, O Lord, I found it full. Then He says, Go and enter Paradise. Then he comes to it and it appears to him as if it is full, so he returns and says, O Lord, I found it full. Then He says, Go and enter Paradise. Then he comes to it and it appears to him as if it is full, so he returns to Him and says, O Lord, I found it full, three times. Then He says, Go, for you is the like of the world and ten times its like, or ten times the like of the world. He said: He says, Lord, do You laugh at me while You are the King? He said: And it was said, This is the lowest of the people of Paradise in station."
"4392","Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, There is none but has assigned to him his companion of the jinn. They said, And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said, And I, except that Allah aided me over him and he submitted, so he orders me only with good."
"4393","He said, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: And Abdullah heard of a land subsidence. He said: We, the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to count signs as blessing, while you count them as fright. While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with no water with us, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us, Seek who has with him, meaning water. So we did, and water was brought, and he poured it into a vessel, then placed his palms, and water began to gush from between his fingers. Then he said, Come to the blessed purification, and blessing is from Allah. So I filled my belly from it, and the people drank. Abdullah said: We used to hear the food glorifying Allah while it was eaten."
"4394","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, A Muslim fighting his brother is kufr, and insulting him is fisq."
"4395","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, A woman shall not touch a woman and describe her to her husband, or depict her to her husband, or to a man, as if he looks at her. And when there are three, two shall not converse privately excluding their companion, for that grieves him. And whoever swears a false oath to cut thereby the wealth of his brother, or he said the wealth of a Muslim man, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. He said: Then al-Ash'ath ibn Qays heard Ibn Mas'ud narrating this and said, Concerning me the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that, and concerning a man with whom we disputed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over a well."
"4396","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, concerning this verse, And he surely saw him another descent, by the Lote Tree of the Utmost, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I saw Jibril, with six hundred wings, scattering from his feathers marvels, pearls and rubies."
"4397","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays, and he did not hear it from him, and a man asked him about the hadith of Alqamah, and it is this hadith, that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud came to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari in his house, and prayer came, so Abu Musa said, Step forward, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for you are older and more knowledgeable. He said, No, rather step forward, for we came to you in your house and your mosque, so you are more entitled. He said: Then Abu Musa stepped forward and removed his sandals. When he gave salutation he said, What did you intend by removing them? Are you in the sacred valley? I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in khuffs and sandals."
"4398","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, he heard it from him, from Abdullah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning people who stay behind from Friday, I have intended to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn down the houses of men who stay behind from Friday."
"4399","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid say, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud performed Hajj, and Alqamah ordered me to stay with him, so I stayed with him, and I was with him, and he mentioned the hadith. When dawn rose he said, Call the iqamah. So I said, Abu Abd al-Rahman, this is an hour I never saw you pray in. He said: He said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray this hour except this prayer in this place on this day. Abdullah said: They are two prayers shifted from their times, Maghrib prayer after the people come to Muzdalifah, and dawn prayer when dawn bursts. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do that."
"4400","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Hudayj, brother of Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us to al-Najashi, we about eighty men, among them Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and Ja'far and Abdullah ibn Urfutah and Uthman ibn Maz'un and Abu Musa. They came to al-Najashi, and Quraysh sent Amr ibn al-As and Umarah ibn al-Walid with a gift. When they entered upon al-Najashi they prostrated to him, then hastened to him on his right and his left, then said to him, Some men of our cousins have settled your land and turned away from us and our religion. He said: Then where are they? He said: They are in your land, so send to them. So he sent to them. Then Ja'far said, I am your spokesman today, so follow me. Then he gave salutation and did not prostrate. They said to him, Why do you not prostrate to the king? He said, We prostrate only to Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: And what is that? He said, Allah, mighty and majestic, sent to us His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ordered us not to prostrate to anyone but Allah, mighty and majestic, and ordered us with prayer and zakah. Amr ibn al-As said: Then they oppose you concerning Isa son of Maryam. He said: What do you say concerning Isa son of Maryam and his mother? They said: We say as Allah, mighty and majestic, said: He is the word of Allah and His spirit, cast to the chaste virgin whom no man touched and no child imposed upon. He said: Then he raised a stick from the ground, then said, O company of Abyssinians and priests and monks, by Allah they add not to what we say concerning him more than this. Welcome to you and to him from whom you came. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah, for he is the one we find in the Gospel, and he is the Messenger whom Isa son of Maryam gave glad tidings of. Settle where you wish. By Allah, were it not for what I am in of kingship, I would come to him until I carry his sandals and perform his ablution. And he ordered the gift of the other two, and it was returned to them. Then Abdullah ibn Mas'ud hastened until he caught Badr, and he claimed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought forgiveness for him when his death reached him."
"4401","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I saw a man ask al-Aswad ibn Yazid while he was teaching the Quran in the mosque, and he said: How do we recite this word, is there any that will remember, with dhal or with dal, so he said: No, rather with dal, then he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite it muddakir with dal."
"4402","Abu Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar, meaning al-Makhrami, narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abu Rafi, he said: Ibn Masud told me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was never any prophet at all but he had among his companions disciples and companions who follow his example and take guidance from his guidance, then there comes after that successors, rulers who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded."
"4403","Muhammad ibn Abdullah Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined, and the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done, and the tattooing woman and the tattooed woman, and the eater of usury and the one who feeds it."
"4404","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Razin, from Ibn Masud, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the cave, and Wal-mursalati urfa was revealed to him, so I recited it close to what he had taught me, except that I do not know with which of the two verses he ended."
"4405","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq said, he informed us, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited Surat al-Najm and prostrated, and no one of the people remained but prostrated except a man who lifted a handful of pebbles and placed it on his face and said: This suffices me. Abdullah said: I saw him after that killed as a disbeliever."
"4406","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one phrase and I say another: Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to the Fire. And Abdullah said: And I say: Whoever dies while not setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to Paradise."
"4407","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrate from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him. And a woman should not touch a woman and then describe her to her husband as if he were looking at her."
"4408","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrate from Abdullah, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, do you see what we did in idolatry, shall we be taken to account for it. He said: Whoever of you does well in Islam will not be taken to account for what he did in idolatry, and whoever of you does badly in Islam will be taken to account for what he did in idolatry and Islam."
"4409","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, that he said: I am told of your gathering, but my coming out to you is prevented by fear of boring you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit us at intervals in the days with admonition for fear of weariness upon us."
"4410","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil narrated to us, from Abu Wail, he said: We came early to Abdullah ibn Masud one day after the morning prayer, and we greeted at the door, and we were given permission, then a man of the people said: I recited all the Mufassal last night. So he said: Like chanting poetry in haste. We have heard the recitation, and I remember the pairs that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite together, eighteen surahs of the Mufassal and two surahs of Al Ha-Mim."
"4411","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest. He said: That you set up a rival to Allah though He created you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what. He said: Then that you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor."
"4412","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, that he said: I was a young boy herding sheep for Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, came, and they had fled from the idolaters, and they said: O boy, do you have any milk to give us to drink. I said: I am entrusted and I will not give you drink. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you have a young she-goat upon which the male has not mounted. I said: Yes. So I brought it to them, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held it and wiped the udder and supplicated, and the udder filled, then Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed stone, and he milked into it, and he drank, and Abu Bakr drank, then I drank, then he said to the udder: Shrink, and it shrank. Then I came to him after that and said: Teach me of this speech. He said: You are a taught boy. He said: So I took from his mouth seventy surahs in which no one disputes me."
"4413","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Had I been taking a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but my brother and my companion, and Allah has taken your companion as a close friend."
"4414","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Masud, that the women were on the day of Uhud behind the Muslims finishing off the wounded of the idolaters, so had I sworn that day I would hope to be truthful, that there was none of us who wanted this world, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Among you are some who desire this world and among you are some who desire the Hereafter, then He turned you away from them to test you. Then when the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, differed and disobeyed what they were commanded, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was left alone among nine, seven of the Ansar and two men of Quraysh, and he was the tenth of them. Then when they pressed upon him, he said: May Allah have mercy on a man who repels them from us. He said: So a man of the Ansar stood and fought for a while until he was killed, then when they pressed upon him again, he said: May Allah have mercy on a man who repels them from us. He kept saying that until the seven were killed. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his two companions: We have not done justice to our companions. Then Abu Sufyan came and said: Exalted be Hubal. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: Allah is Highest and Most Majestic. So they said: Allah is Highest and Most Majestic. Then Abu Sufyan said: We have al-Uzza and you have no al-Uzza. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: Allah is our Protector and the disbelievers have no protector. Then Abu Sufyan said: A day for the day of Badr, a day for us and a day against us, and a day we grieve and a day we rejoice, Hanzalah for Hanzalah, and so-and-so for so-and-so, and so-and-so for so-and-so. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Not equal. As for our slain, they are alive, provided for, and your slain are in the Fire, tormented. Abu Sufyan said: There was mutilation among the people, and it was without the approval of our chiefs. I neither ordered nor forbade, nor loved nor hated, nor was I displeased nor pleased. He said: So they looked, and Hamzah had his belly cut open, and Hind took his liver and chewed it but could not eat it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did she eat any of it. They said: No. He said: Allah would not admit anything of Hamzah into the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed Hamzah and prayed over him, and a man of the Ansar was brought and placed beside him, and he prayed over him, then the Ansari was lifted and Hamzah was left, then another was brought and placed beside Hamzah, and he prayed over him, then he was lifted and Hamzah was left, until he prayed over him that day seventy prayers."
"4415","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do you know which charity is best. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The gift of use, that one of you lend his brother the dirham, or the back of the mount, or the milk of the sheep, or the milk of the cow."
"4416","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, and Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How bad for one of them, or one of you, to say: I forgot verse such and such, rather he was made to forget. And memorize the Quran by heart, for it slips away from the breasts of men faster than camels from their halters. He said, or he said: from its halter."
"4417","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, narrating from Abdullah, he said: We used to speak in prayer, then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and greeted him, and he did not return it to me, so I was seized by old distress and new. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah introduces for His Prophet what He wills. Shubah said: And I think he said: of what He wills. And among what He introduced for His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is that you not speak in prayer."
"4418","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr five, so they said: Has the prayer been increased. So he prostrated two prostrations."
"4419","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur narrate from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no staying up talking at night except for two men, or for one of two men: for one praying and for a traveler."
"4420","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, he said: A man asked Abu Musa al-Ashari about a woman who left her daughter and the daughter of her son and her sister, so he said: Half to the daughter and half to the sister, and he said: Go to Ibn Masud, for he will follow me. He said: So they came to Ibn Masud and told him of the saying of Abu Musa, so he said: I would be astray then and I would not be of the guided. I shall surely judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Shubah said: I found this word written: I shall surely judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: To the daughter is half, and to the son's daughter is the sixth completing the two-thirds, and what remains is to the sister. So they came to Abu Musa and told him of the saying of Ibn Masud, so Abu Musa said: Do not ask me about anything while this scholar is among you."
"4421","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud say: We came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from al-Hudaybiyah, and they mentioned that they camped in a low soft land, meaning dahas is sand, so he said: Who will guard us for us. So Bilal said: I. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then you will sleep. He said: So they slept until the sun rose, then some people woke up, among them so-and-so and so-and-so, among them Umar. He said: So we said: Speak up, meaning speak. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke and said: Do as you used to do. He said: So we did. He said: And he said: So do likewise for whoever sleeps or forgets. He said: And the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, strayed, so I sought it and found its rope caught on a tree, and I brought it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he rode rejoicing. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when revelation came down upon him, that weighed upon him, and we recognized that in him, so he withdrew apart behind us. He said: So he began covering his head with his garment, and that weighed upon him, until we knew that revelation had been sent down to him, then he came to us and told us that there had been revealed to him: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory."
"4422","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hammad, he said: I heard Abu Wail say: Abdullah said: We used to say in the greeting: Peace upon Allah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say: Peace upon Allah, for Allah is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"4423","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which sin is greatest. He said: That you set up a rival to Allah though He created you, and that you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor, and that you kill your child lest he eat with you or eat your food."
"4424","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him. And a woman should not touch a woman and describe her to her husband as if he were looking at her."
"4425","Muhammad ibn Jafar said, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one phrase and I say another: Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to the Fire. He said: And Abdullah said: And I say: Whoever dies while not setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to Paradise."
"4426","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrate from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that he said: Let none of you assign a share to Satan, thinking it a duty upon him to leave to his right. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, most of his leaving was to his left."
"4427","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr, or Ibrahim, Shubah doubted, narrate from Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina two rakas, and with Abu Bakr and Umar, so would that my share of four rakas were two accepted rakas."
"4428","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Harith al-Awar, from Abdullah, that he said: The eater of usury and its giver, and its two witnesses, and its scribe when they know, and the tattooing woman and the woman tattooed and the woman seeking tattooing for beauty, and the withholder of charity, and the apostate Bedouin after migration, are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the Day of Resurrection."
"4429","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Murrah narrate from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: life for life, and the married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion, separating from, or splitting, the community."
"4430","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that he said: He is not of us who strikes the cheeks and tears the openings of garments, or calls with the call of ignorance. Sulayman said: And I think he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4431","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he prayed Zuhr five, so it was said to him: Has the prayer been increased. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And what is that. So they said: You prayed five. So he prostrated two prostrations after he had greeted. Shubah said: And I heard Sulayman and Hammad narrate that Ibrahim did not know whether he prayed three or five."
"4432","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: As if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheek of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for his left greeting."
"4433","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to prefer the congregational prayer over the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five folds, all of them like his prayer."
"4434","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Allah cursed the women seeking tattooing and the women plucking eyebrows and the women making gaps between teeth. Shubah said: And I think he said: The women changing the creation of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it."
"4435","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and I was with him, so he said to me: Seek for me three stones. He said: So I found for him two stones and dung. He said: So I brought them to him, and he took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: This is filth."
"4436","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him."
"4437","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drew a line with his hand, then he said: This is the path of Allah, straight. He said: Then he drew lines to its right and its left, then he said: These are the paths, and there is none of them but upon it is a devil calling to it. Then he recited: And this is My path, straight, so follow it and do not follow the paths."
"4438","Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: A Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was narrating to his companions, so Quraysh said: O Jew, this one claims that he is a prophet. So he said: I shall surely ask him about something none knows but a prophet. He said: So he came until he sat, then he said: O Muhammad, from what is man created. He said: O Jew, from both he is created, from the fluid of the man and from the fluid of the woman. As for the fluid of the man, it is a thick fluid, from it are bone and sinew, and as for the fluid of the woman, it is a thin fluid, from it are flesh and blood. So the Jew stood and said: So used to say those before you."
"4439","Ubaydah, meaning Ibn Humayd, narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah used to remind every Thursday, or the days twice. He said: So we said, or it was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we love your talk and desire it, and we wish you would remind us every day. So Abdullah said: Nothing prevents me from that but that I dislike to bore you, and I visit you with admonition as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit us."
"4440","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks for something while he is independent of it, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches on his face. And charity is not lawful for one who has fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold."
"4441","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment with my husband, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with my father Abu Sufyan, and with my brother Muawiyah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have asked Allah for fixed terms and apportioned provisions and fulfilled traces. Nothing of it is hastened before its time, and nothing of it is delayed after its time. Had you asked Allah to save you from torment in the Fire and torment in the grave, it would have been better for you. He said: So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, are apes and pigs of what was transformed. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, never transformed a people, or destroyed a people, and then made for them offspring or progeny. And apes and pigs existed before that."
"4442","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father from here, and he acknowledged it, and he said: Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafii narrated to me, Said ibn Salim, meaning al-Qaddah, told us, Ibn Jurayj told us that Ismail ibn Umayyah told him, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, that he said: I was present with Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, and two men came to him trading a merchandise, so this one said: I took it for such and such, and this one said: I sold it for such and such. So Abu Ubaydah said: Abdullah ibn Masud was brought the like of this, so he said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the like of this was brought to him, so he ordered the seller to be made to swear, then the buyer is given the choice: if he wishes he takes, and if he wishes he leaves."
"4443","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father, he said: I was told from Hisham ibn Yusuf about the two sellers in the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Ubayd. And my father said: Hajjaj al-Awar said: Abd al-Malik ibn Ubaydah. He said: And Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Masud, and there is not in it: from his father."
"4444","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Awn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Ibn Masud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the two sellers differ, the word is what the seller said, and the buyer has the choice."
"4445","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Waki narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from al-Qasim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the two sellers differ and there is no proof between them, the word is what the owner of the merchandise says, or they rescind."
"4446","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Man, from al-Qasim, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the two sellers differ while the merchandise is as it is, the word is what the seller said, or they rescind."
"4447","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Umar ibn Sad Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Man, from al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah and al-Ashath differed, so this one said: for ten, and this one said: for twenty. He said: Make between me and you a man. He said: You are between me and myself. He said: I judge with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged: When the two sellers differ and there is no proof, the word is the word of the seller, or they rescind the sale."
